E["item:barrow-key"] = {t="item",n="Barrow Key",z="stonetalon",s="Deep beneath Stonetalon Peak, the Barrow Key lies locked in the Talon Den. It is one of three druidic keys guarding the ancient treasures sealed within the den's hoard.",h="Deep beneath Stonetalon Peak, the Barrow Key lies locked in the Talon Den.",sec={{t="A Guardian's Safeguard",b="Night elf druids placed wards throughout the Talon Den's underground barrows to protect their relics from intruders. The Barrow Key is hidden in a cache among the passages, one part of that layered defense. The cache opens only with the Gatekeeper's Key, so a seeker must know the druids' defenses to reach it.",sp=0},{t="Unlocking the Hoard",b="The Barrow Key, the Claw Key, and the Sleepers' Key fit three carved keyholes in a stone altar deep in the Talon Den. Turn all three together, and the protective enchantments fade. The druidic relics in the hidden hoard are then within reach.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Barrow Key used for?",a="The Barrow Key works with the Claw Key and the Sleepers' Key to open the Talon Den Hoard, a stone chest of protected druidic relics deep within Stonetalon Peak.",al={"barrow key purpose","what does barrow key open","use of barrow key"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the Barrow Key hidden?",a="The Barrow Key is locked inside a barrow cache deep in the Talon Den's winding tunnels on Stonetalon Peak. The cache resembles a concealed wall torch.",al={"barrow key location","where is barrow key","find barrow key"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do you open the cache containing the Barrow Key?",a="You need the Gatekeeper's Key to open the cache. The druids hid it in a small lantern near the Talon Den's main entrance.",al={"open barrow cache","unlock barrow key","gatekeeper key barrow"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who hidden the Barrow Key in the Talon Den?",a="Night elf druids living in Stonetalon Peak devised the den's elaborate defenses to keep their powerful artifacts from hostile hands. They concealed the keys in different parts of the den.",al={"who made barrow key","who hid the keys in talon den"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Barrow Key?",a="The Barrow Key is one of three enchanted keys fashioned by the night elf druids within the Talon Den atop Stonetalon Peak. It serves as part of an intricate security ward designed to protect their most prized and powerful relics from falling into enemy hands.",al={"what is barrow key","barrow key info","talon den barrow key"},it="identity",add="6b9fc30c"},{q="Why does anyone want the Barrow Key?",a="Horde forces in the Stonetalon Mountains seek the Barrow Key alongside its sister keys, the Claw Key and the Sleepers' Key. Together, the three keys break the druidic wards sealing the Talon Den Hoard, unlocking the cache of powerful items preserved deep inside the barrow.",al={"why find barrow key","why want barrow key","who wants the barrow key"},it="why_wanted",add="17616df0"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the Barrow Key belongs to an ancient security rite. The druids of the Talon Den designed it to protect sacred belongings in their underground sanctuary.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde operatives in Stonetalon Mountains pry information from captured night elves to find the Barrow Key and plunder the druids' private hoard."},kw={"barrow key","claw key","gatekeeper's key","sleepers' key","stonetalon peak","talon den","talon den hoard","the den"},rel={"quest:1089","item:claw-key","item:sleepers-key","subzone:stonetalon-peak","zone:stonetalon","topic:druid","quest:1088","quest:1087"},src={"Barrow Key","The Den (quest)"}}
E["item:besseleth-s-fang"] = {t="item",n="Besseleth's Fang",z="stonetalon",s="In Sishir Canyon, Besseleth's Fang marks the end of a deadly spider's threat.",h="In Sishir Canyon, Besseleth's Fang marks the end of a deadly spider's threat.",sec={{t="Trophy of the Canyon Stalker",b="Besseleth and her brood make Sishir Canyon dangerous for travelers. At night, the giant spider turns the Webwinder Path into a death trap for those crossing the gorge. Her fang measures nearly two feet and drips with potent venom. Local defenders have suffered her venomous strikes, and presenting the fang brings them relief.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Besseleth's Fang used for?",a="The fang proves that Besseleth, the spider matriarch, has been slain. Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat placed a bounty on her after surviving a near-fatal attack by her fangs, and rewards anyone who brings him the trophy.",al={"besseleth fang purpose","who wants besseleth's fang","fang turn in"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where does this fang come from?",a="The fang comes from Besseleth, a giant predatory spider dwelling inside Sishir Canyon. The canyon lies west of the main road south of Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"how to get besseleth fang","where is besseleth","besseleth location"},it="origin"},{q="Why did Maggran Earthbinder want Besseleth dead?",a="Besseleth and her brood prey on travelers heading along the roads toward Sun Rock Retreat, especially at night. After Besseleth ambushed and wounded him with her fangs, Maggran Earthbinder issued a bounty to secure the trails.",al={"why kill besseleth","maggran bounty spider","why bounty on besseleth"},it="motive"},{q="Who posted the bounty for the fang?",a="Maggran Earthbinder authorized the bounty. A wanted sign warning travelers of Sishir Canyon's hazards stands along the main roadway south of the Windshear Crag fork.",al={"wanted poster stonetalon spider","arachnophobia quest giver"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Besseleth's Fang?",a="Besseleth's Fang is a massive, two-foot tooth taken from the predatory spider Besseleth. She and her brood stalk Sishir Canyon and prey upon travelers along the Webwinder Path at night. The fang serves as undeniable physical proof that the feared arachnid terrorizing the trails of Stonetalon has finally been slain.",al={"what is besseleths fang","besseleth tooth","fang of besseleth"},it="identity",add="f0d9a9a7"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the canyon spider helps safeguard the precarious mountain trails connecting the Barrens border with Sun Rock Retreat.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can claim the venomous tooth of an apex arachnid matriarch, nearly two feet long, as proof of your tracking and combat prowess."},kw={"arachnophobia","besseleth","besseleth's fang","maggran earthbinder","sishir canyon","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","webwinder path"},rel={"quest:6284","npc:maggran-earthbinder","subzone:sishir-canyon","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:webwinder-path","zone:stonetalon","subzone:windshear-crag"},src={"Besseleth's Fang","Arachnophobia (quest)"}}
E["item:bloodfury-ripper-s-remains"] = {t="item",n="Bloodfury Ripper's Remains",z="stonetalon",s="At Sun Rock Retreat, Maggran Earthbinder seeks Bloodfury Ripper's Remains as proof that the Bloodfury harpy leader is dead. Her death strikes at the threat to the tauren settlement.",h="At Sun Rock Retreat, Maggran Earthbinder seeks Bloodfury Ripper's Remains as proof that the Bloodfury harpy...",sec={{t="Severing the Bloodline",b="Bloodfury Ripper leads the harpies of the Charred Vale with fierce, territorial aggression. They nest among the scorched ruins and threaten travelers and shamans across the Stonetalon Mountains. Culling the flock eases the danger for a time, but Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat knows that lasting relief means removing its leader. Bloodfury Ripper rules almost like a queen, directing the harpies' attacks on their territory. Her remains prove she is dead, leaving the flock in disarray and giving the tauren who seek to heal and secure their rugged lands greater peace of mind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Bloodfury Ripper's Remains used for?",a="Bloodfury Ripper's Remains prove that the harpy leader is dead. Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat seeks them to confirm that the queen-like matriarch has been removed.",al={"what do remains do","remains purpose","who wants the remains"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where can Bloodfury Ripper be found?",a="Bloodfury Ripper prowls the western and northwestern hill lines of the Charred Vale in southern Stonetalon Mountains. Her blue plumage sets her apart from her crimson-and-white flock.",al={"bloodfury ripper location","where is ripper","find bloodfury ripper"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Maggran Earthbinder want her dead?",a="Maggran Earthbinder believes that culling ordinary harpies cannot stop their raids on the surrounding lands. He seeks Bloodfury Ripper's death to break their hierarchy and weaken their ability to rally against Sun Rock Retreat.",al={"why kill bloodfury ripper","maggran motivation","why ripper dead"},it="motive"},{q="What are Bloodfury Ripper's Remains?",a="These gruesome remains are the physical proof taken from the body of Bloodfury Ripper, the matriarch and leader of the Bloodfury harpies infesting the Charred Vale. She acts almost as a queen to her flock, guiding their aggressive spread across Stonetalon. Her slain body serves as undeniable evidence that her reign over the vale's harpies has been brought to a bloody end.",al={"what are bloodfury ripper's remains","bloodfury ripper remains what is this","who is bloodfury ripper"},it="identity",add="ff70f27b"},{q="Where do Bloodfury Ripper's Remains come from?",a="These remains are carved from Bloodfury Ripper herself after slaying her among the western hills of the Charred Vale. Unlike her red and white kin, this distinctive blue-feathered harpy leads the Bloodfury brood from the vale's desolate cliffs, making her a prized target for anyone seeking to break the flock's command.",al={"where do bloodfury rippers remains come from","who drops bloodfury rippers remains","bloodfury rippers remains origin"},it="origin",add="ba88af47"},{q="Why does Maggran Earthbinder want Bloodfury Ripper's Remains?",a="Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat demands these remains as proof that the Bloodfury harpies' matriarch is truly dead. Simply culling their numbers was never going to suffice; Maggran believes striking down their queen will leave the surviving harpies helpless and cause their numbers to wither away, freeing him from the bitter anger that consumed his thoughts.",al={"why does maggran want bloodfury rippers remains","why are bloodfury rippers remains wanted","who wants bloodfury ripper's remains"},it="why_wanted",add="81140692"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Bloodfury harpies threaten Sun Rock Retreat directly. Gathering their leader's remains helps protect peaceful tauren settlements in Stonetalon.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing wild dangers such as the Bloodfury matriarch helps keep routes safe for Horde caravans and scouts traveling between the Barrens and Stonetalon."},kw={"bloodfury ripper","charred vale","harpies","maggran earthbinder","remains","stonetalon","sun rock retreat"},rel={"quest:6283","quest:6282","npc:maggran-earthbinder","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","topic:tauren"},src={"Bloodfury Ripper's Remains","Bloodfury Bloodline"}}
E["item:claw-key"] = {t="item",n="Claw Key",z="stonetalon",s="Within the Talon Den atop Stonetalon Peak, three druidic keys open the enchanted hoard.",h="Within the Talon Den atop Stonetalon Peak, three druidic keys open the enchanted hoard.",sec={{t="Wards of the Talon Den",b="High on Stonetalon Peak, night elf druids built the Talon Den as a sanctuary and a storehouse for powerful relics. They hid the treasures behind several layers of protection. Three enchanted locks seal the hoard: the Barrow Key, the Sleepers' Key, and the Claw Key. Each key lies in its own druidic cache, shaped like a torch and hidden in the winding tunnels of the barrow den.",sp=0},{t="Breaching the Caches",b="The druids kept the keys guarded and out of easy reach. Near the barrow entrance lies the Gatekeeper's Key, needed to open the cache that holds the Claw Key. The Claw Key is vital to breaking the druids' seal and claiming the riches hidden deep within the mountain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Claw Key used for?",a="The Claw Key is one of three keys needed to unlock the Talon Den Hoard, a warded stone chest in the heart of the Talon Den on Stonetalon Peak.",al={"claw key purpose","what does claw key open","talon den hoard key"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where can the Claw Key be found?",a="The Claw Key lies in a druid cache disguised as a torch in the Talon Den tunnels on Stonetalon Peak. Opening the cache requires the Gatekeeper's Key from the den entrance.",al={"claw key location","where is claw key","find claw key"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What other keys are needed alongside the Claw Key?",a="The Talon Den Hoard requires the Claw Key, the Barrow Key, and the Sleepers' Key, each kept in a separate cache throughout the den.",al={"other keys","talon den keys","keys for the den"},gp=true},{q="Why did the druids hide these keys?",a="Night elf druids built the Talon Den to keep powerful relics away from prying eyes. They used keys and concealed caches to deter intruders.",al={"why are keys hidden","talon den lore"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Claw Key?",a="The Claw Key is one of three enchanted keys crafted by the night elf druids of Stonetalon Peak. Locked away within a concealed cache inside the subterranean Talon Den, it forms an integral part of an intricate security ward designed to protect their most valued treasures from intrusion.",al={"what is claw key","claw key info","what kind of key is claw key"},it="identity",add="31018164"},{q="Where does the Claw Key come from, and who made it?",a="The key was fashioned by the druids who established the Talon Den high upon Stonetalon Peak. To safeguard their relics, they created this key alongside the Barrow and Sleepers' keys, locking it inside a ward cache that requires the Gatekeeper's Key to open.",al={"who made claw key","claw key origin","where did claw key come from"},it="origin",add="e0ebbe01"},{q="Why does anyone want the Claw Key?",a="The Claw Key is sought because it is required to breach the Talon Den Hoard. The druids locked away many powerful artifacts inside the cavern's depths behind three specialized keyholes, ensuring that only someone who gathers all three keys can claim the hoard's concealed relics.",al={"why find claw key","why get claw key","claw key purpose lore"},it="why_wanted",add="9663afaa"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="By interrogating captured night elves, the Horde can bypass the druids' ancient defenses and pillage the sacred artifacts stored atop Stonetalon Peak.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you bear a key named for the iconic Druids of the Claw. It reflects the sacred traditions and protective wards crafted by night elf barrow dwellers."},kw={"barrow den","claw key","druids' cache","gatekeeper's key","stonetalon peak","talon den","talon den hoard","the den"},rel={"quest:1089","item:barrow-key","item:sleepers-key","subzone:stonetalon-peak","zone:stonetalon","quest:1088","quest:1087","topic:druid"},src={"Claw Key","The Den (quest)"}}
E["item:corroded-shrapnel"] = {t="item",n="Corroded Shrapnel",z="stonetalon",s="In Stonetalon, jagged metal remains lodged deep inside corrupted treants. The Venture Company’s retreating munitions left fragments in the forest’s protectors, now sought for study.",h="In Stonetalon, jagged metal remains lodged deep inside corrupted treants.",sec={{t="Remnants of Industrial Ruin",b="When the Venture Company was driven from Stonetalon’s groves, its goblins used reckless munitions to cover their escape. Explosive shrapnel tore into the valley’s defending treants, lodging deep within their bark and core. The ancient guardians slowly succumbed to corruption. Their wood blackened, and their fury turned against anyone entering the vale. Kaela Shadowspear seeks the rusted fragments so Gaxim Rustfizzle, a gnome, can study how the weapons brought on the treants’ corruption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this shrapnel come from?",a="The shrapnel comes from corrupted treants in the Stonetalon Mountains, including Charred Ancients, Blackened Ancients, and Vengeful Ancients.",al={"where do i find shrapnel","corroded shrapnel drop","who drops shrapnel"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the shrapnel embedded in the treants?",a="The Venture Company’s explosive munitions struck the treants as the forest guardians drove goblin loggers from the vale. Shards lodged in their bark during the battle and remained there.",al={"how did shrapnel get in treants","why are treants full of metal"}},{q="Is the shrapnel responsible for corrupting the forest ancients?",a="Kaela Shadowspear says the gnome Gaxim believes the treants’ corruption is tied to the foul chemical or metallic makeup of the retreating goblins’ weapons.",al={"did shrapnel corrupt treants","why are treants mad"}},{q="Who wants to inspect the shrapnel?",a="Kaela Shadowspear, a night elf, wants a sample to pass to Gaxim, a gnome inventor who plans to study its properties and learn what afflicts the treants.",al={"who needs the shrapnel","shrapnel turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Corroded Shrapnel?",a="Corroded Shrapnel consists of jagged metal fragments left behind from goblin weaponry. Embedded deep inside the scarred bark of Stonetalon's treants, these degraded, rusted bits of explosive munitions are thought to carry a lingering poison or foul taint that afflicts the forest's protectors.",al={"what is corroded shrapnel","corroded shrapnel lore","corroded shrapnel item"},it="identity",add="1f081bfa"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, seeing Kalimdor’s ancients warped by goblin munitions and festering metal shards shows the cost unchecked exploitation brings to the wild.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see Gaxim’s study of tainted shrapnel as a practical, scientific way to investigate an ecological mystery that woodland sentinels cannot explain."},kw={"charred ancient","corroded shrapnel","gaxim","kaela shadowspear","stonetalon","treant","venture co"},rel={"quest:1084","npc:kaela-shadowspear","zone:stonetalon","quest:764","topic:goblin","topic:gnome"},src={"Corroded Shrapnel","Wounded Ancients"}}
E["item:courser-eye"] = {t="item",n="Courser Eye",z="stonetalon",s="Coursers roam the highlands of Stonetalon, where Courser Eye is gathered for a troll witch doctor's brew. Witch Doctor Jin'Zil in Malaka'jin wants many eyes for a concoction he calls forest magic.",h="Coursers roam the highlands of Stonetalon, where Courser Eye is gathered for a troll witch doctor's brew.",sec={{t="A Troll's Concoction",b="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil mixes tribal brews at Malaka'jin to fight the night elves contesting the region. Stag eyes are common in voodoo and folk alchemy, yet Jin'Zil demands thirty courser eyes at once, far more than ordinary spellcraft needs. He mixes them with fey dragon scales, sap, and feline whiskers. The brew is meant for the night elf prisoners held in cages at the back of his den.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are courser eyes found?",a="Courser eyes come from Antlered Coursers and Great Coursers in the higher reaches of Stonetalon Mountains, especially near Mirkfallon Lake and Stonetalon Peak.",al={"courser eye locations","where to get courser eye","how to get courser eye"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Witch Doctor Jin'Zil need so many eyes?",a="Jin'Zil says a proper brew can never have too many eyes. He mixes them with parts from local animals for the concoction he calls forest magic.",al={"why 30 eyes","why does jinzil need eyes","what does jinzil do with courser eyes"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens when Jin'Zil completes his forest magic potion?",a="Jin'Zil plans to use his forest magic brew on the night elf prisoners caged in his cave. What becomes of them is revealed when he carries out the experiment.",al={"jinzil forest magic result","what happens to the prisoners in malakajin"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="What is a Courser Eye?",a="A Courser Eye is an alchemical reagent harvested from the native stag-like coursers roaming the Stonetalon Mountains. To most woodland inhabitants, they are merely part of the local wildlife, but in the hands of a cunning practitioner, these numerous eyes serve as a raw ingredient for potent concoctions.",al={"what is courser eye","courser eye item","what are courser eyes"},it="identity",add="5cdf5ac9"},{q="Where does a Courser Eye come from?",a="These eyes are gathered directly from the antlered coursers and great coursers that graze across the Stonetalon Mountains, particularly around Mirkfallon Lake and near Stonetalon Peak. They are natural parts taken from the mountain's wild beasts rather than crafted or enchanted artifacts.",al={"where do courser eyes come from","who made courser eye","courser eye origin"},it="origin",add="a4aa468a"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you know Jin'Zil's crude use of animal parts reflects a darker, practical side of troll alchemy and mojo craft against the Horde's enemies.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may see the coursers killed to fuel a witch doctor's cruel experiments on captured night elves as an affront to your reverence for nature."},kw={"antlered courser","courser eye","forest magic","great courser","jin'zil","malaka'jin","stonetalon"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-jin-zil","quest:1058","item:fey-dragon-scale","item:stonetalon-sap","item:twilight-whisker","subzone:malaka-jin","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Courser Eye","Jin'Zil's Forest Magic"}}
E["item:covert-ops-pack"] = {t="item",n="Covert Ops Pack",z="stonetalon",s="In Stonetalon, the Covert Ops Pack equips Alliance agents to sabotage Venture Company sites and steal their plans. Its charges and schematics target the company’s work in Windshear Crag.",h="In Stonetalon, the Covert Ops Pack equips Alliance agents to sabotage Venture Company sites and steal their...",sec={{t="Sabotage by Design",b="The Covert Ops Pack carries charges and plans for strikes inside Venture Company territory. Red and blue NG-5 explosives pair with remote detonators, while Plan Alpha and Plan Beta give agents instructions. The explosives target the Cragpool Lake lumber mill and the eastern mine. As goblins rush to fight fires and inspect broken machinery, an infiltrator can slip through the confusion and take documents and schematics.",sp=0},{t="A Confluence of Interests",b="The pack serves both the night elf Sentinels and Alliance engineers in Stonetalon. Its blasts and theft hinder the clear-cutting and excavation of the sacred mountainside. The stolen Venture Company engineering plans also offer insight into goblin heavy machinery. They show where the machines can fail and give Alliance engineers ideas to adapt for their own designs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Covert Ops Pack?",a="The Covert Ops Pack holds red and blue NG-5 explosives with matching remote detonators, along with written instructions for Plan Alpha and Plan Beta.",al={"covert ops pack contents","what does the pack contain","items in covert ops pack"},it="item"},{q="What is the tactical purpose of the explosives?",a="The explosives make loud distractions at Venture Company work sites. With security drawn away, an operative can enter the lumber mill and mine unseen.",al={"why use bombs","what are ng-5 explosives for","alpha beta demolition"},it="purpose"},{q="What intelligence does this operation target?",a="The operation seeks Venture Company engineering plans from the lumber mill south of Cragpool Lake, then executive letters kept in Windshear Mine at the crag’s eastern end.",al={"what do we steal","pack mission objective","covert ops goals"},it="target"},{q="Who benefits from the materials recovered using this pack?",a="The night elf Sentinels and Alliance engineers both benefit. The sabotage hinders deforestation, while engineers study the schematics to find weaknesses in Venture Company shredders and adapt ideas for their own technology.",al={"who wants the venture plans","who is the pack for","sentinels covert ops"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Covert Ops Pack?",a="The Covert Ops Pack is a specialized sabotage kit prepared for infiltration operations in Windshear Crag. It contains color-coded NG-5 explosives, matching remote detonators, and detailed mission plans designed to stage timed distractions while crucial Venture Company documents are retrieved under their noses.",al={"what is covert ops pack","covert ops pack info","covert ops kit"},it="identity",add="8d787d42"},{q="Where does the Covert Ops Pack come from, and who made it?",a="The pack is assembled by an Alliance tinkerer assisting the night elf Sentinels in Stonetalon Mountains. Combining precision engineering with tactical demolition, they crafted the volatile NG-5 charges and remote triggers specifically to aid operative strikes against Venture Company installations.",al={"who made covert ops pack","where did covert ops pack come from","covert ops pack creator"},it="origin",add="23fc442d"},{q="Why is the Covert Ops Pack needed?",a="Directly assaulting fortified Venture Company sites like their lumber mill and mine would be suicidal or alert guards before vital intelligence can be seized. The pack provides the tools to plant remote explosives and trigger controlled chaos elsewhere, drawing defenders away so you can slip inside and recover their engineering plans and correspondence.",al={"why do i need covert ops pack","why covert ops pack","covert ops pack purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="ca775219"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="For an engineer, the pack turns gnomish ingenuity against goblin industry. Its customized NG-5 charges help uncover the workings of Venture Company machinery.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you support the Sentinels’ struggle against commercial despoilment in the Stonetalon Mountains."},kw={"covert ops pack","cragpool lake","ng-5 explosives","plan alpha","plan beta","venture co","windshear crag"},rel={"quest:1079","quest:1080","item:ng-5","item:venture-co-engineering-plans","item:venture-co-letters","subzone:windshear-crag","topic:sentinels","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Covert Ops Pack","Covert Ops - Alpha","Covert Ops - Beta"}}
E["item:crystalized-scales"] = {t="item",n="Crystalized Scales",z="stonetalon",s="Basilisks in harsh Kalimdor lands yield Crystalized Scales for arcane work. The mineralized hides come from the Charred Vale and Thousand Needles, and Collin Mauren seeks them in Stormwind.",h="Basilisks in harsh Kalimdor lands yield Crystalized Scales for arcane work.",sec={{t="A Rare Kalimdor Reagent",b="Basilisks endure heat and ash in Stonetalon's Charred Vale and the salt flats of Thousand Needles. Their hides harden beneath a crystal crust, and the scales hold latent arcane resonance. Wizards across the Great Sea prize them for experiments in rare spellcraft.",sp=0},{t="Mauren's Arcane Work",b="In Stormwind, the mage Collin Mauren seeks travelers bound for Kalimdor to bring him these scales. Mauren pulverizes their crystalline mineral layers into dust, then uses the powder as a reagent for newly conceived spells and his own arcane research.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures yield crystalized scales?",a="Basilisks adapted to harsh regions yield Crystalized Scales, including the scorched, singed, and blackened basilisks of Stonetalon's Charred Vale and the saltstone basilisks of Thousand Needles.",al={"where do scales drop","who drops crystalized scales","basilisk scales source"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who is seeking these scales in Stormwind?",a="Collin Mauren, a wizard in Stormwind City, seeks the scales from travelers heading into Stonetalon for his magical experiments.",al={"who wants crystalized scales","collin mauren scales","who uses these scales"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How are the scales used in spellcasting?",a="Mauren pulverizes the crystalline scales into fine dust, which provides a potent reagent for specialized spells of his own creation.",al={"why are crystalized scales magic","scale spell reagent"},it="purpose"},{q="Can crystalized scales only be found in Stonetalon?",a="Mauren asks travelers bound for the Charred Vale in Stonetalon to seek the scales, and saltstone basilisks in Thousand Needles bear similar crystalline hides.",al={"thousand needles scales","other places to get scales"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are crystalized scales?",a="Crystalized scales are hardened, crystalline outer plates harvested from certain species of basilisks. Notably found on basilisks dwelling in harsh regions like the Charred Vale within the Stonetalon Mountains, these tough scales possess unique mineral-like properties that make them valuable to scholars and spellcasters.",al={"what are crystalized scales","crystalized scales lore","about crystalized scales"},it="identity",add="cec6ea6a"},{q="Where do crystalized scales come from?",a="These scales naturally grow on specific varieties of basilisks. They are commonly harvested from the scorched, blackened, and singed basilisks roaming the fiery wastes of Stonetalon's Charred Vale, as well as saltstone basilisks found in the salt flats of Thousand Needles.",al={"crystalized scales origin","where to get crystalized scales","source of crystalized scales"},it="origin",add="5be8a367"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how harsh surroundings alter a beast's magical nature and yield reagents for unusual spells.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you carry these scales between Stormwind and the wilds of Kalimdor."},kw={"basilisk","charred vale","collin mauren","crystalized scales","reagent","stonetalon mountains","stormwind","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:collin-mauren","quest:1078","subzone:charred-vale","zone:stonetalon","zone:thousandneedles","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Crystalized Scales","Retrieval for Mauren"}}
E["item:enchanted-gaea-seeds"] = {t="item",n="Enchanted Gaea Seeds",z="stonetalon",s="At Sun Rock Retreat, Enchanted Gaea Seeds are prepared for the Charred Vale. Druidic magic gives them strength to take root in ash-choked soil and begin restoring Kalimdor's ravaged land.",h="At Sun Rock Retreat, Enchanted Gaea Seeds are prepared for the Charred Vale.",sec={{t="A Spark in the Ashes",b="The Horde's druids are trying to heal the deep scars across Stonetalon Mountains. At Sun Rock Retreat, Tammra Windfield enchants raw Gaea Seeds so they can withstand corruption and elemental blight. Planted in the fertile dirt mounds beneath the Charred Vale's soot, they take root despite the harsh land. Hostile fire elementals and invasive harpies still dominate the vale.",sp=0},{t="The Promise of Renewal",b="Planting the seeds is part of the struggle for Stonetalon's future. Their enchanted husks resist lingering corruption and give native plants a foothold. The returning vegetation is meant to soothe agitated fire elementals, crowd out feral harpies, and counter the deforestation caused by the Venture Company's relentless logging.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Enchanted Gaea Seeds used for?",a="Plant the seeds in fertile dirt mounds in the Charred Vale. They are meant to grow resilient plants that resist corruption and begin healing land scarred by fire and warfare.",al={"gaea seeds purpose","what do enchanted gaea seeds do","why plant gaea seeds"},it="purpose"},{q="Who created or enchanted these seeds?",a="Raw Gaea Seeds are gathered in the surrounding wilderness and brought to Tammra Windfield at Sun Rock Retreat. She enchants them to help them survive the Charred Vale's hostile, ash-laden soil.",al={"who made the seeds","tammra windwhisper seeds","how are gaea seeds made"},it="origin"},{q="Why must they be planted in the Charred Vale?",a="The Charred Vale is the center of ecological destruction in the Stonetalon Mountains, overrun by angry fire elementals and harpies. Planting the seeds in its surviving soil mounds brings new life meant to soothe the region's turmoil.",al={"where do i plant them","why charred vale","charred vale planting"},it="place"},{q="What threats face the planted seeds?",a="Hostile fire elementals born of the blaze and aggressive Bloodfury harpies nesting in the ruins threaten the planted seeds. The Venture Company's nearby operations bring further industrial destruction.",al={"dangers in charred vale","what is destroying the land"},it="threat"},{q="What are Enchanted Gaea Seeds?",a="Enchanted Gaea Seeds are resilient, magically treated seeds prepared by Tammra Windfield at Sun Rock Retreat. Designed to withstand environmental blight, they serve as a powerful catalyst for rebirth, capable of taking root in devastated earth and initiating the long process of healing scorched terrain.",al={"what are enchanted gaea seeds","enchanted gaea seed lore","what is enchanted gaea seeds"},it="identity",add="2eba8b82"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you help nurture the cycle of rebirth, coaxing resilient life back into a land consumed by ruin and wildfire.",["race:Tauren"]="As one of the Shu'halo of Sun Rock Retreat, you plant the enchanted seeds as spiritual stewardship, honoring the Earth Mother and reclaiming wounded land."},kw={"charred vale","enchanted gaea seeds","gaea seed","rebirth","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","tammra windwhisper"},rel={"quest:6381","quest:6301","item:gaea-seed","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","quest:6282","quest:764"},src={"Enchanted Gaea Seeds","New Life"}}
E["item:enchanted-resonite-crystal"] = {t="item",n="Enchanted Resonite Crystal",z="stonetalon",s="In Stonetalon, Mor'rogal has altered resonite crystals with shamanic magic. The Enchanted Resonite Crystal is made to break the cask holding Goggeroc.",h="In Stonetalon, Mor'rogal has altered resonite crystals with shamanic magic.",sec={{t="Breaker of Ancient Stone",b="Deep in the caverns of the Stonetalon Mountains, raw resonite crystals carry unusual harmonic and earthen properties. Shaman Mor'rogal sensed danger sleeping inside a sealed underground cask and altered the minerals with his elemental powers. The Enchanted Resonite Crystal can break the reinforced Resonite cask and rouse Goggeroc, a giant Earthen, while he is still dazed from his long sleep.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Goggeroc",b="Mor'rogal believed an unchecked ancient Earthen could bring catastrophe to Stonetalon and greater Kalimdor. By using the enchanted crystal to break the cask, he means to wake Goggeroc while he is weakened. That leaves a brief chance to destroy him before his full elemental might returns.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Enchanted Resonite Crystal used for?",a="The crystal breaks the Resonite cask deep in the kobold-infested caves of the Stonetalon Mountains and releases Goggeroc, a slumbering Earthen.",al={"enchanted resonite crystal use","what does crystal do","break resonite cask"},sp=1,it="purpose",bt={"q6421.2"}},{q="Who created this enchanted crystal?",a="Shaman Mor'rogal created the crystal by infusing raw resonite with his shamanic powers to weaken and expose the sleeping creature inside the cask.",al={"who made crystal","mor'rogal crystal","enchanted resonite creator"},it="origin"},{q="Why must Goggeroc be awakened and destroyed?",a="Mor'rogal fears an ancient Earthen's unmatched might could endanger Stonetalon and Kalimdor. The crystal wakes Goggeroc while he is temporarily weakened, making him vulnerable.",al={"why kill goggeroc","is goggeroc dangerous","goggeroc threat"},it="threat"},{q="What should I do with the crystal after defeating Goggeroc?",a="Bring the Enchanted Resonite Crystal back to Mor'rogal and confirm that Goggeroc has been slain.",al={"return resonite crystal","turn in enchanted resonite crystal"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Enchanted Resonite Crystal?",a="It is an altered mineral talisman imbued with shamanistic power by Mor'rogal at Sun Rock Retreat. Resonite crystals are naturally occurring minerals found in the caves of Stonetalon Mountains. Once magically transformed, this crystal serves as a key and a hammer designed specifically to shatter the Resonite cask holding the slumbering earthen giant, Goggeroc.",al={"what is enchanted resonite crystal","enchanted resonite crystal lore","resonite crystal meaning"},it="identity",add="ed58de6b"},{q="Why does Mor'rogal want the Enchanted Resonite Crystal?",a="Mor'rogal needs the crystal to free and eliminate Goggeroc before the earthen awakens at full strength. He fears that an unleashed earthen poses an unmatched peril that could devastate all of Stonetalon Mountains. Shattering the cask forces Goggeroc awake in a severely weakened state, giving you the only viable chance to strike him down.",al={"why want enchanted resonite crystal","why does morrogal need crystal","why enchanted resonite crystal"},it="why_wanted",add="d1731b4b"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see how elemental power can weaken the magic binding living stone.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help Mor'rogal protect Stonetalon's fragile balance by stopping ancient threats before they endanger regional outposts."},kw={"earthen arise","enchanted resonite crystal","goggeroc","mor'rogal","resonite cask","resonite crystal","stonetalon mountains"},rel={"quest:6481","npc:mor-rogal","item:resonite-crystal","zone:stonetalon","zone:thunderbluff","topic:kobold"},src={"Enchanted Resonite Crystal","Earthen Arise"}}
E["item:fey-dragon-scale"] = {t="item",n="Fey Dragon Scale",z="stonetalon",s="Around Stonetalon Peak, faerie dragons yield scales coveted by Jin'Zil. The Darkspear witch doctor uses one as a reagent in a brew that mocks night elven nature magic.",h="Around Stonetalon Peak, faerie dragons yield scales coveted by Jin'Zil.",sec={{t="A Rare Forest Harvest",b="Around Stonetalon Peak, faerie dragons haunt the wild groves of Kalimdor. Their scales gleam with natural magic. Night elves revere them as harmless woodland spirits and allies, while outsiders prize the scales as rare magical ingredients.",sp=0},{t="A Mocking Concoction",b="At Malaka'jin, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil mixes a brew that mocks kaldorei traditions. He combines a fey dragon scale with tree sap, feline whiskers, and dozens upon dozens of courser eyes, calling the result 'forest magic.' He means the cruel concoction for the three night elves he keeps caged.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this scale come from?",a="The scale comes from faerie dragons in the highland groves around Stonetalon Peak, including Wily Fey Dragons and Nal'taszar.",al={"fey dragon scale drop","where to find fey dragon scale","who drops fey dragon scale"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Witch Doctor Jin'Zil want a fey dragon scale?",a="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil in Malaka'jin wants the scale with other woodland reagents for a brew he sneeringly calls 'forest magic,' meant for his caged night elf prisoners.",al={"why does jin'zil want this","what is the scale used for","jin'zil forest magic reagent"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens when Jin'Zil finishes his brew?",a="Jin'Zil plans to use the finished brew on his three captive night elves. When he carries out that plan, the fate of his prisoners is revealed.",al={"what does jin'zil do with the brew","jin'zil magic result","prisoners of jin'zil"},sp=1},{q="What is a Fey Dragon Scale?",a="A Fey Dragon Scale is a shimmering, iridescent scale harvested from the elusive faerie dragons of Stonetalon Peak. These mystical creatures are deeply tied to the natural energies of the wild. To an alchemist or witch doctor, the scale serves as a potent, magically attuned reagent steeped in the raw essence of the ancient forest.",al={"what is fey dragon scale","fey dragon scale lore","about fey dragon scales"},it="identity",add="9423a9c1"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know faerie dragons as treasured companions and forest guardians of the kaldorei. Seeing their scales taken for a troll witch doctor's deadly mockery is an outrage to nature.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help Jin'Zil secure the Horde's footing in the Stonetalon Mountains and strike at the night elven presence higher on the slopes."},kw={"faerie dragon","fey dragon scale","forest magic","jin'zil","malaka'jin","nal'taszar","stonetalon peak"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-jin-zil","quest:1058","subzone:stonetalon-peak","subzone:malaka-jin","item:stonetalon-sap","item:twilight-whisker","item:courser-eye","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Fey Dragon Scale","Jin'Zil's Forest Magic"}}
E["item:gaea-seed"] = {t="item",n="Gaea Seed",z="stonetalon",s="Along Mirkfallon Lake, Gaea Seeds offer a way to heal Stonetalon's wounded land. Tauren shamans value the hardy kernels for restoring places scarred by war and industry.",h="Along Mirkfallon Lake, Gaea Seeds offer a way to heal Stonetalon's wounded land.",sec={{t="Vessels of Renewal",b="Gaea Seeds wash ashore or grow along Mirkfallon Lake in the Stonetalon Mountains. Small and fibrous, they look like coconuts, yet endure harsh conditions. As conflict and industry scar the land, shamans see the seeds as a means to heal it.",sp=0},{t="Blessings of the Earthmother",b="At Sun Rock Retreat, the tauren shaman Tammra Windfield gathers Gaea Seeds to counter the destruction across the peaks. Shamans use traditional chants and elemental rites to bless the dormant husks with the Earthmother's power. That blessing hastens their growth, making them hardy saplings able to take root in scorched, barren ground such as the Charred Vale.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are Gaea Seeds found?",a="Gaea Seeds wash ashore along Mirkfallon Lake, in the mountains north of Sun Rock Retreat in Stonetalon.",al={"gaea seed location","where to find gaea seeds","how to get gaea seed"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are Gaea Seeds used for?",a="At Sun Rock Retreat, Tammra Windfield gathers Gaea Seeds for an elemental blessing. The blessed seeds help restore plant life in devastated places such as the Charred Vale.",al={"gaea seed purpose","why collect gaea seeds","what does tammra do with gaea seeds"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do shamans need to imbue the seeds?",a="Fire, warfare, and logging have badly damaged parts of Stonetalon. The Earthmother's power quickens the seeds' growth and strengthens them to take root in ruined soil.",al={"why bless the seeds","shaman gaea seed magic"},it="power"},{q="What do Gaea Seeds look like?",a="Gaea Seeds look like small, brown, rounded husks or coconuts along the water's edge of Mirkfallon Lake.",al={"gaea seed appearance","how to spot gaea seeds"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is a Gaea Seed?",a="A Gaea Seed is a hardy, coconut-like kernel of life native to the Stonetalon Mountains. Blessed with natural resilience, these seeds hold potent vegetative potential that tauren shamans draw upon through the blessings of the Earthmother to bring restorative growth to lands scarred by industrial greed and warfare.",al={"what are gaea seeds","gaea seed info","what is gaea seed"},it="identity",add="0f706426"},{q="Where does a Gaea Seed come from?",a="Gaea Seeds are natural botanical wonders found solely along the water's edge of Mirkfallon Lake, nestled high in the Stonetalon Mountains north of Sun Rock Retreat. They are not crafted by mortal hands, but rather are natural gifts of the Earthmother, flourishing naturally around the lake's shores.",al={"who made gaea seed","gaea seed origin","where do gaea seeds come from"},it="origin",add="e9a7441d"},{q="Why does Tammra Windfield want Gaea Seeds?",a="Tammra Windfield, a shaman at Sun Rock Retreat, seeks Gaea Seeds to heal the scarred Stonetalon wilderness. Continuous logging and fighting have devastated the region, particularly the scorched earth of the Charred Vale. By gathering these seeds, she can channel the Earthmother's blessing and shamanistic power into them, accelerating their growth to replenish the ruined land.",al={"why gather gaea seeds","who wants gaea seeds","why does anyone want gaea seed"},it="why_wanted",add="3509f4c5"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you see how elemental rites and the Earthmother's blessing can hasten growth and help heal damaged land.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you share the people of Sun Rock Retreat's sacred duty to heal land damaged by outside warfare and lumbering."},kw={"charred vale","cycle of rebirth","earthmother","gaea seed","mirkfallon lake","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","tammra windfield"},rel={"quest:6301","quest:6381","npc:tammra-windfield","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:charred-vale","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Gaea Seed","Cycle of Rebirth"}}
E["item:gerenzo-s-mechanical-arm"] = {t="item",n="Gerenzo's Mechanical Arm",z="stonetalon",s="In the Stonetalon Mountains, goblin operatives seek Gerenzo's Mechanical Arm as proof while clearing out competition. Taken from rogue engineer Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, the grafted limb marks his death.",h="In the Stonetalon Mountains, goblin operatives seek Gerenzo's Mechanical Arm as proof while clearing out...",sec={{t="A Bizarre Invention",b="Above Cragpool Lake, rogue engineer Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle grafted whirring gears and metal onto his failing body. The renegade gnome replaced his natural limbs with intricate machinery. Goblin tinker Ziz Fizziks seeks Gerenzo's elimination to impress his superiors, and this distinctive arm is the trophy he needs as indisputable proof of the engineer's death.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Philosophy, Goblin Critique",b="Ziz Fizziks sees little sense in amputating a working arm to attach a mechanical replacement. A proper goblin engineer, he says, would keep both biological arms and mount a mechanical third one instead. Despite that divide in engineering thought, delivering the severed limb satisfies Sputtervalve and helps Ziz petition for an assignment in Gadgetzan or Undermine.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does Gerenzo's Mechanical Arm come from?",a="The arm comes from Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, who oversees logging and engineering operations high above Cragpool Lake, near the water wheel in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who drops gerenzo arm","gerenzo arm location","where get gerenzo mechanical arm"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Ziz Fizziks want this arm?",a="Ziz Fizziks needs proof for his superior, Sputtervalve, that Gerenzo is dead. Gerenzo's unique prosthetic arm cannot be forged or mistaken for anyone else's.",al={"why ziz want arm","arm quest turn in","proof of gerenzo death"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why did Gerenzo replace his own arm?",a="Ziz Fizziks says Gerenzo's flesh appeared to be rotting away. Gerenzo grafted machinery onto himself and replaced his failing limbs with mechanical counterparts, driven by desperation or obsessive gnomish experimentation.",al={"why is gerenzo a cyborg","gerenzo rotting flesh","why mechanical arm"}},{q="What is Gerenzo's Mechanical Arm?",a="It is the crude cybernetic prosthetic grafted directly onto the body of Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a diseased gnome overseer lurking near the water wheel above Cragpool Lake. Rather than living with natural flesh, Gerenzo augmented his rotting frame with clockwork gears and metal plating, making this intricate mechanical limb his most recognizable feature.",al={"what is gerenzos arm","gerenzo arm item","gerenzos mechanical arm"},it="identity",add="379afa91"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The arm shows two different engineering traditions. Gnomes willingly sacrifice their own biology for mechanical precision, while goblins favor external additions and brute firepower.",["race:Gnome"]="Gerenzo represents a grim extreme of gnomish ingenuity, taking mechanical replacement far beyond conventional medical prosthetics and into morbid self-augmentation."},kw={"arm","cragpool lake","gerenzo","mechanical arm","sputtervalve","stonetalon","wrenchwhistle","ziz fizziks"},rel={"quest:1096","quest:1483","subzone:cragpool-lake","npc:sputtervalve","zone:stonetalon","subzone:gadgetzan","topic:gnome"},src={"Gerenzo's Mechanical Arm","Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle (quest)"}}
E["item:ken-zigla-s-draught"] = {t="item",n="Ken'zigla's Draught",z="stonetalon",s="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Ken'zigla prepares a bitter draught for the gravely wounded. A careful half dose restores enough strength to move, while more can make a patient bleed out.",h="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Ken'zigla prepares a bitter draught for the gravely wounded.",sec={{t="A Bitter Remedy",b="Ken'zigla prepares the draught in the Stonetalon Mountains for those near death. Its strength must be measured with care: more than half a dose at once can make the patient bleed out as their circulation surges. Half a dose gives a wounded person enough vigor to move and flee danger. The rest must wait until the body steadies after a full night's rest.",sp=0},{t="Mercy in the Barrens",b="Horde warlocks carry the draught into a hostile razormane encampment north of Camp Taurajo, where Dogran is held. The operative was captured and tortured by quilboar. The medicine gives him enough vitality to hobble away, though his severe wounds have permanently cost him the use of his limbs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Ken'zigla's Draught used for?",a="Ken'zigla's Draught restores strength to people who are dying or grievously injured. Given carefully, it can help a wounded person move and escape captivity without fatal bleeding.",al={"what does kenziglas draught do","draught purpose","why do i need kenziglas draught"},it="purpose"},{q="Who makes the draught?",a="Ken'zigla, who lives in the Stonetalon Mountains, prepares the draught.",al={"who brews the draught","who is kenzigla","kenzigla location"},it="origin"},{q="Why must the draught only be taken half at a time?",a="The draught is exceptionally harsh on the body. Half a dose gives enough vigor to move without causing severe bleeding; the other half must wait until the patient has rested for a night to avoid fatal strain.",al={"how to take kenziglas draught","half dose draught","draught instructions"},it="power"},{q="Who receives the draught?",a="Dogran receives the draught. He is an operative held prisoner and badly injured in a quilboar camp north of Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.",al={"who drinks the draught","who is dogran","where to deliver draught"},it="target"},{q="Why are warlocks sent to retrieve this medicine?",a="Horde warlocks seeking to bind a succubus are led to Dogran, who possesses an item of deep emotional resonance. Delivering the draught helps them reach him and secure what they need for the summoning ritual.",al={"why do warlocks need this","succubus quest draught","warlock quest kenzigla"},it="why_me"},{q="What is Ken'zigla's Draught?",a="It is a potent, foul-tasting medicinal brew prepared by the troll apothecary Ken'zigla in the Stonetalon Mountains. Crafted to sustain severe trauma, the concoction is powerful enough to restore a mortally wounded soldier's vitality and allow them to move, though it must be administered with great caution.",al={"what is the draught","kenziglas draught","kenzigla potion"},it="identity",add="6eadaa9a"},{q="Why is Ken'zigla's Draught needed?",a="An orc named Dogran was captured and brutally tortured by quilboar in the Barrens. Bleeding out and near death in captivity, he cannot survive or escape without the draught's restorative magic. Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo desperately requires the remedy so Dogran can withstand his injuries long enough to flee his captors.",al={"why do they need the draught","who needs kenziglas draught","why make the draught"},sp=1,it="why_wanted",add="42d17912"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you must find and deliver the draught during your trials to summon and bind a succubus. The journey across the Barrens tests your resourcefulness and tracking abilities.",["faction:Horde"]="With Camp Taurajo undermanned because of foraging patrols, the draught is the only lifeline for an operative captured behind enemy quilboar lines."},kw={"camp taurajo","dogran","grunt logmar","ken'zigla's draught","kenzigla","stonetalon mountains","succubus quest","the barrens"},rel={"quest:1511","quest:1515","quest:1509","quest:1512","quest:1471","npc:grunt-logmar","subzone:camp-taurajo","topic:quilboar"},src={"Ken'zigla's Draught","Ken'zigla's Draught (quest)","Dogran's Captivity"}}
E["item:letter-to-jin-zil"] = {t="item",n="Letter to Jin'Zil",z="stonetalon",s="At the Crossroads, Letter to Jin'Zil carries word of Serena Bloodfeather's defeat. Darsok Swiftdagger sends it to the Darkspear witch doctor in the Stonetalon Mountains, telling him the northern Barrens are free of the Bloodfeather threat.",h="At the Crossroads, Letter to Jin'Zil carries word of Serena Bloodfeather's defeat.",sec={{t="A Messenger to Stonetalon",b="After the harpies at the Dry Hills are wiped out and Serena Bloodfeather is slain, Darsok Swiftdagger writes to an old comrade. The harpies of the Barrens first roosted in the peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains. Darsok sends news of the fallen matron to Jin'Zil, a witch doctor, and introduces a promising warrior to the wider frontier.",sp=0},{t="Old Memories in Malaka'jin",b="At the cave in Malaka'jin, Jin'Zil receives the news with nostalgic satisfaction. Serena's death recalls the founding of Durotar after the Third War, when Rokhan, Jin'Zil's friend, joined Rexxar, a half-ogre beastmaster, to kill Serena's elder sister, Bloodfeather. Serena has fallen too, and Jin'Zil believes the Bloodfeather line's vengeance is ended.",sp=1,bt={"q867.3"}}},faq={{q="Who wrote the Letter to Jin'Zil?",a="Darsok Swiftdagger, an orc at the Crossroads in the Barrens, wrote the letter. He coordinates the defense against marauding harpy covens.",al={"who wrote this","letter sender","darsok letter"},it="origin"},{q="Where is Jin'Zil located?",a="Jin'Zil lives in a cave at Malaka'jin, a Darkspear troll outpost in the southeast crags of the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"where is jinzil","jin'zil location","find jinzil"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the news contained in the letter?",a="The letter tells Jin'Zil that Serena Bloodfeather, leader of the harpies descending into the northern Barrens, has been slain. Her death secures the perimeter north of the Crossroads.",al={"what does the letter say","letter message"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Jin'Zil care about the Bloodfeathers?",a="Jin'Zil remembers the founding of Durotar after the Third War, when his companion Rokhan and Rexxar, a half-ogre warrior, killed Serena's elder sister. Serena sought revenge against the Horde ever since, so her downfall brings a welcome resolution.",al={"why jinzil harpies","bloodfeather history","rokhan and bloodfeather"},sp=1,it="ties",bt={"q867.3"}},{q="Why does Jin'Zil want the Letter to Jin'Zil delivered to him?",a="The letter brings long-awaited news from his old friend Darsok Swiftdagger in the Barrens. Jin'Zil has not heard from Darsok in many years, and the missive confirms the death of Serena Bloodfeather, putting an end to the harpy matriarchs who troubled both the Barrens and Stonetalon.",al={"why deliver letter to jinzil","who wants letter to jinzil","why does jinzil care about the letter"},it="why_wanted",add="f9426e82"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you carry news from defending the Barrens into the deeper conflicts of the Stonetalon Mountains.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you can bring the letter to Witch Doctor Jin'Zil, an elder practitioner who carries on traditional voodoo outside the Echo Isles."},kw={"darsok swiftdagger","harpies","jin'zil","letter to jin'zil","malaka'jin","rokhan","serena bloodfeather","stonetalon"},rel={"quest:1060","quest:876","subzone:malaka-jin","zone:stonetalon","zone:barrens","topic:harpy","quest:875","quest:867"},src={"Letter to Jin'Zil","Letter to Jin'Zil (quest)"}}
E["item:maggran-s-reserve-letter"] = {t="item",n="Maggran's Reserve Letter",z="stonetalon",s="At Sun Rock Retreat, Maggran Earthbinder sends orders to relieve a guard at the Great Lift. The letter promises Grish Longrunner leave to visit his family.",h="At Sun Rock Retreat, Maggran Earthbinder sends orders to relieve a guard at the Great Lift.",sec={{t="A Sentry Relieved",b="Maggran Earthbinder sends orders from Sun Rock Retreat to the Great Lift. Grish Longrunner, a Horde sentry at the post, is to be relieved by a replacement warrior. The Great Lift's wooden winches stand far to the south, where Grish has kept watch. With the new warrior taking his place, he can leave his post and return home to visit his family.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Maggran's Reserve Letter?",a="Maggran Earthbinder's orders relieve Grish Longrunner from his post at the Great Lift in the southern Barrens, so he can return home and visit his family.",al={"what does this letter do","maggran letter purpose","why deliver letter"},it="purpose"},{q="Who wrote the letter?",a="Maggran Earthbinder wrote the letter. He is an elder at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who wrote it","author of reserve letter","maggran earthbinder"},it="origin"},{q="Who is meant to receive it?",a="The letter is addressed to Grish Longrunner, a Horde guard stationed at the top of the Great Lift, which connects the southern Barrens to Thousand Needles.",al={"who gets the letter","letter recipient","where does it go"},it="target"},{q="Where is the letter delivered?",a="Carry the letter south across the Barrens to the edge of the Thousand Needles canyon, where the Great Lift stands.",al={"delivery location","where is grish","great lift location"},it="place"},{q="What is Maggran's Reserve Letter?",a="It is an official written dispatch penned by Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. The message informs a stationed Horde guard, Grish Longrunner, that a relief warrior from the reserves is being dispatched to take over his post, granting him leave to visit his family.",al={"what is maggrans reserve letter","maggrans letter","reserve letter"},it="identity",add="419ae143"},{q="Why does Grish Longrunner want Maggran's Reserve Letter?",a="Grish requested relief from his post long ago and is eager for news. Guarding the Great Lift in the southern Barrens is a monotonous duty, and this letter formally authorizes his replacement by a reserve warrior, finally granting him long-awaited time away to visit his family.",al={"why does grish want the letter","why is the reserve letter wanted","why need maggrans reserve letter"},it="why_wanted",add="eb8a36e5"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see its effort to care for scattered forces by sending fresh reserves to remote outposts across Kalimdor."},kw={"barrens","earthbinder","grish","letter","lift","longrunner","maggran","reserve","stonetalon"},rel={"quest:5881","npc:maggran-earthbinder","npc:grish-longrunner","subzone:great-lift","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","zone:barrens","zone:thousandneedles"},src={"Maggran's Reserve Letter","Calling in the Reserves"}}
E["item:ng-5"] = {t="item",n="NG-5",z="stonetalon",s="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Gaxim Rustfizzle needs NG-5 for his explosive plans. The volatile chemical is Nitromirglyceronium, the ignition compound he needs to set off wagons loaded with dynamite as a distraction.",h="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Gaxim Rustfizzle needs NG-5 for his explosive plans.",sec={{t="A Volatile Reagent",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle, a gnome operative in the Stonetalon Mountains, needs NG-5 for his engineering plans. The compound is formally known as Nitromirglyceronium, a hazardous chemical solution that demands care—or reckless gnomish enthusiasm. Gaxim says it provides the reaction needed to detonate entire wagons loaded with dynamite, creating a massive explosion to distract his adversaries in the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is NG-5?",a="NG-5 is short for Nitromirglyceronium, a highly unstable chemical used as an ignition reagent in advanced demolition and gnomish engineering.",al={"what is ng5","what is nitromirglyceronium","ng 5 item"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants NG-5 and why?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle, a gnome engineer in the Stonetalon Mountains, needs NG-5 as the ignition compound for several wagons packed with dynamite, which he plans to use as a distraction.",al={"who needs ng-5","gaxim rustfizzle ng-5","why get ng5"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is NG-5 dangerous to handle?",a="NG-5 is extremely dangerous to handle. The supplier warns couriers to treat it with absolute care and jokes that anyone who is not Gaxim's ally will likely blow themselves to pieces.",al={"is ng5 safe","ng-5 explosive","will ng5 blow up"},it="danger"},{q="Where does NG-5 come from, and who made it?",a="NG-5, also known as Nitromirglyceronium, is obtained from an acquaintance of Gaxim Rustfizzle who brews specialized chemical compounds. It is an extremely volatile alchemical mixture concocted specifically for explosive reactions, handed over only with stern warnings about how easily it can blow an unwary courier to pieces.",al={"who made ng-5","where do you get ng-5","ng5 creator"},it="origin",add="43a87313"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers will recognize NG-5 as Nitromirglyceronium, a temperamental chemical catalyst prized by tinkers when ordinary black powder lacks the punch for heavy ordinance.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may recognize the high-risk ingenuity in using an unstable chemical to blow up whole wagons of dynamite as a simple distraction."},kw={"dynamite","explosives","gaxim rustfizzle","gnome","ng-5","ng5","nitromirglyceronium","stonetalon"},rel={"quest:1073","npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","zone:stonetalon"},src={"NG-5","Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun (2)"}}
E["item:ordanus-head"] = {t="item",n="Ordanus' Head",z="stonetalon",s="At Raynewood Retreat, Ordanus' Head is claimed as proof that Keeper Ordanus has fallen. Blood elf magi Braelyn Firehand seeks it in Ashenvale.",h="At Raynewood Retreat, Ordanus' Head is claimed as proof that Keeper Ordanus has fallen.",sec={{t="A Grudge from the Past",b="Keeper Ordanus was an ancient keeper of the grove and one of Cenarius's elder sons. Braelyn Firehand climbed the heights of Stonetalon Mountains on her master's orders, seeking to end the druids' stifling of magic at the peak and take vengeance on Ordanus. Before she could strike, the keeper was spirited away to the heart of Ashenvale. Braelyn used arcane scrying to peer through the forest canopy and found his sanctuary in the boughs of Raynewood Retreat. She demanded his severed head as proof that the wild demigod's arrogance had been answered.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Hubris",b="Braelyn holds an old grievance against Ordanus, whom she knew long ago, and hates the druids who seek to stifle magic. In life, Ordanus considered himself superior even to the ancient Highborne nobility. By taking his head, Braelyn Firehand strikes back at the legacy of Cenarius and declares that no guardian of the wild can stem the return of raw magical power.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Keeper Ordanus?",a="Keeper Ordanus was an ancient keeper of the grove and an elder son of Cenarius. Long ago, he clashed with arcane practitioners among the night elven nobility and was known for deep arrogance toward those who practiced the arcane arts.",al={"who is ordanus","ordanus lore","what is ordanus"},it="identity"},{q="Where is this head collected?",a="The head is claimed from Keeper Ordanus atop the elevated wooden platform at Raynewood Retreat, a fortified night elven canopy enclave in central Ashenvale.",al={"where to find ordanus head","ordanus location","raynewood retreat ordanus"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Braelyn Firehand want his head?",a="Braelyn Firehand knew Ordanus long ago and despised his arrogance; he held himself above even the Highborne. She also hates the druids and sons of Cenarius for trying to halt the flow of magic and for spiriting Ordanus away from the peak before she could reach him.",al={"why braelyn wants ordanus head","braelyn grudge","why kill ordanus"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens after the head is delivered?",a="Delivering Ordanus' Head to Braelyn at Sunrock Retreat satisfies her blood debt, and she rewards the mercenary with the mighty gift she promised.",al={"ordanus head turn in","after ordanus dies","braelyn firehand quest reward"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where does Ordanus' Head come from?",a="This grim trophy is taken directly from Keeper Ordanus, one of the eldest sons of the forest demigod Cenarius. Though once thought safe atop Stonetalon Peak, Ordanus fled into Ashenvale and took refuge high within Raynewood Retreat before being hunted down.",al={"ordanus head origin","where did ordanus head come from","who does ordanus head belong to"},it="origin",add="e1459048"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For a member of the Horde, striking down Ordanus and delivering his head to Braelyn helps cement the Horde's foothold across the contested borders of Stonetalon and Ashenvale, weakening local night elf leadership.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, carrying the severed head of an elder son of Cenarius is a stark reminder of the bitter, bloody animosity arcane sorcerers still bear toward the protectors of the wild."},kw={"ashenvale","braelyn firehand","cenarius","keeper of the grove","ordanus","ordanus' head","raynewood retreat","stonetalon","sunrock retreat"},rel={"quest:1088","npc:braelyn-firehand","subzone:raynewood-retreat","zone:ashenvale","zone:stonetalon","quest:1087","quest:1089","topic:cenarius"},src={"Ordanus' Head","Ordanus (quest)"}}
E["item:resonite-crystal"] = {t="item",n="Resonite Crystal",z="stonetalon",s="In Boulderslide Cavern, kobolds are digging frantically for Resonite Crystal. Their work has drawn Mor'rogal's concern at Sun Rock Retreat.",h="In Boulderslide Cavern, kobolds are digging frantically for Resonite Crystal.",sec={{t="Ancient Resonance",b="Resonite Crystal has drawn kobolds into frantic digging deep in Boulderslide Ravine. Their sudden focus on these stones alarms the shamans at Sun Rock Retreat. Mor'rogal examines the crystals and finds a faint magical hum. He recognizes traces of Earthen magic, signs that the kobolds have broken into an ancient layer shaped by the Titans.",sp=1,bt={"q6421.2"}},{t="Tapping the Earth",b="Resonite Crystal shows that kobold diggers have reached deep enough to disturb the ancient Earthen. The Titans shaped the Earthen to carve and mold the foundations of the world, and their magic still clings to the surrounding rock. Horde agents gather the crystals to learn what drives the kobolds and turn the enchanted stone's power against whatever slumbers below.",sp=1,bt={"q6421.2"}}},faq={{q="Where are Resonite Crystals found?",a="Resonite Crystals are found inside Boulderslide Cavern, deep within Boulderslide Ravine in the southeastern Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"resonite location","where to get resonite","resonite crystal farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the kobolds mining Resonite Crystals?",a="The kobolds are mining the rare crystals frantically, but Mor'rogal does not know why. He asks for samples and an investigation of the cave's depths to learn what they are doing.",al={"why kobolds mining","kobold crystal plot","boulderslide kobolds"},it="motive"},{q="What kind of power is in a Resonite Crystal?",a="Mor'rogal suspects the crystals connect to something troubling beneath the mountains. He identifies their magical nature after samples and news from the cavern reach him.",al={"resonite crystal magic","what is resonite","is resonite magical"},it="power"},{q="Who is studying these crystals?",a="Mor'rogal, a tauren at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains, studies the crystals to understand the sudden rise in kobold activity and find a way to counter the evil uncovered.",al={"who wants resonite","mor'rogal crystals","sun rock retreat resonite"},it="people"},{q="What are the Earthen mentioned in connection to the crystal?",a="The Earthen are said to have been created by the Titans to shape the land. Mor'rogal investigates a possible connection between them and Resonite.",al={"what are earthen","earthen titan connection"},it="origin"},{q="What is Resonite Crystal?",a="Resonite is a rare mineral crystal found in Boulderslide Cavern in the Stonetalon Mountains. The kobolds' frantic mining has alarmed Mor'rogal, who requests samples and news from the cave to investigate.",al={"what is resonite","resonite crystal lore","resonite ore"},it="identity",add="c14b6c8c"},{q="Why does anyone want Resonite Crystal?",a="Mor'rogal wants ore samples to understand the kobolds' frantic mining and learn what lies beneath Boulderslide Ravine. He asks an adventurer to explore the cave as well as gather the crystals.",al={"why gather resonite crystals","who wants resonite crystal","resonite crystal purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="af246400"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can sense the unsettling resonance in Resonite Crystals: dormant, primordial earth magic left by Titan creations buried beneath the mountains.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you find Resonite in intensely concentrated formations unlike ordinary copper or tin veins. Reaching it means delving past aggressive kobolds into the deepest subterranean strata."},kw={"boulderslide","crystal","earthen","kobold","mor'rogal","resonite","stonetalon","titans"},rel={"subzone:boulderslide-cavern","quest:6421","npc:mor-rogal","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","topic:kobold","topic:titan","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Resonite Crystal","Boulderslide Ravine (quest)"}}
E["item:scroll-of-messaging"] = {t="item",n="Scroll of Messaging",z="stonetalon",s="In Stonetalon, Gaxim Rustfizzle has a plan for the Scroll of Messaging. The gnome engineer means to use its sending spell to trigger remote explosives.",h="In Stonetalon, Gaxim Rustfizzle has a plan for the Scroll of Messaging.",sec={{t="A Volatile Message",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle plans to turn a message into a blast at the Venture Company's logging operation. He will combine the scroll's transmission incantation with volatile NG-5 charges. The explosion is meant to distract the guards, giving operatives time to slip past and steal engineering schematics and confidential correspondence.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Scroll of Messaging used for?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle uses the Scroll of Messaging's transmission magic as a remote trigger. Paired with NG-5, it lets him set off an explosion from a distance.",al={"scroll of messaging use","what does scroll of messaging do","why gaxim wants scroll"},it="purpose"},{q="Who receives this scroll?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle, a gnome engineer in the Stonetalon Mountains, receives the scroll.",al={"who gets scroll of messaging","where do i bring scroll of messaging","scroll recipient"},it="target"},{q="Why does Gaxim need a remote explosive?",a="Gaxim needs a major diversion at the Venture Company operation. The chaos will cover an infiltration, the theft of engineering plans, and the recovery of documents meant to halt the company's clear-cutting of the forest.",al={"gaxim explosive reason","why blow up venture co","stonetalon distraction"},it="motive"},{q="What is NG-5?",a="NG-5 is an explosive chemical charge used by Gaxim Rustfizzle. Combined with the scroll's magical signal, it forms a remote detonator.",al={"ng-5","what is ng-5","ng5 explosive"},it="item"},{q="What is the Scroll of Messaging?",a="The Scroll of Messaging is an enchanted parchment bearing an arcane spell. Gaxim Rustfizzle sought it out as an unconventional catalyst to combine with his volatile explosive compound, NG-5, enabling him to craft a remotely triggered charge against Venture Company operations in Stonetalon.",al={"what is scroll of messaging","scroll of messaging lore","about scroll of messaging"},it="identity",add="2071477e"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The scroll shows how gnomish engineering can put arcane magic to use as a receiver for remote explosives.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance operatives, the scroll helps sabotage Venture Company machinery and hinder its destruction of the Stonetalon forest."},kw={"explosives","gaxim rustfizzle","ng-5","remote detonator","scroll of messaging","stonetalon","venture co"},rel={"quest:1077","npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","item:ng-5","zone:stonetalon","quest:764"},src={"Scroll of Messaging","Special Delivery for Gaxim"}}
E["item:sealed-envelope"] = {t="item",n="Sealed Envelope",z="stonetalon",s="Fizziks has sealed Venture Company secrets inside the Sealed Envelope for delivery to Sputtervalve in Ratchet.",h="Fizziks has sealed Venture Company secrets inside the Sealed Envelope for delivery to Sputtervalve in Ratchet.",sec={{t="Corporate Espionage",b="After the Venture Company cast goblin engineer Fizziks out of its logging operations in the Stonetalon Mountains, he smuggled out company secrets. The envelope holds internal manuals, operating procedures, and technical specifications. Among them are schematics for the Super Reaper 6000, a machine built for industrial clear-cutting.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to Ratchet",b="Fizziks sends the documents south to Sputtervalve, an engineer in the neutral goblin port of Ratchet. The Steamwheedle Cartel's business rivals have little personal love or trust for Fizziks, yet the designs have undeniable engineering value. They reveal Venture Company mechanical ingenuity and give independent engineers a chance to exploit its advanced logging technologies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Sealed Envelope?",a="The envelope holds internal Venture Company documents, technical manuals, and schematics for the Super Reaper 6000, a wood-clearing machine. Fizziks stole them when he left the company in haste.",al={"envelope contents","what is in sealed envelope","sealed envelope items"},it="identity"},{q="Who prepared this packet?",a="Disgruntled goblin engineer Fizziks prepared the envelope after the Venture Company ejected him from its logging operation in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who made the envelope","who gave sealed envelope","fizziks envelope"},it="origin"},{q="Who is intended to receive it?",a="The envelope is meant for Sputtervalve, a goblin tinkerer in the port town of Ratchet, within the Barrens.",al={"who gets the envelope","where does envelope go","sputtervalve delivery"},it="target"},{q="Why does Sputtervalve want these documents?",a="Sputtervalve dislikes the Venture Company, and the documents offer valuable improvements and schematics that let outside tinkerers understand and adopt its powerful mechanical designs.",al={"why sputtervalve wants it","venture company tech ratchet"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The envelope holds technical drawings for the Super Reaper 6000, a destructive and lucrative machine devised by goblin hands.",["faction:Horde"]="Carrying these papers south from Stonetalon aids the neutral goblins of Ratchet in undermining the Venture Company's aggressive, exploitative logging operations."},kw={"blueprints","fizziks","ratchet","sealed envelope","sputtervalve","stonetalon","super reaper 6000","venture company"},rel={"quest:1094","item:super-reaper-6000-blueprints","npc:sputtervalve","topic:venture-company","zone:stonetalon","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","quest:1093"},src={"Sealed Envelope","Further Instructions"}}
E["item:sleepers-key"] = {t="item",n="Sleepers' Key",z="stonetalon",s="At Stonetalon Peak, Sleepers' Key helps guard a sacred druidic vault. Night elf druids made it one of three enchanted keys for the Talon Den Hoard.",h="At Stonetalon Peak, Sleepers' Key helps guard a sacred druidic vault.",sec={{t="A Druidic Safeguard",b="The Talon Den rises on Stonetalon Peak as a redoubt and sanctum for the druids of Kalimdor. To guard sacred relics and potent treasures from unwanted attention, night elf keepers built a system of locks and hidden caches. Sleepers' Key is one of three keys that together form a protective ward. The key lies in a secluded cache deep in the den, opened with the Gatekeeper's Key hidden near the threshold. The Claw Key and the Barrow Key complete the set. Set all three into the Talon Den Hoard's stone locks, and the ward fades, revealing the ancient items within.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sleepers' Key used for?",a="Sleepers' Key opens the Talon Den Hoard with the Barrow Key and Claw Key. The warded stone vault lies deep within the barrow den at Stonetalon Peak.",al={"what does sleepers key do","sleepers key purpose","talon den hoard keys"},it="purpose"},{q="How was the Sleepers' Key locked away?",a="The druids placed Sleepers' Key in the Sleepers' Cache in the Talon Den's northwestern tunnels. The Gatekeeper's Key opens it; the druids hid that key in an unassuming lantern near the den's entrance.",al={"where is sleepers key","opening sleepers cache","gatekeepers key requirement"}},{q="Why did the druids hide their relics with multiple keys?",a="The night elf druids built complex safeguards so their powerful items and sacred heirlooms would not fall into enemy hands if the den came under attack. By dispersing the keys among hidden caches, they made the hoard difficult for intruders to plunder.",al={"why so many keys","talon den defense","druid hoard puzzle"},it="motive"},{q="Why is it called the Sleepers' Key?",a="The druids never explain the name. Sleepers' Key shares it with the Sleepers' Cache, the hidden chest in the Talon Den where the key is kept.",al={"who are the sleepers","sleepers key name meaning"},it="name"},{q="What is the Sleepers' Key?",a="The Sleepers' Key is one of three specialized keys crafted by the night elf druids of Stonetalon Peak. Concealed within a locked cache deep inside the Talon Den, it forms an essential component of the warding system guarding the druids' central hoard of sacred relics.",al={"what is sleepers key","sleepers key lore","about sleepers key"},it="identity",add="0a862a33"},{q="Where does the Sleepers' Key come from, and who made it?",a="The key was fashioned by the druids who established the Talon Den on Stonetalon Peak. To safeguard their potent artifacts from intruders, they devised an intricate security scheme, securing the key inside a dedicated chest called the Sleepers' Cache.",al={"who made sleepers key","sleepers key origin","where did sleepers key come from"},it="origin",add="8275ad63"},{q="Why does anyone want the Sleepers' Key?",a="The Horde seeks the key to bypass the druids' layered defenses and unlock the Talon Den Hoard. Together with the Claw Key and the Barrow Key, it opens the stone vault holding the powerful relics the druids stashed away on Stonetalon Peak.",al={"why find sleepers key","why need sleepers key","who wants sleepers key"},it="why_wanted",add="3884172c"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see how the Talon Den keys and caches layer defenses, using hidden caches and keyed locks to seal away relics of power.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, acquiring Sleepers' Key is part of an orchestrated raid into the heart of Stonetalon Peak, stripping away the night elves' defensive wards to claim the relics sealed in their hoard."},kw={"gatekeeper's key","sleepers cache","sleepers key","sleepers' key","stonetalon peak","talon den","talon den hoard","the den"},rel={"quest:1089","item:barrow-key","item:claw-key","subzone:stonetalon-peak","zone:stonetalon","quest:1088","quest:1087","topic:druid"},src={"Sleepers' Key","The Den (quest)"}}
E["item:smoldering-embers"] = {t="item",n="Smoldering Embers",z="stonetalon",s="In the Charred Vale, Smoldering Embers remain after fire elementals are extinguished. Night elf Sentinels gather them as proof that the fires are being subdued.",h="In the Charred Vale, Smoldering Embers remain after fire elementals are extinguished.",sec={{t="Remnants of the Charred Vale",b="Venture Company logging and industry set the Charred Vale ablaze and stirred destructive forces from deep within the earth. Burning Ravagers, Burning Destroyers, and Rogue Flame Spirits then swept across the scorched basin. When an elemental is extinguished, its ash-covered core remains as a Smoldering Ember. These cinders show that the fires overrunning the vale are being brought under control.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Smoldering Embers come from?",a="Smoldering Embers come from fire elementals in the Charred Vale of southern Stonetalon Mountains. Burning Ravagers, Burning Destroyers, and Rogue Flame Spirits all leave them behind.",al={"where do i find smoldering embers","who drops smoldering embers","smoldering ember source"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Kaela Shadowspear want these embers?",a="Kaela Shadowspear wants the embers as proof that the fire elementals in the Charred Vale are being culled. She believes the scarred land cannot heal under Elune's grace while violent spirits roam unchecked.",al={"why collect smoldering embers","kaela shadowspear embers","enraged spirits goal"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What caused the fire elementals to appear in the Charred Vale?",a="The Venture Company brought fire elementals to the Charred Vale by clearing the ancient forest with aggressive machinery and indiscriminate burning. Its reckless exploitation destabilized the land and unleashed hostile elementals of flame and stone, which drove the goblins out.",al={"what happened to charred vale","why are there fire elementals in stonetalon","venture co fire spirits"},it="history"},{q="What are Smoldering Embers?",a="Smoldering Embers are the burning physical remains left behind by the destructive fire elementals infesting the Charred Vale. These glowing remnants linger after creatures like Burning Ravagers, Rogue Flame Spirits, and Burning Destroyers are slain, serving as tangible proof that their fiery rampage across the ruined forest has been quelled.",al={"what are smoldering embers","smoldering embers lore","what is smoldering ember"},it="identity",add="4d13fc7e"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the Charred Vale burning is a wound upon Kalimdor. Gathering its embers is a solemn duty to purge foreign desecration and restore peace beneath Elune's gaze.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the embers as tragic proof that industrial greed has unbalanced nature. Elemental fury keeps the ash-choked soil from regenerating."},kw={"burning destroyer","burning ravager","charred vale","enraged spirits","kaela shadowspear","rogue flame spirit","smoldering embers","stonetalon","venture co"},rel={"quest:1083","subzone:charred-vale","npc:kaela-shadowspear","zone:stonetalon","quest:764","topic:elune"},src={"Smoldering Embers","Enraged Spirits"}}
E["item:stonetalon-sap"] = {t="item",n="Stonetalon Sap",z="stonetalon",s="Near Mirkfallon Lake and Stonetalon Peak, sap beasts carry the sap Jin'Zil seeks. The Darkspear witch doctor uses it in a brew for his caged night elf prisoners.",h="Near Mirkfallon Lake and Stonetalon Peak, sap beasts carry the sap Jin'Zil seeks.",sec={{t="A Bitter Harvest",b="Sap beasts near Mirkfallon Lake and Stonetalon Peak carry a potent woodland fluid. Jin'Zil of Malaka'jin seeks the sap for a brew he calls forest magic. He intends it for his caged night elf prisoners, turning the essence of their cherished wilderness against them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What creatures carry Stonetalon Sap?",a="Sap beasts near Mirkfallon Lake and on the slopes toward Stonetalon Peak carry Stonetalon Sap.",al={"where do you get stonetalon sap","who drops stonetalon sap","sap beasts"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What does Witch Doctor Jin'Zil use the sap for?",a="Jin'Zil combines the sap with courser eyes, twilight whiskers, and a fey dragon scale to make a toxic brew for his caged night elf prisoners.",al={"why does jin'zil want sap","jin'zil forest magic recipe"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the best place to find sap beasts?",a="Sap beasts live in the groves around Mirkfallon Lake and along the paths toward Stonetalon Peak.",al={"sap beast location","mirkfallon lake sap beasts"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is the sap magical on its own?",a="The sap carries the vitality of the Stonetalon highlands, but Jin'Zil needs troll mojo and specific reagents to make it lethal.",al={"is stonetalon sap magic","properties of stonetalon sap"},it="power"},{q="What is Stonetalon Sap?",a="Stonetalon Sap is a sticky, natural resin gathered from the sap beasts that roam the Stonetalon Mountains, particularly around places like Mirkfallon Lake and Stonetalon Peak. It is thick, viscous, and full of raw natural essence, making it an ideal component for concoctions and voodoo brews that tap into the peculiar magic of the local wilderness.",al={"what is stonetalon sap","stonetalon sap item","about stonetalon sap"},it="identity",add="b24da591"},{q="Where does Stonetalon Sap come from?",a="This amber sap is harvested directly from the living sap beasts that wander the forests and lake shores of the Stonetalon Mountains. It is not manufactured or distilled by any mortal craftsman, but rather secreted naturally by these bizarre, primordial plant creatures.",al={"stonetalon sap source","where to get sap","origin of stonetalon sap"},it="origin",add="7615d27b"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil shows how the Darkspear can turn an enemy's beloved surroundings into a weapon of voodoo.",["race:NightElf"]="A Horde witch doctor poisons caged night elf prisoners with Stonetalon's native elements, an outrage against nature and Elune."},kw={"jin'zil","malaka'jin","mirkfallon lake","sap beast","stonetalon peak","stonetalon sap"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-jin-zil","quest:1058","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","subzone:stonetalon-peak","subzone:malaka-jin","item:courser-eye","item:fey-dragon-scale","item:twilight-whisker"},src={"Stonetalon Sap","Jin'Zil's Forest Magic"}}
E["item:super-reaper-6000-blueprints"] = {t="item",n="Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints",z="stonetalon",s="In Windshear Crag, the Venture Company’s Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints are coveted by goblin rivals. They hold the technical schematics for an enormous mechanized woodcutter deployed in Stonetalon Mountains, designed under gnome engineer Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle’s supervision.",h="In Windshear Crag, the Venture Company’s Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints are coveted by goblin rivals.",sec={{t="Industrial Espionage in Windshear Crag",b="Venture Company operators carry the Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints through Windshear Crag. The plans show how to build the massive mechanized lumber harvesters driving the company’s relentless clear-cutting. To the dismay of traditional goblin engineers, the Venture Company put Gerenzo, a gnome, in charge of designing the model. When goblin engineer Ziz Fizziks was ousted from the operation, Sputtervalve quickly hired him to steal the designs. Yet Gerenzo’s dense, eccentric gnomish notations are almost as hard to decipher as the plans are to take by force.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Super Reaper 6000?",a="The Super Reaper 6000 is an enormous mechanized woodcutter developed for the Venture Company’s clear-cutting in Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"what is super reaper","super reaper machine"},it="identity"},{q="Who designed the Super Reaper 6000?",a="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a gnome engineer, designed the plans under the Venture Company’s supervision after being hired to lead its mechanical efforts in Windshear Crag. His appointment annoyed local goblin mechanics.",al={"who made blueprints","who designed super reaper"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Ziz Fizziks want these blueprints?",a="After the Venture Company ousted Ziz Fizziks, Sputtervalve hired him to steal the plans. Ziz wants to prove his worth and mechanical genius to his new boss.",al={"why does ziz want plans","who wants blueprints"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who holds the blueprints in Windshear Crag?",a="Venture Co. operators carrying the physical schematics oversee machinery and clear timber throughout Windshear Crag.",al={"where do blueprints drop","who drops blueprints"},it="target"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how Gerenzo’s precise gnomish schematics leave ordinary tinkers baffled, even as goblin corporate muscle puts the machinery to work.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle’s ingenuity at work in the blueprints. Even the Venture Company relies on a gnome engineer to design its complex heavy machinery."},kw={"blueprints","gerenzo","sputtervalve","stonetalon","super reaper 6000","venture company","windshear crag","ziz fizziks"},rel={"quest:1093","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","npc:sputtervalve","topic:venture-company","topic:gnome","topic:goblin","quest:1483"},src={"Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints","Super Reaper 6000 (quest)"}}
E["item:toxic-fogger"] = {t="item",n="Toxic Fogger",z="stonetalon",s="In Stonetalon, the Toxic Fogger is bound for the Venture Company's air routes. The Forsaken Royal Apothecary Society filled the device with lethal poison to contaminate the company's flights.",h="In Stonetalon, the Toxic Fogger is bound for the Venture Company's air routes.",sec={{t="A Forsaken Solution",b="Apothecary Zamah sends the Toxic Fogger against the Venture Company's mining work. Apothecary Lydon brewed its toxin in Tarren Mill, and Zamah dispatched it from Thunder Bluff. She suspects the goblins use courier flying machines to carry messages and light cargo between Stonetalon and their headquarters. Her plan is to release the poison where those machines land and refuel. The Forsaken aim to strike the company's supply route instead of fighting its mercenary crews in drawn-out skirmishes.",sp=0},{t="Sabotage at Cragpool Lake",b="The Toxic Fogger is meant for the Venture Company's copter pad near Cragpool Lake. The secluded landing site stands above the cleared hills and links distant crews with outside hubs. Releasing the fogger spreads toxic vapor across the staging ground, catching returning pilots unaware. Some Horde may recoil at using poison, but Zamah tells her agents to put guilt aside. She believes no method is too dark if it brings victory over the exploiters.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Toxic Fogger used for?",a="The Toxic Fogger is meant to poison the Venture Company's sky port at Cragpool Lake in the Stonetalon Mountains. Its vapor contaminates the light cargo and couriers headed to company headquarters.",al={"what does toxic fogger do","fogger purpose","why use toxic fogger"},it="purpose"},{q="Who created the Toxic Fogger?",a="Apothecary Lydon brewed the toxin in Tarren Mill from the blood of innocents. Apothecary Zamah, an envoy of the Royal Apothecary Society in the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff, sent it for delivery.",al={"who made the fogger","toxic fogger creator","apothecary zamah poison"},it="origin"},{q="Where does the Toxic Fogger need to be placed?",a="Plant the Toxic Fogger atop the elevated Venture Company copter pad near Cragpool Lake in the Stonetalon Mountains, south of the large waterwheel.",al={"where do i put the fogger","copter pad location","sky port location"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does the Horde resort to using poison against the Venture Company?",a="The Venture Company's logging and mining ravage Stonetalon. Apothecary Zamah considers conventional combat too slow and believes the Horde must use ruthless methods to destroy the goblins before they cause irreparable harm.",al={"why poison goblins","is poison allowed in horde","forsaken methods in stonetalon"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Toxic Fogger?",a="The Toxic Fogger is a specialized dispersal device filled with a lethal concoction crafted by the Forsaken. Designed to release a noxious cloud upon deployment, it serves as an instrument of sabotage intended to contaminate the Venture Company's logistics network and disrupt their operations in Stonetalon.",al={"what is toxic fogger","toxic fogger item","toxic fogger device"},it="identity",add="3a36a6bd"},{q="Why does Apothecary Zamah want the Toxic Fogger deployed?",a="Apothecary Zamah intends to strike directly at the Venture Company's supply chain. By deploying the fogger at their small sky port, the toxin can coat departing flying machines and cargo, carrying the poison back to the goblins' headquarters and delivering devastating payback for their unchecked exploitation.",al={"why use toxic fogger","why want toxic fogger","why toxic fogger needed"},it="why_wanted",add="bbff0049"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see the Royal Apothecary Society's field strategy at work: disrupting enemy supplies with airborne toxins and showing allies that dark methods can bring results.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you may find lethal vapors at odds with traditional codes of honor. The Venture Company's damage to the land leads many in Thunder Bluff to tolerate Zamah's harsh measures."},kw={"apothecary zamah","copter pad","cragpool lake","sky port","stonetalon","toxic fogger","venture company"},rel={"quest:1086","quest:853","subzone:cragpool-lake","zone:stonetalon","topic:venture-company","topic:forsaken","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Toxic Fogger","The Flying Machine Airport"}}
E["item:twilight-whisker"] = {t="item",n="Twilight Whisker",z="stonetalon",s="In Malaka'jin, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil gathers Twilight Whisker for his brew. Twilight runners carry the whiskers in the northern heights of the Stonetalon Mountains.",h="In Malaka'jin, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil gathers Twilight Whisker for his brew.",sec={{t="A Witch Doctor's Reagent",b="Twilight runners prowl the high crags near Stonetalon Peak. Hunters prize their pelts, while Witch Doctor Jin'Zil of Malaka'jin wants their stiff whiskers for a darker purpose. He seeks vengeance on night elves captured after defending these woodlands. To mock and poison his captives, Jin'Zil gathers resinous sap, countless eyes, fey dragon scales, and Twilight Whisker for a lethal draught he calls forest magic.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Twilight Whiskers found?",a="Twilight runners on the slopes around Stonetalon Peak in the northern Stonetalon Mountains carry Twilight Whisker.",al={"twilight whisker location","who drops twilight whiskers","where to get twilight whiskers"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Witch Doctor Jin'Zil want them?",a="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil combines Twilight Whisker with sap, courser eyes, and a fey dragon scale to brew a deadly concoction for his night elf captives in Malaka'jin.",al={"jinzil whiskers","why does jinzil want twilight whiskers","jin'zil forest magic ingredients"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens after Jin'Zil receives the whiskers?",a="After receiving the ingredients, Jin'Zil unleashes his brew in his cave. It swiftly kills the caged night elf prisoners, whose spirits emerge as wisps and drift away.",al={"forest magic outcome","what happens to the prisoners"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is a Twilight Whisker?",a="A Twilight Whisker is a stiff facial hair harvested from the twilight runners prowling the heights of Stonetalon Mountains. To most, it is merely beast offal, but to practitioners of voodoo and alchemy, it serves as a potent reagent carrying the wild essence of the local predators.",al={"what is twilight whisker","twilight whisker info","what are twilight whiskers"},it="identity",add="15466f07"},{q="Where does a Twilight Whisker come from?",a="Twilight Whiskers are plucked from twilight runners, predatory felines native to the Stonetalon Mountains. They are not crafted by mortal hands, but rather taken directly from the beasts roaming near Stonetalon Peak.",al={"twilight whisker origin","where to get twilight whisker","who drops twilight whisker"},it="origin",add="8f61da64"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you see Jin'Zil use local beasts as reagents in Darkspear voodoo, turning the forest's natural essence against his enemies.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see sacred woodland creatures like twilight runners and fey dragons desecrated to poison night elf captives in Kalimdor's forests."},kw={"forest magic","malaka'jin","stonetalon mountains","stonetalon peak","twilight runner","twilight whisker","witch doctor jin'zil"},rel={"quest:1058","npc:witch-doctor-jin-zil","item:stonetalon-sap","item:fey-dragon-scale","item:courser-eye","subzone:stonetalon-peak","subzone:malaka-jin","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Twilight Whisker","Jin'Zil's Forest Magic"}}
E["item:unidentified-ore"] = {t="item",n="Unidentified Ore",z="stonetalon",s="At Windshear Crag, Unidentified Ore draws the Venture Company's attention. Piznik recovered a sample and passed it to Ziz Fizziks for study in Undermine.",h="At Windshear Crag, Unidentified Ore draws the Venture Company's attention.",sec={{t="A Curious Strike in Windshear",b="The Venture Company's clear-cutting and strip mining at Windshear Crag exposed unusual mineral strata in the Stonetalon Mountains. The site's new boss, Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, ordered large amounts of strange gold-green ore mined. Demoted goblin worker Piznik remained loyal to his fired former boss, Ziz Fizziks, and secured a sample while plotting his exit from the outfit. He handed it to a traveler bound for the crag's western ridge. Ziz planned to send most of the ore to Undermine for study and keep a small cut for personal profit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Unidentified Ore?",a="The Unidentified Ore is a mineral sample dug up during Venture Company operations at Windshear Crag. Its composition draws the interest of Ziz Fizziks and mining engineers in Undermine.",al={"what is this ore","unidentified ore lore","what rock is this"},it="identity"},{q="Who found the ore?",a="Piznik, a Venture Company goblin stationed at Windshear Crag, salvaged the sample. After recent mishaps, he feared retribution from company supervisors and saw a chance to flee and secure new employment.",al={"who dug it up","who gives the ore","piznik ore"}},{q="Who is trying to study this sample?",a="Ziz Fizziks, a goblin camped along the western edge of Windshear Crag, received the mineral. He plans to send most of it to engineers in Undermine and keep a small portion for himself.",al={"who wants the ore","who analyzes it","ziz fizziks ore"}},{q="Why does Undermine care about this stone?",a="Goblins scout for new explosive, metallurgical, or combustible materials. A strange mineral from Kalimdor's ancient mountains could hold industrial and commercial potential for the trade cartels.",al={"undermine interest","why do goblins want it"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the Unidentified Ore come from?",a="The sample comes from the Venture Company's mine in Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains, where the site's new boss, Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, ordered large amounts of a strange gold-green ore dug up. Piznik, still loyal to his fired former boss Ziz Fizziks, mined a sample in secret so it could be taken to Ziz.",al={"unidentified ore origin","where was unidentified ore found","where did the ore come from"},it="origin",add="4673b3b7"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners find ordinary veins throughout Windshear Crag, but this sample defies common trade knowledge and intrigues even Undermine's best appraisers.",["profession:Engineering"]="Goblincraft seeks raw compounds with unique reactive properties, so unclassified ores from untamed crags give innovative tinkers material to study."},kw={"piznik","stonetalon","undermine","unidentified ore","venture company","windshear crag","ziz fizziks"},rel={"quest:1090","npc:piznik","quest:1483","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Unidentified Ore","Gerenzo's Orders (2)"}}
E["item:venture-co-engineering-plans"] = {t="item",n="Venture Co. Engineering Plans",z="stonetalon",s="At Windshear Crag, the Venture Co. Engineering Plans reveal how the logging machinery is built. Alliance operatives recover the schematics from the goblin mill.",h="At Windshear Crag, the Venture Co.",sec={{t="Industrial Secrets",b="Inside the lumber mill south of Cragpool Lake, the Venture Co. Engineering Plans show the construction, strengths, and flaws of the timber-harvesting machines. The Venture Company uses those machines to strip the forests of Stonetalon, while smoke hangs over Windshear Crag.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Espionage",b="Gnome engineer Gaxim Rustfizzle directs a covert operation against the Venture Company's logging works and seeks the plans. Explosives can disrupt the mill at once, while the schematics let Alliance craftspeople exploit weaknesses in goblin equipment and adapt its designs for Alliance projects.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are the Venture Co. Engineering Plans located?",a="The Venture Co. Engineering Plans are inside the Venture Company's primary lumber mill at Windshear Crag, south of Cragpool Lake in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"where to find engineering plans","plans location stonetalon","where are the plans"},gp=true},{q="Who wants these engineering plans?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle, an Alliance gnome coordinating covert actions in the Stonetalon Mountains, sends agents to recover the plans.",al={"who needs the plans","who turns in engineering plans","gaxim rustfizzle plans"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are these blueprints important to the Alliance?",a="The schematics reveal flaws in the Venture Company's logging machinery, helping operatives dismantle it and giving Alliance gnomes industrial designs to adapt for their own inventions.",al={"why steal the plans","what do the plans do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What operation is tied to stealing these plans?",a="Recovering the plans is the chief aim of Covert Ops - Alpha. Agents also plant detonators throughout the site, but returning with the blueprints marks the operation's success.",al={"covert ops alpha objective","what quest is this for"},it="purpose"},{q="What are the Venture Co. Engineering Plans?",a="These documents contain detailed technical schematics and blueprints created by the Venture Company's engineers in Stonetalon Mountains. Kept inside their lumber mill near Cragpool Lake, they outline the construction, wiring, and operational designs behind the deforesting machinery and industrial contraptions the company relies upon to clear Windshear Crag.",al={"what are venture co engineering plans","venture company engineering plans","venture co plans"},it="identity",add="605bae91"},{q="Where do the Venture Co. Engineering Plans come from?",a="The plans originated from the Venture Company's industrial operations in Windshear Crag. Developed by their own engineers and operators to oversee logging and mechanical construction, they were kept secure within the main lumber mill located just south of Cragpool Lake before being targeted by Alliance covert operatives.",al={"where did the engineering plans come from","who made venture co engineering plans","origin of venture co plans"},it="origin",add="a84a85f7"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome tinkerer, capturing rival goblin schematics offers an intellectual victory and industrial ideas to adapt.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can study the Venture Company's brutal, resource-hungry machines for insights into heavy industrial machinery."},kw={"covert ops","cragpool lake","engineering plans","gaxim rustfizzle","stonetalon","venture co.","windshear crag"},rel={"quest:1079","npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","item:covert-ops-pack","subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:cragpool-lake","zone:stonetalon","quest:764"},src={"Venture Co. Engineering Plans","Covert Ops - Alpha"}}
E["item:venture-co-letters"] = {t="item",n="Venture Co. Letters",z="stonetalon",s="At Windshear Mine, Venture Co. Letters carry word of the cartel's work in Stonetalon Mountains. Recovered amid explosive distractions, they give the night elf Sentinels intelligence on goblin operations.",h="At Windshear Mine, Venture Co.",sec={{t="Industrial Intelligence",b="Venture Company machines cut timber and strip-mine the ancient woodland around Windshear Crag. Alliance operatives set off covert sabotage to distract the workers and enter Windshear Mine. The letters they recover hold private messages and logistical records of the company's local work. Sentinel leaders can learn how the defilers arrange their workforce and supply lines from those records.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to the Sentinels",b="The letters are carried from deep inside Windshear Mine to Sentinel commander Kaela Shadowspear. Goblin defilers and Horde incursions both pressure the Sentinels across Stonetalon. The stolen correspondence helps them anticipate the Venture Company's next moves and protect what remains of the sacred mountains.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are the Venture Co. Letters?",a="The Venture Co. Letters are internal correspondence and operational records kept by the Venture Company at Windshear Mine in Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"venture co letters","what are the letters","stonetalon letters"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the letters found?",a="The letters are among Venture Co. Documents inside Windshear Mine, at the eastern end of Windshear Crag.",al={"where are the letters","letters location","windshear mine letters"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants these letters?",a="Gnome operative Gaxim Rustfizzle oversees the effort to steal the letters, which are delivered to Kaela Shadowspear, leader of the local night elf Sentinels.",al={"who gets the letters","who wants them","turn in letters"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why do the Sentinels need this correspondence?",a="The Sentinels fight to halt deforestation and excavation in Stonetalon. The letters reveal Venture Company plans and priorities, helping the defenders plan against them.",al={"why do sentinels want letters","sentinel interest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do the Venture Co. Letters come from, and who wrote them?",a="These documents originate from the Venture Company's mining operation at Windshear Mine, situated at the far eastern edge of Windshear Crag. They comprise internal corporate correspondence kept among the documents at the site, written by the company's regional operators and overseers to coordinate their aggressive extraction and logging efforts across Stonetalon.",al={"venture co letters origin","who wrote the venture co letters","where do the letters come from"},it="origin",add="52f3029e"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Goblin lumber machines desecrate Stonetalon's wilderness. Intelligence on Venture Company schemes matters greatly to the Sentinels.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts carry out covert operations against the Venture Company to protect night elf holdings in Stonetalon from industrial exploitation."},kw={"kaela shadowspear","sentinels","stonetalon mountains","venture co","venture co. letters","windshear crag","windshear mine"},rel={"quest:1080","quest:1091","npc:kaela-shadowspear","item:venture-co-documents","item:covert-ops-pack","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","topic:sentinels"},src={"Venture Co. Letters","Covert Ops - Beta","Kaela's Update"}}
E["npc:braelyn-firehand"] = {t="npc",n="Braelyn Firehand",z="stonetalon",s="At Sun Rock Retreat, Braelyn Firehand lives among the Horde and draws travelers into a campaign against the night elves of Stonetalon Peak.",h="At Sun Rock Retreat, Braelyn Firehand lives among the Horde and draws travelers into a campaign against the...",sec={{t="An Unlikely Guest",b="At Sun Rock Retreat, Braelyn Firehand is a blood elf living openly among tauren lodges and orcish tents. The retreat’s shamans and chieftains tolerate her, apparently unaware of her true loyalties. She calls herself an observer of the region’s magic and hires passing Horde mercenaries for dangerous work among the crags.",sp=0},{t="A Grudge Against the Grove",b="Braelyn Firehand sends her allies against the night elven druids and Cenarius’s sacred offspring at Stonetalon Peak. She says the druids choke the ley lines and hinder arcane power across the peaks. Her grievance is personal: she remembers Keeper Ordanus as arrogant, believing himself above even the Highborne. She pays Horde travelers to hunt him down and bring back his head.",sp=1},{t="Ties to Jaedenar",b="Braelyn Firehand’s hatred serves the aims of the Shadow Council sect in Jaedenar, Felwood. She urges Horde champions to kill the night elves and the keepers guarding the sacred peaks, clearing the way for darker powers while disguising her ties as frontier skirmishes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Braelyn Firehand?",a="Braelyn Firehand is an elven mage living at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. Though surrounded by the Horde, she pursues an arcane campaign against the night elves guarding Stonetalon Peak.",al={"who is braelyn","braelyn firehand lore","elf in sun rock retreat"},it="identity"},{q="Why is an elf staying in Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Sun Rock Retreat is an isolated frontier camp that tolerates Braelyn. She uses its steady flow of Horde warriors to hire attackers against the night elves without drawing immediate suspicion from its leaders.",al={"why is she with the horde","why is braelyn in sun rock","blood elf in stonetalon"},it="why_here"},{q="What does she want done at Stonetalon Peak?",a="Braelyn asks travelers to attack the druids and children of Cenarius at Stonetalon Peak, claiming they hinder the flow of magic. Her pursuit of Keeper Ordanus takes her to Raynewood Retreat in Ashenvale.",al={"braelyn quest goals","why kill ordanus","braelyn firehand tasks"},it="wants"},{q="What is her history with Keeper Ordanus?",a="Braelyn claims she knew Keeper Ordanus personally in the distant past. She bitterly resents his immense arrogance and says he considered himself superior even to the ancient Highborne.",al={"braelyn and ordanus","how does she know ordanus","ordanus backstory"},it="history"},{q="What does Braelyn Firehand claim to be researching?",a="Braelyn claims the druids and children of Cenarius at Stonetalon Peak restrict the flow of magic. She wants them gone so she can draw on that power.",al={"braelyn true faction","braelyn shadow council","who does she work for"},sp=2,it="side"},{q="Is Braelyn a mage or a warlock?",a="Braelyn practices arcane magic and fights with Fireballs.",al={"braelyn class","is braelyn a warlock","braelyn firehand spells"},sp=2},{q="Who is Braelyn Firehand tied to?",a="Braelyn serves a master in Jaedenar and is tied to the Shadow Council. She recruits Horde travelers for attacks on the night elves and children of Cenarius.",al={"braelyn firehand ties","who is braelyn affiliated with","braelyn firehand allies"},sp=1,it="ties",add="deec6fbf"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find Braelyn hiring wanderers to strike the night elves. Their territorial clashes in Kalimdor give cover to her deeper agenda.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may recognize Braelyn’s talk of ley energies and mystical blockages. She appeals to those who understand arcane magic flowing through the land.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the slaughter of Cenarius’s sons and the plundering of Talon Den as crimes against nature’s balance."},kw={"braelyn","cenarius","firehand","highborne","ordanus","stonetalon","sun rock retreat"},rel={"subzone:sun-rock-retreat","quest:1088","quest:1087","quest:1089","subzone:stonetalon-peak","topic:shadow-council","subzone:jaedenar","topic:highborne"},src={"Braelyn Firehand"}}
E["npc:darn-talongrip"] = {t="npc",n="Darn Talongrip",z="stonetalon",s="Near Malaka'jin, Darn Talongrip watches the Stonetalon frontier. The orc scout tracks threats in the crags and carries word between forward outposts and Horde commanders.",h="Near Malaka'jin, Darn Talongrip watches the Stonetalon frontier.",sec={{t="Frontier Scout of Stonetalon",b="Darn Talongrip watches the rugged climbs into Stonetalon from the southern Barrens. At Malaka'jin, he directs recruits toward the Horde's new fronts in Ashenvale. Travelers climbing into the contested peaks can reach the Horde through his post.",sp=0},{t="Eyes for the Command",b="From Malaka'jin, Darn sends messages and reports from the front to commanders such as Kadrak, at the watch tower in the northern Barrens. Encampments scattered through the mountains face constant pressure, and Darn keeps the Horde vanguard informed as a sentry and courier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Darn Talongrip?",a="Darn Talongrip scouts for the Horde from Malaka'jin in the southern Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who is darn talongrip","darn talongrip identity","who is this orc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Darn Talongrip be found?",a="Darn Talongrip can be found in the troll settlement of Malaka'jin, in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"darn talongrip location","where is darn talongrip","darn talongrip coordinates"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is his role in Stonetalon?",a="Darn directs recruits to Kadrak in the northern Barrens to help defend the Horde's outposts in Ashenvale.",al={"what does darn talongrip do","darn talongrip purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Kadrak, and why does Darn send travelers to him?",a="Kadrak commands the Horde from the watch tower in the northern Barrens and leads its Ashenvale campaign. Darn sends recruits to him to help defend the Horde's new fronts in Ashenvale.",al={"who is kadrak","report to kadrak"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Darn Talongrip on?",a="Darn Talongrip stands firmly with the Horde. Operating out of Stonetalon Mountains near Malaka'jin, he works alongside fellow orcs to secure the rugged trails and further the Horde's foothold across Kalimdor.",al={"darn talongrip faction","is darn talongrip horde","who does darn talongrip serve"},it="side",add="b53227de"},{q="What does Darn Talongrip want?",a="Darn Talongrip looks to protect the Horde's presence along the pass and direct able-bodied adventurers where their strength is needed most, particularly by dispatching travelers to assist Kadrak with urgent Horde operations nearby.",al={"what is darn talongrip looking for","darn talongrip goals","what does darn want"},it="wants",add="3e5a66b7"},{q="Why is Darn Talongrip here in Stonetalon?",a="Stationed around Malaka'jin and the surrounding passes of the Stonetalon Mountains, Darn Talongrip maintains the Horde's frontier presence, keeping watch over the mountain roads and ensuring reports flow swiftly between outpost sentries.",al={"why is darn talongrip in stonetalon","why is darn here","darn talongrip stonetalon reason"},it="why_here",add="d56f5cfb"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Darn Talongrip watches the ascent into Stonetalon and gives Horde adventurers fresh from the Barrens a point of contact.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the harsh frontier where Darn keeps watch among jagged rocks and hostile wildlife."},kw={"darn talongrip","kadrak","malakajin","orc scout","stonetalon"},rel={"subzone:malaka-jin","npc:kadrak","quest:6541","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Darn Talongrip"}}
E["npc:gaxim-rustfizzle"] = {t="npc",n="Gaxim Rustfizzle",z="stonetalon",s="At a small Alliance camp on the Webwinder Path, Gaxim Rustfizzle seeks to win over Stonetalon’s night elves. The ambitious gnome scholar and tinker represents the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, and aims to prove that artifice and alchemy can preserve their woodland realm. He also bears a fierce grudge against the Venture Company’s destructive operations.",h="At a small Alliance camp on the Webwinder Path, Gaxim Rustfizzle seeks to win over Stonetalon’s night elves.",sec={{t="A Scientific Emissary",b="In Stonetalon’s craggy passes, Gaxim Rustfizzle brings night elves a different way to defend the wilds. He represents the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, and believes calculated mechanisms and chemical solutions can defend and restore Kalimdor’s wilderness as well as prayers to Elune. Alongside the sentinel Kaela Shadowspear, he camps on the Webwinder Path and works to convince his tall, reclusive allies that engineering can serve the living forest.",sp=0},{t="Sabotaging the Saws",b="The Venture Company’s clear-cutting and industrial greed scar nearby Windshear Crag, drawing much of Gaxim’s effort. He believes their crude goblin machinery deserves neither respect nor mercy, and coordinates covert operations and volatile chemical sabotage against their logging operations. Crippling the shredders and stealing their schematics are operations he coordinates, meant to show that gnomish intellect can defeat careless corporate plunder.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is a gnome scholar and inventor at an Alliance lookout on the Webwinder Path in the Stonetalon Mountains. He represents the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences.",al={"who is gaxim","gaxim rustfizzle lore","gnome in stonetalon"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences?",a="The Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences is a gnomish academic society that blends arcane magic, alchemical mixtures and mechanical engineering. Gaxim represents its ideals abroad in Kalimdor.",al={"enlightened assembly","gaxim faction","gaxim group"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Gaxim working with the night elves?",a="Gaxim wants to show the night elves that gnomish science and alchemy can protect and heal woodlands. He offers a modern Alliance answer to forest conservation alongside traditional druidism.",al={"why is gaxim here","gaxim night elves","gaxim purpose"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Gaxim hate the Venture Company?",a="Gaxim hates the Venture Company for ruthlessly clear-cutting Windshear Crag with crude machines and toxic pollution. He despises their reckless exploitation and turns volatile chemicals and sabotage against their operations.",al={"gaxim venture co","gaxim vs venture company","why fight venture co"},it="wants"},{q="Who is camped with Gaxim on Webwinder Path?",a="Gaxim shares his small outpost on Webwinder Path with Kaela Shadowspear, a night elf sentinel watching the trails into Windshear Crag.",al={"gaxim companion","who is with gaxim","gaxim and kaela"}},{q="Where can Gaxim Rustfizzle be found?",a="Gaxim is at a modest Alliance camp on the Webwinder Path, just southwest of Windshear Crag’s industrial logging pits in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"gaxim location","where is gaxim","gaxim rustfizzle map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Gaxim Rustfizzle on?",a="Gaxim is loyal to the Alliance and works directly alongside the night elves in Stonetalon. Representing the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, he acts as an emissary of gnomish ingenuity, aiming to prove to skeptical kaldorei allies that combining arcane lore, chemical mixtures, and mechanical craft can preserve nature rather than destroy it.",al={"gaxim rustfizzle faction","is gaxim alliance","who does gaxim work for"},it="side",add="d5f6878f"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Gaxim carries gnomish academic pride into Kalimdor, showing its ancient cultures that gears and reagents can save a forest as well as nature magic.",["race:NightElf"]="Gaxim is a steadfast ally, actively defending the Ashenvale and Stonetalon borders from goblin industry.",["profession:Engineering"]="Gaxim applies engineering in the field, designing covert operations and tactical devices specifically tuned to disrupt crude Venture Company machinery.",["faction:Alliance"]="On the perilous Webwinder Path, Gaxim provides scouting, intelligence and sabotage missions to check aggressive industrial incursions in Stonetalon."},kw={"assembly","gaxim","gnome","kaela","rustfizzle","stonetalon","venture company","webwinder","windshear"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","subzone:webwinder-path","subzone:windshear-crag","npc:kaela-shadowspear","topic:venture-company","quest:1073","quest:1079","quest:1080"},src={"Gaxim Rustfizzle"}}
E["npc:grunt-logmar"] = {t="npc",n="Grunt Logmar",z="stonetalon",s="At Camp Taurajo, Grunt Logmar watches the southern Barrens frontier for the Horde. He tracks threats near the camp and seeks aid for missing scouts.",h="At Camp Taurajo, Grunt Logmar watches the southern Barrens frontier for the Horde.",sec={{t="Duty at Camp Taurajo",b="At Camp Taurajo, Grunt Logmar guards the Horde's southern Barrens frontier. The camp lies among the tauren, near hostile quilboar grounds and the mountain passes into Stonetalon and Mulgore. Logmar keeps watch over these dangers and coordinates scouting reports. When his comrades are ambushed or captured by local hostiles, he calls on capable Horde travelers to help find and aid them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grunt Logmar?",a="Grunt Logmar is an orc soldier at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. He guards the settlement for the Horde and oversees rescue and scouting efforts.",al={"grunt logmar","who is logmar","logmar barrens"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Grunt Logmar be found?",a="You can find Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo, in the southern Barrens along the road toward the Great Lift and Thousand Needles.",al={"where is logmar","logmar location","find grunt logmar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What matters does Logmar oversee?",a="Logmar oversees the safety of missing Horde scouts. He sends travelers to investigate the disappearance and captivity of fellow grunt Dogran and recover vital supplies such as Ken'zigla's draught.",al={"logmar quests","what does logmar want","dogran rescue"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Grunt Logmar on?",a="Grunt Logmar is a loyal soldier of the Horde. Stationed out among the tauren settlements, he serves the Warchief by keeping watch over the southern frontiers and supporting Horde operations across the plains.",al={"is logmar horde","grunt logmar faction","grunt logmar side"},it="side",add="ce116068"},{q="Why is Grunt Logmar here?",a="Logmar is stationed as a vanguard guard to bolster defense and maintain military communication. The surrounding wilderness poses constant threats from hostile wildlife, centaur marauders, and nearby quilboar, requiring steadfast soldiers to safeguard travelers and secure the southern Barrens.",al={"why is grunt logmar here","why is logmar in taurajo","logmar post"},it="why_here",add="1f3f5c49"},{q="What does Grunt Logmar want?",a="Logmar seeks aid in resolving pressing military emergencies in the region, particularly the rescue and recovery of captured comrades such as Dogran, and securing restorative draughts needed to sustain his fellow fighters in the field.",al={"what does logmar want","grunt logmar goal","what does grunt logmar need"},it="wants",add="e7dd0701"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Logmar is a frontline Horde soldier supporting the tauren in the Barrens. He relies on Horde champions to aid fallen and captured scouts.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc grunt stationed far from Orgrimmar, you stand alongside the Horde's tauren allies."},kw={"camp taurajo","dogran","grunt logmar","ken'zigla's draught","orc grunt","taurajo","the barrens"},rel={"subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:barrens","quest:1515","quest:1511","zone:stonetalon","topic:alliance"},src={"Grunt Logmar"}}
E["npc:kaela-shadowspear"] = {t="npc",n="Kaela Shadowspear",z="stonetalon",s="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Kaela Shadowspear watches the wilderness southwest of Windshear Crag. She coordinates with fellow sentinels as tensions rise and the land suffers new disruptions. Travelers help scout dangerous ground and learn what has corrupted the ancient defenders.",h="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Kaela Shadowspear watches the wilderness southwest of Windshear Crag.",sec={{t="A Scout on the Frontier",b="Kaela Shadowspear watches the passes southwest of Windshear Crag. The Horde presses into the Stonetalon Mountains, while goblin operations exploit the land's natural bounty. Working beside the gnome Gaxim Rustfizzle, Kaela tracks threats pushing deeper into night elf ancestral territory.",sp=0},{t="Healing the Land",b="Violence against nature has stirred the elementals and harmed the forest's ancient guardians. Kaela sends travelers against the raging spirits and seeks the cause of the corruption afflicting the wounded treants who once guarded the Vale. She works to restore peace before the land is scarred beyond repair.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kaela Shadowspear?",a="Kaela Shadowspear is a night elf sentinel at a frontier camp southwest of Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. She oversees scouting and helps protect local wildlife and spirits.",al={"who is kaela","kaela shadowspear identity","kaela npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Kaela Shadowspear be found?",a="Kaela is in a small Alliance camp southwest of Windshear Crag, along the road through the Stonetalon Mountains. The gnome engineer Gaxim Rustfizzle shares the camp.",al={"kaela shadowspear location","where is kaela","kaela stonetalon camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who does Kaela report to?",a="Kaela coordinates with Sentinel Thenysil, exchanging intelligence on enemy movements and local threats across Stonetalon.",al={"kaela reports to who","kaela thenysil","kaela's commander"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Kaela concerned about the elementals?",a="The Venture Co. set the Charred Vale aflame and tore at it with machines, releasing spirits of flame, stone, and rage. Kaela wants their numbers reduced so the land can recover.",al={"enraged spirits quest","why are spirits angry","kaela elemental spirits"},it="threat"},{q="What is happening to the ancients near Windshear Crag?",a="The treants who protect the Charred Vale helped drive back the Venture Co., but they have since become corrupt. Gaxim suspects the goblins' weapons are to blame, so Kaela asks travelers to bring him a piece of corroded shrapnel from a wounded treant to study.",al={"wounded ancients quest","kaela ancients","stonetalon wounded ancients"},it="danger"},{q="Why is a gnome stationed with Kaela?",a="Kaela shares her camp with Gaxim Rustfizzle, an Alliance gnome. She tends to the wilderness's spiritual and tactical balance, while Gaxim works against the hostile goblin machinery and operations nearby.",al={"gaxim rustfizzle kaela","why is gaxim with kaela","gnome and night elf camp"},it="allies"},{q="Whose side is Kaela Shadowspear on?",a="Kaela stands firmly with the night elves and the Alliance. Stationed in Stonetalon, she serves Darnassus and sentinel command, coordinating closely with fellow Alliance scouts to defend the land against encroaching adversaries.",al={"kaela shadowspear faction","is kaela alliance","kaela shadowspear allegiance"},it="side",add="e879ebe3"},{q="What does Kaela Shadowspear want?",a="Kaela aims to protect the Stonetalon Mountains from devastation. She seeks to thin out the enraged elemental spirits the Venture Co. unleashed, learn what has corrupted the wounded ancients of the Charred Vale, and keep her commanders informed of regional threats.",al={"kaela shadowspear goal","what does kaela want","kaela objectives"},it="wants",add="6c46a0c6"},{q="Why is Kaela Shadowspear here?",a="Kaela is deployed southwest of Windshear Crag as a sentinel scout. From this outpost, she monitors disturbances across Stonetalon, particularly the plight of the corrupted local spirits and the distress of the nearby ancients.",al={"why is kaela shadowspear in stonetalon","kaela shadowspear mission","why is kaela here"},it="why_here",add="bb8cec73"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can bring Kaela intelligence from the contested reaches of Stonetalon and help coordinate it between distant outposts.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the need to defend sacred ground. Kaela works to soothe outraged spirits and protect Kalimdor's revered ancients.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can help Kaela uncover what corrupted the Vale's ancients and ease the pain of its disturbed nature spirits."},kw={"ancients","kaela","rustfizzle","sentinel","shadowspear","spirits","stonetalon","thenysil","windshear"},rel={"subzone:windshear-crag","npc:sentinel-thenysil","npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","quest:1084","quest:1083","quest:1091","quest:1082","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Kaela Shadowspear"}}
E["npc:keeper-albagorm"] = {t="npc",n="Keeper Albagorm",z="stonetalon",s="At Stonetalon Peak, Keeper Albagorm watches the Charred Vale burn and seeks help healing the wilds.",h="At Stonetalon Peak, Keeper Albagorm watches the Charred Vale burn and seeks help healing the wilds.",sec={{t="A Guardian on the Peak",b="Keeper Albagorm guards the night elven refuge at Stonetalon Peak. Like other sons of Cenarius, he feels the pain of the natural world. South of the peak, the Charred Vale lies scorched by a greedy mechanized army of industrialists. Bloodfury harpies now hold the ruins and prevent new growth. From his sanctuary, Albagorm works to halt the corruption and restore balance to the wounded forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Keeper Albagorm?",a="Keeper Albagorm is a keeper of the grove, one of Cenarius's demigod offspring, stationed at Stonetalon Peak in the Stonetalon Mountains. He allies with the night elves and Kalimdor's natural guardians.",al={"keeper albagorm","who is albagorm","albagorm stonetalon"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Keeper Albagorm?",a="You can find Keeper Albagorm at Stonetalon Peak, an Alliance-aligned druidic refuge high in the northwestern Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"keeper albagorm location","where is albagorm","albagorm coords"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Keeper Albagorm want help with?",a="Albagorm wants help healing the Charred Vale. He sends travelers into the ash-choked basin to cleanse the blighted land and drive out the Bloodfury harpies that prevent natural regrowth.",al={"keeper albagorm quests","what does albagorm want","reclaiming the charred vale"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Keeper Albagorm on?",a="Keeper Albagorm is aligned with the night elves and the Cenarion druids of Stonetalon Peak, offering his counsel and guidance to champions of the Alliance. Like all sons of Cenarius, his deeper loyalty lies with the balance of nature, seeking out allies who are willing to aid in healing Kalimdor's scarred landscapes.",al={"keeper albagorm faction","albagorm alliance or horde","is albagorm friendly"},it="side",add="23205c35"},{q="Why is Keeper Albagorm here at Stonetalon Peak?",a="Keeper Albagorm watches over the sanctuary of Stonetalon Peak, a vital bastion of nature tucked high in the mountains. From this haven, he observes the corruption and destruction spreading across the region, directing trustworthy travelers to push back the blight and mend the devastation threatening the Charred Vale nearby.",al={"why is albagorm at stonetalon peak","albagorm purpose stonetalon","keeper albagorm role"},it="why_here",add="28024e4a"},{q="Who is Keeper Albagorm tied to?",a="As a keeper of the grove, Albagorm is one of the revered sons of Cenarius, linking him by sacred bloodline directly to the Demigod of the Moon and the natural order. In Stonetalon, he stands closely alongside the local night elven sentinels and Cenarion protectors stationed at the mountain's peak.",al={"keeper albagorm ties","albagorm connections","who does albagorm answer to"},it="ties",add="7aa8d5e1"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share the Cenarion lineage with Albagorm, and his effort to cleanse the Charred Vale touches that bond.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can find shelter and guidance from Albagorm while traveling through the night elven refuge at Stonetalon Peak."},kw={"cenarius","charred vale","keeper albagorm","keeper of the grove","stonetalon","stonetalon peak"},rel={"subzone:stonetalon-peak","quest:1057","subzone:charred-vale","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Keeper Albagorm"}}
E["npc:maggran-earthbinder"] = {t="npc",n="Maggran Earthbinder",z="stonetalon",s="At Sun Rock Retreat, Maggran Earthbinder guards a Horde camp in the Stonetalon Mountains. Cairne Bloodhoof sent the battle-worn tauren to lead its defense against beasts and harpies.",h="At Sun Rock Retreat, Maggran Earthbinder guards a Horde camp in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Veteran's Haven",b="High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof sent Maggran Earthbinder to the Stonetalon Mountains to lead Sun Rock Retreat. Countless skirmishes and bloody campaigns have hardened his heart, stripping away the gentleness natural to his people. The outpost was also meant to offer him respite, where warm winds and mountain sunshine might ease his battle-worn spirit.",sp=0},{t="Threats in the Crags",b="Peace remains scarce in Stonetalon. From Sun Rock Retreat, Maggran coordinates defenses against Bloodfury harpies nesting in the peaks and gathers fighters to face predators across the crags. He once survived an ambush by the giant spider Besseleth, and knows how deadly the wilderness can be. He often enlists travelers to kill regional predators before they overrun the outpost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Maggran Earthbinder?",a="Maggran Earthbinder commands the tauren at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. Cairne Bloodhoof stationed him there after countless battles to guard the settlement and secure its supply roads and borders.",al={"maggran","who is maggran","sun rock retreat leader"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Maggran sent to Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Cairne Bloodhoof appointed Maggran to lead Sun Rock Retreat for his seasoned military leadership and to give him a place of respite. A lifetime of combat has worn him down, and the quiet mountain sun offers some healing.",al={"why is maggran here","maggran background","cairne and maggran"},it="why_here"},{q="What threats does Maggran ask adventurers to deal with?",a="Maggran directs defenses against Bloodfury harpies in the mountains and sends fighters after dangerous regional predators. The giant spider Besseleth is among them, after Maggran narrowly survived an ambush by her.",al={"maggran quests","what does maggran want","harpies stonetalon"},it="wants"},{q="What happened between Maggran and Besseleth?",a="Maggran survived an ambush by the giant spider Besseleth. He escaped with his life and now sends capable adventurers to kill her before others fall victim to her web.",al={"maggran besseleth","spider quest maggran","arachnophobia lore"},it="history"},{q="Does Maggran have a role in Thunder Bluff?",a="Maggran answers to Cairne Bloodhoof, Thunder Bluff's High Chieftain. Though stationed at Sun Rock Retreat, his authority and orders come from the capital.",al={"maggran thunder bluff","maggran cairne"},it="ties"},{q="Is Maggran Earthbinder friendly to Alliance players?",a="No. Maggran leads the Horde and is hostile to Alliance adventurers who enter Sun Rock Retreat.",al={"can alliance talk to maggran","maggran hostile"},it="side"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see in Maggran the toll warfare takes on the shu'halo spirit. Conflict can harden even the most grounded children of the Earth Mother.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler on Stonetalon's steep climbs, you can look to Maggran to coordinate local patrols and keep supply routes clear of beasts and harpies."},kw={"besseleth","bloodfury","cairne bloodhoof","earthbinder","harpies","maggran","stonetalon","sun rock retreat"},rel={"subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","quest:6284","quest:6282","quest:6283","quest:5881","topic:tauren","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Maggran Earthbinder"}}
E["npc:makaba-flathoof"] = {t="npc",n="Makaba Flathoof",z="stonetalon",s="At Camp Aparaje, Makaba Flathoof has lost his home to the Grimtotem clan. He seeks Horde champions to strike back and keep his family safe.",h="At Camp Aparaje, Makaba Flathoof has lost his home to the Grimtotem clan.",sec={{t="Tragedy at Camp Aparaje",b="Makaba Flathoof grieves for Camp Aparaje, his home in the Stonetalon Mountains. The Grimtotem clan struck without warning and laid the settlement low. Many tauren seek peace and unity under Cairne Bloodhoof, but the Grimtotem keep spreading discord and violence. Makaba is among the survivors left displaced and grieving.",sp=0},{t="A Plea for Vengeance",b="Makaba Flathoof calls on Horde travelers to strike back, since he cannot retake Camp Aparaje alone. He wants the Grimtotem who overran his home to face fierce retaliation for the slaughter of his kin. His chief concern is Grundig Darkcloud, the warlord responsible. Makaba believes his daughter, Kaya, was lost in the attack.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Makaba Flathoof?",a="Makaba Flathoof is a tauren survivor from Camp Aparaje in the Stonetalon Mountains. The Grimtotem clan overran his home, and he seeks help from Horde champions.",al={"makaba","who is makaba flathoof","makaba flathoof lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where did Makaba come from?",a="Makaba came from Camp Aparaje, a small tauren settlement in the Stonetalon Mountains. The Grimtotem attacked and devastated it.",al={"makaba origin","where is makaba from","camp aparaje makaba"},it="origin"},{q="Who attacked Makaba's village?",a="The Grimtotem clan sacked Camp Aparaje. Grundig Darkcloud was among the figures leading them there.",al={"who attacked camp aparaje","makaba enemies","who sacked aparaje"},it="conflict"},{q="What does Makaba want Horde adventurers to do?",a="Makaba wants Horde champions to avenge his fallen home by cutting down the Grimtotem at Camp Aparaje and eliminating their leader, Grundig Darkcloud.",al={"makaba quests","what does makaba ask for","makaba tasks"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Kaya to Makaba?",a="Kaya Flathoof is Makaba's daughter. She vanished in the attack on Camp Aparaje, and her family believes she was lost in the assault.",al={"kaya flathoof","who is kaya","makaba relative kaya"},it="ties"},{q="Is Makaba related to Dim Flathoof?",a="Makaba and Dim share the Flathoof surname, but their family relationship is unconfirmed.",al={"dim flathoof","makaba and dim","flathoof family"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Makaba Flathoof on?",a="Makaba Flathoof is a loyal member of the Horde and the tauren people. Fleeing the violence that struck his home, he seeks assistance exclusively from Horde travelers and champions to protect his kin and strike back against their attackers.",al={"makaba flathoof faction","is makaba horde","who does makaba serve"},it="side",add="586aa360"},{q="Why is Makaba Flathoof here?",a="Makaba has taken refuge in Stonetalon after tragedy struck his home at Camp Aparaje. Driven from his settlement by violent raiders, he now stays here seeking aid to avenge his fallen kin and ensure the safety of survivors like Kaya.",al={"why is makaba flathoof here","why is makaba in stonetalon","makaba flathoof purpose"},it="why_here",add="6e0e5223"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see the Grimtotem's bitter treachery in Makaba's plight. Some of your kin honor neither peace nor unity.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion, you can answer Makaba's call for aid and punish those who butcher peaceful encampments."},kw={"camp aparaje","flathoof","grimtotem","grundig darkcloud","kaya","makaba","stonetalon"},rel={"subzone:camp-aparaje","quest:6548","quest:6629","quest:6523","quest:6401","zone:stonetalon","topic:tauren"},src={"Makaba Flathoof"}}
E["npc:mor-rogal"] = {t="npc",n="Mor'rogal",z="stonetalon",s="In Sun Rock Retreat, Mor'rogal guides travelers toward the dangers and promise of the Stonetalon Mountains.",h="In Sun Rock Retreat, Mor'rogal guides travelers toward the dangers and promise of the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Watcher in the Crags",b="Mor'rogal watches the deep crevices and caverns of the Stonetalon Mountains from Sun Rock Retreat. Their twisting passages offer riches, but can also bring deadly danger. He sends brave Horde wanderers to troubled places such as Boulderslide Ravine. To Mor'rogal, facing those depths tests the spirit of anyone who seeks glory by following heart and soul.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mor'rogal?",a="Mor'rogal is a tauren guide in Sun Rock Retreat, in the Stonetalon Mountains. He urges Horde travelers to test their mettle in the dangerous caves and ravines scattered across the mountains.",al={"morrogal","who is mor'rogal","mor rogal lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Mor'rogal?",a="You can find Mor'rogal in Sun Rock Retreat, the main Horde outpost among the peaks of the central Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"mor'rogal location","where is mor'rogal","morrogal spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Mor'rogal offer?",a="Mor'rogal sends capable champions to the cave at Boulderslide Ravine, where kobolds mine Resonite crystals, then asks them to slay Goggeroc, a sleeping Earthen the kobolds dug up.",al={"mor'rogal quests","what does mor'rogal want"},sp=1,it="purpose",gp=true,bt={"q6421.2"}},{q="Why is Mor'rogal focused on caves and ravines?",a="Mor'rogal believes Stonetalon's perilous caverns offer adventure and a test of spiritual resolve, with glory and riches for those willing to risk their lives.",al={"why caves","mor'rogal caves"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Mor'rogal on?",a="Mor'rogal is aligned with the Horde and his fellow tauren. Stationed within Sun Rock Retreat, a secluded Horde outpost high in the Stonetalon Mountains, he offers guidance and assignments to adventurers who serve the Horde's interests in the region.",al={"mor'rogal faction","mor'rogal horde or alliance","mor'rogal loyalty"},it="side",add="9b06cf83"},{q="What does Mor'rogal want?",a="Mor'rogal seeks brave adventurers willing to brave the perilous caves and ravines of the Stonetalon Mountains. He directs scouts into hostile places like Boulderslide Ravine, urging bold spirits to confront the earthen dangers lurking underground in exchange for honor and riches.",al={"mor'rogal goals","what is mor'rogal doing","mor'rogal quests purpose"},it="wants",add="27de9984"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you may see the deep stone hollows of Kalimdor as sacred ground, where physical and spiritual trials can prove your worth.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde arriving at Sun Rock Retreat, you can turn to Mor'rogal for information about threats in the crags beyond the settlement."},kw={"boulderslide ravine","earthen arise","mor'rogal","morrogal","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","tauren"},rel={"subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","quest:6421","quest:6481","topic:tauren","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Mor'rogal"}}
E["npc:piznik"] = {t="npc",n="Piznik",z="stonetalon",s="Deep in Windshear Mine, Piznik watches the Venture Company at work. Once second-in-command, he was pushed aside by Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle and now plots against his former boss.",h="Deep in Windshear Mine, Piznik watches the Venture Company at work.",sec={{t="Fallen from Grace",b="Before Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle took control of Windshear Crag, Piznik ranked second across the entire operation. When Gerenzo seized authority, the Venture Company pushed Piznik aside and sent him into the depths of Windshear Mine. Piznik has not accepted the demotion quietly. Underground, he watches the mine's movements and waits for a chance to take revenge on the boss who demoted him.",sp=0},{t="Corporate Espionage",b="Piznik's rebellion took shape through an alliance with Ziz Fizziks, another former Venture Company worker cast out by Gerenzo. From inside the mine, Piznik gathers what he can about Gerenzo's plans. He smuggled a sample of the mysterious gold-green ore Gerenzo ordered mined in bulk to Ziz. Together, they work to disrupt the Venture Company's deforestation and mining efforts, bringing setbacks to Gerenzo's leadership.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Piznik?",a="Piznik is deep inside Windshear Mine, in the tunnels carved into Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. Venture Company workers are nearby.",al={"piznik location","where is piznik","find piznik stonetalon"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Piznik's grudge against Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle?",a="Piznik once ranked second across the Windshear Crag operation. When Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle took command of the logging and mining project, he demoted Piznik, who now resents him and wants to see him ruined.",al={"why does piznik hate gerenzo","piznik gerenzo feud"},it="conflict"},{q="How does Piznik fit into Ziz Fizziks' plans?",a="Ziz Fizziks was fired by Gerenzo, while Piznik was demoted. Piznik uses his access inside Windshear Mine to learn of Gerenzo's plans and get a sample of the mysterious ore to Ziz.",al={"piznik and ziz","who does piznik work with"},it="ties"},{q="Is Piznik still loyal to the Venture Company?",a="Piznik remains a Venture Company employee so he can stay inside the mine. He acts for his own interests and wants to sabotage Gerenzo.",al={"is piznik venture co","piznik faction"},it="side"},{q="Who is Piznik?",a="Piznik is a goblin operative hiding deep inside Windshear Mine within the Stonetalon Mountains. He was once the second-in-command of the entire Venture Company operation across Windshear Crag, enjoying considerable status and influence until Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle arrived, took control, and systematically stripped him of his position.",al={"who is piznik","piznik lore","piznik background"},it="identity",add="73f53239"},{q="What does Piznik want?",a="Piznik wants payback against Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle for ruining his standing in the Venture Company, and a payday. At the request of his old boss Ziz Fizziks, whom Gerenzo fired, he stays in the mine to learn Gerenzo's plans, and he slips out a sample of the gold-green ore Gerenzo has ordered mined in bulk so Ziz's new employer can study it.",al={"what does piznik want","piznik goal","piznik motive"},it="wants",add="04ccaf91"},{q="Why is Piznik in Windshear Mine?",a="When Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle seized control of the Venture Company's local enterprise, he sent Piznik down to work in Windshear Mine. Piznik stays in the tunnels at Ziz Fizziks' request, acting as an internal informant and quietly collecting intelligence without alerting the rest of the operation.",al={"why is piznik here","why is piznik in windshear mine","piznik location reason"},it="why_here",add="e9de2964"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you may cross paths with Piznik inside Windshear Mine, where he watches the company that demoted him."},kw={"gerenzo wrenchwhistle","piznik","stonetalon","venture co","windshear crag","windshear mine","ziz fizziks"},rel={"quest:1090","quest:1096","quest:1483","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","topic:goblin"},src={"Piznik"}}
E["npc:sentinel-thenysil"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Thenysil",z="stonetalon",s="In Astranaar, Sentinel Tara Thenysil watches Ashenvale and the southern road into Stonetalon. She tracks military movements and keeps scouts watching neighboring lands, with special attention on allied forces moving south.",h="In Astranaar, Sentinel Tara Thenysil watches Ashenvale and the southern road into Stonetalon.",sec={{t="Watching the Borders",b="At her post in Astranaar, Sentinel Thenysil helps guard Ashenvale as hostility grows. Night elf lands across the region face steady encroachment, so outposts must stay in contact. While much of the garrison defends the forest road, Thenysil sends Alliance volunteers beyond Ashenvale to support distant allies.",sp=0},{t="Ties to Stonetalon",b="Sentinel Thenysil shares a close friendship and military bond with Kaela Shadowspear, an operative sent south into the Stonetalon Mountains. When she learns Kaela was sent with an eccentric gnome mage, Thenysil takes the strange pairing as a sign of serious trouble in the peaks. Concerned for her comrade, she sends capable travelers south with support and asks them to report on the mission.",sp=0},{t="Audience in the Canopy",b="Scouts return from Stonetalon with word that their strikes have driven back the Venture Company’s defiling operations. Sentinel Thenysil knows that halting the company’s mechanized exploitation protects the neighboring wilds as well. She commends the heroes and sends them to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, where High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind will receive them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can Sentinel Thenysil be found?",a="Sentinel Thenysil is stationed in Astranaar, the main night elf stronghold along Ashenvale’s central road.",al={"thenysil location","where is sentinel thenysil","thenysil astranaar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Thenysil send travelers to Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Thenysil sends travelers south because her friend Kaela Shadowspear was deployed to Stonetalon with a gnome mage. She sees the unusual pairing as a sign of danger and sends dependable travelers to support Kaela’s mission.",al={"why stonetalon","thenysil quest stonetalon","on guard in stonetalon why"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Kaela Shadowspear?",a="Kaela Shadowspear is a night elf scout and close friend of Sentinel Thenysil. She is stationed in Stonetalon, investigating threats to the land.",al={"who is kaela","kaela shadowspear relation","thenysil friend"},it="ties"},{q="What threats are being fought in Stonetalon?",a="The Venture Company has established invasive, destructive industrial operations in Stonetalon, strip-mining and clearing the forests.",al={"stonetalon threat","what is happening in stonetalon","venture co stonetalon"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Thenysil send adventurers to Tyrande Whisperwind?",a="After travelers help Kaela Shadowspear halt the Venture Company’s schemes, Thenysil sends them to Darnassus. High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind will personally acknowledge their service to the night elves.",al={"reception from tyrande","why see tyrande","thenysil darnassus referral"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="What is Sentinel Thenysil's role in Astranaar?",a="Thenysil watches regional intelligence and the borders from Astranaar, and sends reliable Alliance recruits to support distant garrisons.",al={"thenysil rank","what does thenysil do","sentinel thenysil duties"},it="identity"},{q="Whose side is Sentinel Thenysil on?",a="Sentinel Thenysil is dedicated to the night elves and the Alliance. As an active soldier in the Sentinels based in Astranaar, she guards the borders of Ashenvale and coordinates support for night elf outposts and operations across Kalimdor.",al={"sentinel thenysil faction","who does thenysil serve","is thenysil alliance"},it="side",add="cd8ae8e6"},{q="Why is Sentinel Thenysil in Astranaar?",a="Astranaar is the primary night elf hub in Ashenvale, serving as a frontline command post for defending the forest. Sentinel Thenysil is stationed there to help maintain vigil over the region, watch trade routes, and recruit capable travelers when neighboring lands require urgent reinforcement.",al={"why is thenysil in astranaar","thenysil post ashenvale","why is sentinel thenysil here"},it="why_here",add="ad790eb1"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see in Thenysil the Sentinels’ steady watch over Kalimdor’s sacred groves and their care for allied operatives across the borders.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you may find in Thenysil a link between Ashenvale and Stonetalon, with a chance to earn favor with Darnassus’s leaders.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may find Thenysil’s alarm at a gnome mage’s deployment to Stonetalon a reminder that your kind can still surprise the night elves."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","kaela shadowspear","sentinels","stonetalon","tara thenysil","thenysil","tyrande whisperwind"},rel={"subzone:astranaar","npc:kaela-shadowspear","quest:1070","quest:1082","quest:1081","zone:ashenvale","zone:stonetalon","npc:tyrande-whisperwind"},src={"Sentinel Thenysil"}}
E["npc:tammra-windfield"] = {t="npc",n="Tammra Windfield",z="stonetalon",s="At Sun Rock Retreat, Tammra Windfield guides Horde travelers in honoring the land's renewal. The tauren watches over the wilderness and the safety of her kin in the Stonetalon Mountains.",h="At Sun Rock Retreat, Tammra Windfield guides Horde travelers in honoring the land's renewal.",sec={{t="A Warden of Sun Rock",b="Sun Rock Retreat shelters the Horde among the crags of Stonetalon. Harpies, Venture Company loggers, and predators threaten the settlement. Tammra Windfield watches over the mountain wilderness and the travelers who enter. Her gentle manner carries the resolve needed to keep a home safe in such rugged country.",sp=0},{t="Nurturing the Land",b="Tammra honors the Earth Mother by watching nature's steady rhythm of growth and decay. She asks travelers to tend the cycle of rebirth and bring forth new life, working against the harm conflict and exploitation cause in Stonetalon. For Tammra, protecting the land means healing it so life can flourish in scarred mountain soil.",sp=0},{t="Kinship and Vigilance",b="Tammra's concern reaches beyond the wilds to the companions and kin who travel Stonetalon's dangerous trails. When word comes that travelers or family have vanished among the crags, she is among the first to seek reliable aid. Sun Rock Retreat endures through loyalty and mutual protection, as well as harmony with nature.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tammra Windfield?",a="Tammra Windfield is a tauren at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. She cares for the settlement, the mountain landscape's natural cycles, and the safety of her fellow travelers.",al={"who is tammra","tammra windfield","sun rock retreat tammra"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Tammra Windfield?",a="Find Tammra inside Sun Rock Retreat, the Horde encampment in the western heights of the Stonetalon Mountains. A mountain trail branches off the main valley road and leads there.",al={"tammra windfield location","where is tammra","find tammra windfield"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Tammra offer?",a="Tammra asks travelers to help with renewal and the welfare of her kin, including Cycle of Rebirth, New Life, and Kaya's Alive, where travelers report on kin's survival.",al={"tammra quests","tammra windfield quest list"},gp=true},{q="What is Tammra's role in Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Tammra cares for the community and its spiritual life at Sun Rock Retreat. She directs travelers to restore the surrounding wilderness and protect the bonds that keep the outpost safe.",al={"what does tammra do","tammra role"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Tammra care about the natural cycle?",a="Tauren believe balance depends on nurturing the Earth Mother's cycles of death and regeneration. With outside forces and mountain beasts threatening the region, Tammra seeks new life to heal the wounded wilderness.",al={"cycle of rebirth lore","why rebirth stonetalon"},it="wants"},{q="Is Tammra friendly to Alliance players?",a="No. Sun Rock Retreat is a Horde outpost, and Tammra is aligned with Thunder Bluff and the Horde. She is hostile to Alliance intruders.",al={"is tammra hostile","can alliance talk to tammra"},it="side"},{q="Why is Tammra Windfield in Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Tammra resides in Sun Rock Retreat to tend to the spirits of the land and observe the natural cycle of life in the Stonetalon Mountains. From this high sanctuary, she watches over the troubled crags and reaches out to travelers who can assist in nurturing renewal amidst the region's hardships.",al={"why is tammra here","tammra windfield sun rock retreat why","why is tammra in stonetalon"},it="why_here",add="590ef84e"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see Tammra's devotion to the Earth Mother in her work to restore the land, even far from Mulgore.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you will recognize how Tammra's care for rebirth and new life echoes the heart of druidism.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help Tammra keep Sun Rock Retreat a secure, lasting foothold for Horde travelers in contested Stonetalon."},kw={"cycle of rebirth","kaya","new life","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","tammra","tauren","windfield"},rel={"subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","quest:6301","quest:6381","quest:6401","topic:tauren","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Tammra Windfield"}}
E["npc:witch-doctor-jin-zil"] = {t="npc",n="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil",z="stonetalon",s="In Malaka'jin, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil turns dark voodoo against the Horde's enemies. The Darkspear troll mystic lives in a cave in the southern Stonetalon Mountains and is a longtime comrade of Darsok Swiftdagger and the shadow hunter Rokhan.",h="In Malaka'jin, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil turns dark voodoo against the Horde's enemies.",sec={{t="The Hermit of Malaka'jin",b="In a cave east of Malaka'jin, Jin'Zil practices the ancient arts of jungle trolls, far from his tribe's coastal home. Bubbling cauldrons and captive prisoners fill his cavern. He gathers exotic reagents from the Stonetalon crags, weaving blessings and curses to defend the Horde's mountain camp.",sp=0},{t="A Trusted Veteran",b="Jin'Zil is an old friend of senior Horde scouts Darsok Swiftdagger and the shadow hunter Rokhan. Darsok leads frontline skirmishes against night elves and harpies. Jin'Zil fights the war through spirit and alchemy, using forest magic and volatile voodoo to weaken threats before they reach the camp gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Witch Doctor Jin'Zil?",a="Jin'Zil lives in a cave on the eastern side of Malaka'jin, a Horde settlement in the southern pass of the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"jin'zil location","where is jinzil","jinzil cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Jin'Zil's connection to Rokhan and Darsok Swiftdagger?",a="Jin'Zil is an old, trusted friend of Darsok Swiftdagger and the shadow hunter Rokhan. Scouts across Stonetalon rely on his magic when unusual threats arise.",al={"jin'zil friends","darsok and jinzil","rokhan connection"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Jin'Zil have prisoners in his cave?",a="Jin'Zil keeps captive enemies caged in his cavern workshop. He uses captives and raw reagents to test curses, divine portents, and craft defensive voodoo for the settlement.",al={"prisoners of jinzil","jinzil cages","why does jinzil have captives"},it="motive"},{q="What kind of tasks does he give to Horde adventurers?",a="He sends travelers across Stonetalon to gather mystical components for his forest magic and voodoo rituals.",al={"jinzil quests","what does jinzil want"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Witch Doctor Jin'Zil?",a="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is a Darkspear jungle troll mystic residing in the craggy hills of Stonetalon Mountains. Lurking in a shadowed cave overlooking the settlement of Malaka'jin, he practices deep voodoo rituals and brews potent forest magic, lending his ancient craft and spiritual foresight to the Horde's frontier struggles.",al={"who is jinzil","jin'zil lore","witch doctor jinzil identity"},it="identity",add="3fda7979"},{q="Whose side is Witch Doctor Jin'Zil on?",a="Jin'Zil stands firmly with the Horde, specifically maintaining deep ties to his Darkspear troll brethren and their allies carving out footholds in Kalimdor. He directs his magical rites and strategic aid toward supporting local outposts, aiding champions sent across the mountain paths on behalf of the Warchief.",al={"is jinzil horde","witch doctor jinzil faction","jinzil loyalty"},it="side",add="088a369a"},{q="What does Witch Doctor Jin'Zil want?",a="Jin'Zil seeks potent reagents from Stonetalon's wildlife and magical phenomena, including beast components, to fuel his voodoo charms and hexes. Through these brewed blessings, he aims to empower the Horde's presence and secure the mountain passes against encroaching threats.",al={"what does jinzil want","jinzil goals","why gather ingredients jinzil"},it="wants",add="6d312970"},{q="Why is Witch Doctor Jin'Zil in Stonetalon?",a="He has established his secluded den at Malaka'jin to observe the volatile spirits and raw natural magic of the Stonetalon Mountains. From this rocky outpost, he weaves spells and monitors southern paths, providing supernatural insight and enchanted aid directly to Horde scouts defending the region.",al={"why is jinzil in stonetalon","why malakajin jinzil","why is jinzil here"},it="why_here",add="5da55a71"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you see Jin'Zil carry Darkspear witch doctor practices into Kalimdor's rugged wilderness. He has deep ties to prominent figures such as Rokhan.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can rely on Jin'Zil for occult defense and intelligence support alongside the outpost's scouts as the Horde secures Stonetalon's southern paths."},kw={"darsok","jin'zil","jinzil","malaka'jin","rokhan","stonetalon","voodoo","witch doctor"},rel={"subzone:malaka-jin","npc:darsok-swiftdagger","quest:1058","quest:1060","zone:stonetalon","topic:troll"},src={"Witch Doctor Jin'Zil"}}
E["quest:1057"] = {t="quest",n="Reclaiming the Charred Vale",z="stonetalon",s="At Stonetalon Peak, Keeper Albagorm sends Alliance fighters to clear the Bloodfury harpies from the ruined Charred Vale. Their removal will open a path for druids and caretakers to begin healing the scorched land.",h="At Stonetalon Peak, Keeper Albagorm sends Alliance fighters to clear the Bloodfury harpies from the ruined...",sec={{t="The Wounded Valley",b="South of Stonetalon Peak, the Charred Vale lies in ash and smoldering ruins where a lush alpine haven once stood. A mechanized logging and mining army swept through the sacred crags, stripping trees and setting uncontrolled fires. For the guardians around Stonetalon, ancient woodland lost to industrial greed is a wound they cannot ignore.",sp=0},{t="The Harpy Menace",b="Bloodfury harpies took hold in the ashes left by the mechanical fires. Opportunistic and vicious, they swarm the smoking lowlands, nest there, and aggressively ambush anyone who approaches the valley. Keeper Albagorm and his allies cannot walk the soil to sow seeds of renewal; the harpies violently bar passage to every outsider.",sp=0},{t="Clearing the Path to Renewal",b="Restoration cannot begin until the Bloodfury roosts are broken. Albagorm sends seasoned Alliance fighters deep among the tribe to slay its hunters, ambushers, and roguefeathers. Thinning their predatory flock is the first step toward reclaiming the land for nature and giving the forest spirits room to breathe once more.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Charred Vale?",a="The Charred Vale lies in the southwestern heights of the Stonetalon Mountains. Fire consumed the once-lush forest and scorched it to bedrock as industrial logging forces exploited the land without restraint.",al={"charred vale lore","what happened to charred vale","why is it burned"},it="place"},{q="Who is Keeper Albagorm?",a="Keeper Albagorm is a woodland keeper and caretaker at the Alliance settlement on Stonetalon Peak. He protects nature and forest spirits, works to curb desolation in the mountains, and drives back encroaching beasts.",al={"keeper albagorm","who gives reclaiming the charred vale","albagorm lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why are harpies living in the Charred Vale?",a="Bloodfury harpies thrive in disrupted, blighted lands. After fire leveled the valley, the opportunistic flock moved into the basin and attacks anyone who tries to enter.",al={"bloodfury harpies","why harpies here","bloodfuries in stonetalon"},it="target"},{q="Who set fire to the Charred Vale in the first place?",a="Keeper Albagorm names a greedy mechanized army of industrialists as the cause. Their unchecked logging machinery and explosive expansion brought devastating blazes that consumed the woodland.",al={"who burned charred vale","mechanized army industrialists","venture company charred vale"},it="history"},{q="What must be done after thinning the harpies?",a="Once the Bloodfury numbers are curbed, Keeper Albagorm turns to planting seeds and channeling restorative magic to coax new life from the scorched soil.",al={"next quest charred vale","reclaiming the charred vale part 2","what happens next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest available to Horde adventurers?",a="No. Keeper Albagorm works from the Alliance redoubt atop Stonetalon Peak, so Alliance heroes alone can clear the Bloodfury harpies for him.",al={"can horde do this quest","horde reclaiming charred vale"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Why does Keeper Albagorm want the Bloodfuries culled?",a="As a keeper of the grove and protector of forest spirits, Albagorm seeks to heal and restore the scarred, burnt landscape of the Charred Vale to the lush sanctuary it once was. However, the aggressive Bloodfury harpies who swarmed the ruins vigorously block any entry, actively preventing the Cenarion Circle from initiating their sacred rites of renewal and regrowth.",al={"why clear the charred vale","keeper albagorm motive","why kill the harpies charred vale"},it="motive",add="d7987d6f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you revere Stonetalon's wild forests. Driving vile harpies from sacred groves defiled by foreign engines is an urgent calling.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you serve the Cenarion circle and defend nature's harmony. You help the Keepers clear blighted nests so magical reforestation can begin.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you help secure the high passes and southern valleys, protecting vulnerable night elf settlements and sanctuaries across Stonetalon Peak from predatory threats."},kw={"bloodfury","charred vale","harpies","keeper albagorm","reclaiming the charred vale","stonetalon","stonetalon peak"},rel={"subzone:charred-vale","subzone:stonetalon-peak","npc:keeper-albagorm","topic:harpy","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Keeper Albagorm",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=1057},src={"Reclaiming the Charred Vale"}}
E["quest:1058"] = {t="quest",n="Jin'Zil's Forest Magic",z="stonetalon",s="At small Malaka'jin, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil holds three night elven scouts in crude iron cages. He sends Horde adventurers to Stonetalon Peak for wilderness reagents to brew a grim forest magic.",h="At small Malaka'jin, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil holds three night elven scouts in crude iron cages.",sec={{t="A Bitter Brew",b="Under the Horde's watch, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil practices his craft in Malaka'jin's red-rock defile. When three night elf captives fall into his hands, he chooses a mocking ritual made for his woodland foes instead of ordinary butchery. He sends travelers north into the peaks for thick tree sap, feline whiskers from predatory twilight runners, a shimmering fey dragon scale, and scores of eyes from the local forest coursers.",sp=0},{t="A Taste of Home",b="Jin'Zil's playful manner hides a cruel troll humor. He says the brew will help the imprisoned elves feel at home, though they have no forest to frolic in. But magical fauna and concentrated sap make a volatile, lethal venom. When Jin'Zil releases the concoction in the cave, it chokes the life from the caged captives. Their bodies perish, and their ancestral spirits dissolve into luminous wisps that float into the mountains, leaving empty cages behind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Witch Doctor Jin'Zil?",a="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is a Darkspear troll at Malaka'jin in the southern Stonetalon Mountains. He aids the Horde war effort against the night elves with troll alchemy, voodoo, and interrogation.",al={"who is jin'zil","witch doctor jin'zil","jinzil lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Jin'Zil want so many courser eyes?",a="Jin'Zil says fierce forest magic takes an abundance of eyes. Troll witch doctors use strange organic ingredients in their potions, but the absurd number also suits Jin'Zil's eccentric, vindictive nature.",al={"why courser eyes","30 courser eyes","why so many eyes"},it="item"},{q="What happens to the caged night elves when the quest finishes?",a="After you bring the reagents, Jin'Zil releases toxic brew through his cave. It poisons the three captives, killing them, and their spirits drift away as wisps.",al={"what happens to the elves","caged elves fate","prisoners of jin'zil"},sp=1},{q="Where are all these reagents found?",a="You can gather courser eyes and Stonetalon sap around Mirkfallon Lake and the northern highlands. Twilight whiskers and the rare fey dragon scale come from farther north, near Stonetalon Peak, where magical beasts roam.",al={"where to find forest magic reagents","stonetalon sap location","fey dragon scale spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde fighting night elves in Stonetalon?",a="Horde logging in neighboring Ashenvale has drawn fierce resistance from the Sentinels. The night elves still hold Stonetalon Peak and its sacred groves above Horde outposts such as Malaka'jin.",al={"why fight night elves in stonetalon","horde night elf conflict stonetalon","stonetalon war"},it="conflict"},{q="Why do the dying elves turn into wisps?",a="Wisps are the spirits of dead night elves, bound closely to nature. When they die, their souls take a glowing, arboreal form instead of lingering as ordinary ghosts or shades.",al={"why do elves become wisps","elven wisps in cave","wisp lore"}},{q="Why does Witch Doctor Jin'Zil want this done?",a="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil has captured three night elf sentinels and locked them in cages within his cavern at Malaka'jin. Rather than simply executing them, he wants to concoct a spiteful brew mockingly termed \"forest magic.\" By combining raw, potent essences from their beloved wilderness, he intends to create a lethal poison that turns the forest's own natural gifts against his prisoners.",al={"jinzil forest magic why","why make forest magic","jin'zil motive"},sp=1,it="motive",add="58b555cd"},{q="What is the Stonetalon Sap for?",a="Taken from the living wood and sap beasts of the region, the thick resin serves as a viscous, sticky base for Jin'Zil's concoction. It traps and blends the other woodland reagents together, grounding his toxic brew in the raw essence of the mountains.",al={"stonetalon sap use","why collect sap","what is the sap for"},it="item",add="840e6ff0"},{q="What is the Fey Dragon Scale for?",a="Fey dragons are mystical creatures deeply intertwined with the emerald power of Stonetalon Peak and the Kaldorei. Jin'Zil requires a scale to infuse his brew with their innate magical warding and wild energies, warping it into a lethal agent specifically tuned to harm night elves.",al={"fey dragon scale use","why need fey dragon scale","what is the fey dragon scale for"},it="item",add="70cbdf3f"},{q="What is the Twilight Whisker for?",a="Harvested from the prowling twilight runners lurking in the woods, these whiskers contribute the feral, predatory instinct of Stonetalon's native predators into the mixture, sharpening the brew into an aggressive poison.",al={"twilight whisker use","why twilight whiskers","what are twilight whiskers for"},it="item",add="a0fa7c69"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you know Jin'Zil's grim humor and practical voodoo alchemy as hallmarks of Darkspear witch doctor craft.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the execution of captives with twisted woodland materials as one of the Horde's crueler acts in Stonetalon.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see majestic fey drakes, coursers, and ancient forest sap harvested for lethal poison, a grim perversion of nature's balance.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know securing Malaka'jin means subduing night elf resistance across the range, even through a recluse witch doctor's unorthodox methods."},kw={"courser eye","fey dragon","forest magic","jin'zil","malaka'jin","prisoners","stonetalon","twilight runner","witch doctor"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-jin-zil","subzone:malaka-jin","subzone:stonetalon-peak","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil",level="26",faction="Horde",id=1058,ri={"Courser Eye","Fey Dragon Scale","Stonetalon Sap","Twilight Whisker"}},src={"Jin'Zil's Forest Magic"}}
E["quest:1059"] = {t="quest",n="Reclaiming the Charred Vale",z="stonetalon",s="Keeper Albagorm seeks help for the Charred Vale from far to the south. The Bloodfury harpies have been driven back for now, but the wounded land needs more than force to heal.",h="Keeper Albagorm seeks help for the Charred Vale from far to the south.",sec={{t="The Scars of the Vale",b="The Charred Vale lies beneath ash in southern Stonetalon Mountains, scarred by terrible destruction. Alliance forces under Keeper Albagorm have driven the Bloodfury harpies from their nests in the ruins, but their retreat may not last. Albagorm knows that force can only hold the harpies back. The ravaged earth must be healed before they return and take the Vale again.",sp=0},{t="A Plea to the South",b="The grove tenders need help beyond their own means to restore the scorched land. Albagorm sends you south, past the salt flats and canyons of Thousand Needles, to Thalanaar on the border of Feralas. Falfindel Waywarder waits there. The night elf druid is known for a rare gift: calling on ancient forest spirits to bring life back to dead soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Keeper Albagorm?",a="Keeper Albagorm is a keeper of the grove at Stonetalon Peak. He oversees Alliance efforts to cleanse and restore the blighted Charred Vale.",al={"who is albagorm","keeper albagorm"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Falfindel Waywarder located?",a="Falfindel Waywarder is at Thalanaar, on the western border where Thousand Needles meets Feralas.",al={"where is falfindel","falfindel waywarder location","find waywarder"},gp=true},{q="Why send for a druid all the way in Feralas?",a="Keeper Albagorm believes Falfindel can summon ancient forest spirits powerful enough to heal the deep damage in the Charred Vale.",al={"why go to feralas","why falfindel"},it="purpose"},{q="What threat resides in the Charred Vale?",a="Hostile Bloodfury harpies, fire elementals, and wild beasts live in the valley, thriving in the wake of its burning.",al={"charred vale enemies","what is attacking the vale"},it="threat"},{q="Does this quest require combat?",a="No combat is required. You carry Albagorm's message across central and southern Kalimdor.",al={"is this quest hard","combat in charred vale quest"},gp=true},{q="How do you reach Thousand Needles from Stonetalon?",a="From Stonetalon Mountains, travel east into the Barrens, then south along the Gold Road. Take the Great Lift down into Thousand Needles and continue west toward Feralas.",al={"how to get to thousand needles","travel route to feralas"},gp=true},{q="Why does Keeper Albagorm want this done?",a="Though you struck down many of the Bloodfury harpies, Keeper Albagorm knows they will quickly regroup and reclaim their hold over the Charred Vale if no lasting action is taken. The land remains ruined and vulnerable, and culling beasts alone cannot heal the scorched earth. He urgently needs the powerful forest spirits that only a druid like Falfindel Waywarder can summon to restore life to the vale before the harpies rally and undo your progress.",al={"keeper albagorm motive","why send for falfindel","why reclaim charred vale"},it="motive",add="edca7440"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share the Cenarion duty to reach beyond local garrisons and call on primal nature spirits to heal lands scarred by unnatural ruin.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you rely on Stonetalon Peak's foothold and the links between frontier outposts across Kalimdor's vast, contested reaches."},kw={"bloodfuries","charred vale","falfindel waywarder","feralas","thalanaar","keeper albagorm","stonetalon peak","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:1057","npc:keeper-albagorm","npc:falfindel-waywarder","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:thalanaar","zone:stonetalon","zone:feralas","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Keeper Albagorm",["end"]="Falfindel Waywarder",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=1059},src={"Reclaiming the Charred Vale (2)"}}
E["quest:1060"] = {t="quest",n="Letter to Jin'Zil",z="stonetalon",s="Darsok Swiftdagger sends you from the northern Barrens into Stonetalon Mountains with news for his old friend, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil. Serena Bloodfeather has fallen, and Darsok wants Jin'Zil to know.",h="Darsok Swiftdagger sends you from the northern Barrens into Stonetalon Mountains with news for his old...",sec={{t="A Message into the Mountains",b="Darsok Swiftdagger sends you into Stonetalon Mountains after Serena Bloodfeather falls. The Witchwing and Bloodfeather broods came from the rugged ridges northwest of the northern Barrens, not the scrublands. Now that you have defeated Serena, Darsok asks you to carry the news of her death to his old acquaintance, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil. Jin'Zil lives at the troll settlement of Malaka'jin, in the dangerous mountain peaks.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Bloodfury Claws",b="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil remembers an earlier campaign when he hears that Serena Bloodfeather has fallen. The shadow hunter Rokhan and the wandering Beastmaster Rexxar slew Serena's elder sister, Bloodfeather. Serena's death brings a sense of finality to the long feud between the Horde's frontier outposts and Kalimdor's bloodthirsty harpies.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Letter to Jin'Zil?",a="Darsok Swiftdagger gives you the task at the Crossroads in the Barrens, after you complete the hunt for Serena Bloodfeather.",al={"quest giver","where to get quest","who starts letter to jin'zil"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Where can I find Witch Doctor Jin'Zil?",a="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil lives in a cave at Malaka'jin, a Darkspear troll encampment just off the main path into Stonetalon Mountains from the Barrens.",al={"where is jin'zil","jin'zil location","malaka'jin location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Darsok send you to Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Darsok sends you to tell his old friend Jin'Zil that Serena Bloodfeather's death has broken the harpy threat. He also sends a capable adventurer toward the wider challenges facing the Horde in the Stonetalon peaks.",al={"why go to stonetalon","why darsok sends letter"},it="motive"},{q="What previous sister of Serena is Jin'Zil referring to?",a="Jin'Zil refers to Bloodfeather, Serena's elder sister, who terrorized Kalimdor years earlier. The shadow hunter Rokhan and the half-ogre warrior Rexxar slew her while traveling with the founding Horde.",al={"serena older sister","rokhan and rexxar harpy","bloodfury"},it="history"},{q="Is this quest part of a larger chain?",a="Yes. This follows Harpy Raiders, Harpy Lieutenants, and Serena Bloodfeather, and concludes the northern Barrens harpy hunt. It also points toward Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"quest chain","prerequisites","what leads to this"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What faction can undertake this task?",a="Only the Horde can undertake this work. Darsok Swiftdagger and Witch Doctor Jin'Zil both serve the Horde frontier.",al={"is this horde only","can alliance do this quest"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Why does Darsok need you to deliver the letter to Jin'Zil?",a="Darsok Swiftdagger remains stationed at the Crossroads maintaining watch over the northern Barrens. Having watched you successfully purge the witchwing harpies and slay their leader Serena Bloodfeather, he views you as a proven, capable messenger who can handle the dangerous journey into Stonetalon Mountains. Passing word of Serena's downfall also gives you a worthy pretext to explore lands beyond the arid plains.",al={"why send me letter to jinzil","why cant darsok deliver the letter","why me letter to jinzil"},it="why_me",add="a93c7265"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warrior, you carry the effort to secure the Barrens' internal trade routes into the contested Stonetalon Mountains.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you find Jin'Zil's cave at Malaka'jin, an important spiritual and tactical outpost for Darkspear trolls securing the mountain approaches."},kw={"bloodfury","darsok swiftdagger","harpies","letter to jin'zil","malaka'jin","serena bloodfeather","stonetalon mountains","witch doctor jin'zil"},rel={"quest:876","npc:witch-doctor-jin-zil","npc:darsok-swiftdagger","subzone:malaka-jin","zone:stonetalon","quest:875","quest:867","zone:barrens"},m={start="Darsok Swiftdagger",["end"]="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1060},src={"Letter to Jin'Zil (quest)"}}
E["quest:1062"] = {t="quest",n="Goblin Invaders",z="stonetalon",s="At the Barrens and Stonetalon border, Seereth Stonebreak sends the Horde to strike Venture Company loggers in Windshear Crag. Their work lays waste to the mountains' ancient woodlands.",h="At the Barrens and Stonetalon border, Seereth Stonebreak sends the Horde to strike Venture Company loggers in...",sec={{t="A Forest in Agony",b="The Venture Company has cut deep into the Stonetalon Mountains, tearing through crags and valleys. Its loggers strip hillsides of timber and burn the underbrush, leaving scorched ground behind. For tauren and their allies, this is more than the destruction of forests by a mining and lumber company. The primal spirits bound to Stonetalon howl in torment. Seereth Stonebreak, stationed along the mountain border, sees that the goblins' relentless assault has left the spirits blind with agony and fury.",sp=0},{t="The Language of Force",b="The Venture Company's executives and hirelings care only for profit, and reason will not sway them. Seereth sends travelers past Greatwood Vale and into Windshear Crag to kill fifteen loggers. The Horde means to meet the company's greed with force, halting the deforestation and buying time for tauren elders to soothe the land's agitated spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Seereth Stonebreak?",a="Seereth Stonebreak is an orc shaman stationed near the southern boundary between the Barrens and the Stonetalon Mountains. She watches hostile factions encroach and works to protect the region's spiritual balance.",al={"seereth stonebreak","quest giver","who gives goblin invaders"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the goblins deforesting Stonetalon Mountains?",a="The Venture Company pursues profit without regard for the damage it causes. It treats Stonetalon's ancient forests and mineral-rich hills as materials to harvest, process, and sell, heedless of the natural and spiritual devastation left behind.",al={"why venture co logging","venture company motivation stonetalon","why cut trees"},it="why_here"},{q="Where is Windshear Crag located?",a="Windshear Crag lies in the central Stonetalon Mountains. From the Barrens border, follow the mountain road northwest through Greatwood Vale to the crag, where the forest gives way to Venture Company logging camps and clear-cut hills.",al={"windshear crag location","where are loggers","where to find venture co loggers"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do the spirits react to the Venture Company's presence?",a="Seereth Stonebreak says the land spirits suffer near-madness from rage and pain caused by the logging and burning. Their suffering disrupts nature's balance and threatens the entire region spiritually.",al={"stonetalon spirits angry","spirits of stonetalon reaction"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after culling the Venture Company loggers?",a="Killing the loggers is only the first blow against the operation. Seereth next directs the Horde against the company's machinery and recommends seeking tauren elders as guides who can help soothe the wounded spirits.",al={"after goblin invaders","next quest after loggers"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does the Horde care about logging in Stonetalon?",a="The tauren hold the Stonetalon Mountains dear for their culture and spiritual life. The Horde also sees the Venture Company's unchecked aggression and theft of resources as threats to its influence in the region and to spiritual harmony.",al={"horde interest stonetalon","why horde fight venture co"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Seereth Stonebreak want the Venture Company loggers killed?",a="The Venture Company is ruthlessly clear-cutting and burning large tracts of the Stonetalon Mountains. Their reckless destruction has driven the local nature spirits mad with agonizing pain and fury. Seereth wants the loggers struck down to halt the relentless pillaging and prove that the Horde will not tolerate the defilement of these sacred grounds.",al={"seereth stonebreak motive","why kill loggers","why does seereth care about goblins"},it="motive",add="c7723727"},{q="Who are the Venture Co. Loggers?",a="The Venture Co. Loggers are hired laborers and technicians employed by the notorious goblin syndicate. Driven purely by profit, they have pushed past Greatwood Vale into Windshear Crag, clear-cutting ancient timber and operating heavy machinery with complete disregard for the land or the wrath of its native spirits.",al={"who are the loggers","venture co loggers","venture company workers"},it="target",add="4d329e4c"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you have urgent cause to confront the Venture Company: its destruction of Stonetalon's forests torments the earth spirits you honor with the Earth Mother.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the destruction of living groves and ancient trees in Windshear Crag as an assault on the natural order you defend.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can feel the local elementals and nature spirits crying out, blinded by fury amid smoke and goblin machinery's destruction.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure the borderlands between the Barrens and the higher passes, so hostile commercial syndicates cannot fortify central Kalimdor."},kw={"goblin","greatwood vale","logger","seereth stonebreak","spirits","stonetalon mountains","venture company","windshear crag"},rel={"npc:seereth-stonebreak","subzone:windshear-crag","quest:1061","subzone:greatwood-vale","zone:stonetalon","topic:venture-company","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},m={start="Seereth Stonebreak",level="19",faction="Horde",id=1062},src={"Goblin Invaders"}}
E["quest:1068"] = {t="quest",n="Shredding Machines",z="stonetalon",s="In Windshear Crag, the Venture Company’s shredders wound Stonetalon’s spirits. Seereth Stonebreak hears their cries as XT:4 and XT:9 tear through the forest.",h="In Windshear Crag, the Venture Company’s shredders wound Stonetalon’s spirits.",sec={{t="A Vision of Deforestation",b="Orc shaman Seereth Stonebreak is stationed along the dusty border between the Barrens and the Stonetalon Mountains. She listens to the unseen realm, though chaos drowns out much of Stonetalon’s spiritual voice. One vision came through with harrowing clarity: man-shaped contraptions tearing through ancient woods with unnatural haste. Marked XT:4 and XT:9, the goblin-engineered shredders butcher Windshear Crag’s timberlands and send waves of distress through the surrounding nature spirits.",sp=0},{t="Silencing the Saws",b="The Venture Company operates in Windshear Crag, northwest of Greatwood Vale. To stem the devastation, Horde champions venture there and track down the logging constructs. Wrecking XT:4 and XT:9 deals a sharp blow to the mountains’ commercial deforestation and calms the immediate cries of wounded tree spirits. Seereth warns that unless the Venture Company abandons Stonetalon entirely, far darker atrocities await the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Seereth Stonebreak?",a="Seereth Stonebreak is an orc shaman posted along the southern border between the Barrens and the Stonetalon Mountains. Attuned to the land’s elemental and spiritual forces, she acts as a conduit for forest spirits anguished by the Venture Company’s rapid expansion.",al={"who is seereth","quest giver seereth","seereth stonebreak lore"},it="identity"},{q="What are XT:4 and XT:9?",a="XT:4 and XT:9 are specialized logging shredders operated by the Venture Company in Windshear Crag. Goblin operators pilot these steam-powered mechanical walkers, which cut ancient timber far faster than manual laborers.",al={"what are the shredders","xt4 and xt9","shredder targets"},it="target"},{q="Where is Windshear Crag?",a="Windshear Crag lies in the northern reaches of the Stonetalon Mountains, northwest of Greatwood Vale. The Venture Company has transformed it into a massive industrial logging basin.",al={"windshear crag location","where do i find the shredders","where are the machines"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does a shaman care about trees and druidic magic?",a="As Seereth explains, shamanistic communion with spirits shares close ties with druidic nature magic. Trauma inflicted on living forests echoes into the spiritual realm, letting perceptive shaman hear slaughtered tree spirits’ wails alongside elemental unrest.",al={"why do shaman care about trees","shaman druid connection","nature spirits shaman"},it="purpose"},{q="Who owns and operates these shredders?",a="The shredders belong to the Venture Company, an unscrupulous, goblin-run commercial conglomerate infamous across Azeroth for ruthlessly stripping valuable natural resources without regard for local ecosystems or ancestral inhabitants.",al={"who made xt4","who runs the shredders","venture company shredders"},it="people"},{q="Does destroying XT:4 and XT:9 drive the Venture Company away?",a="No. Destroying these machines calms the weeping tree spirits and sets back local logging, but the Venture Company keeps an extensive industrial foothold across Windshear Crag. Defenders of the wild must continue resisting its presence.",al={"does the venture company leave","after shredding machines","quest outcome"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Seereth Stonebreak want XT:4 and XT:9 destroyed?",a="As a shaman attuned to the spirit world, Seereth hears the agonizing cries of Stonetalon's battered land. The natural connection between shamanic spirituality and nature's balance allows her to perceive the tree spirits wailing as the Venture Company tears through the mountains. In a clear spiritual vision, she witnessed these two specific mechanical terrors felling the ancient timber at unnatural speed. To her, destroying them is vital spiritual stewardship; if these machines continue their unchecked slaughter of the forest, the land's wounds may never heal.",al={"why kill the shredders","seereth stonebreak motive","why destroy xt4 and xt9"},it="motive",add="0171bd6f"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Seereth points to the close ties between spiritual magic and nature. Elemental balance depends on defending the spirits that inhabit the land.",["race:Tauren"]="The desecration of Stonetalon’s ancient forests by soulless goblin machinery violates devotion to the Earth Mother.",["profession:Engineering"]="The XT-series logging mechs show advanced goblin shredder design, joining mechanical hydraulic saws with steam locomotion.",["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde establishes footholds across Kalimdor, checking the Venture Company’s unregulated greed matters for preserving the land and keeping transit through Stonetalon safe."},kw={"logging","seereth stonebreak","shredder","shredding machines","stonetalon mountains","venture company","windshear crag","xt:4","xt:9"},rel={"npc:seereth-stonebreak","subzone:windshear-crag","topic:venture-company","zone:stonetalon","quest:1061","subzone:greatwood-vale","topic:druid","zone:barrens"},m={start="Seereth Stonebreak",level="23",faction="Horde",id=1068},src={"Shredding Machines"}}
E["quest:1070"] = {t="quest",n="On Guard in Stonetalon",z="stonetalon",s="In Ashenvale, Sentinel Thenysil sends travelers south to check on Kaela Shadowspear. The scout went into Stonetalon to watch Venture Company incursions with a gnome mage, but word from her has fallen silent.",h="In Ashenvale, Sentinel Thenysil sends travelers south to check on Kaela Shadowspear.",sec={{t="A Scout Sent South",b="In Astranaar, Sentinel Thenysil watches for threats pressing toward the ancient forest. Her friend Kaela Shadowspear went into the Stonetalon Mountains at Sentinel Wolfrunner’s order, to survey turmoil in the heights. Thenysil asks passing Alliance champions to find Kaela; no word has come, and she fears for her friend’s safety.",sp=0},{t="Uneasy Partnerships in the Crags",b="Kaela’s companion is a gnome mage assigned by Alliance leaders. The night elves joined the Grand Alliance for strategic reasons, but many Sentinels distrust arcane practitioners and gnome tinkers in the wilderness. Kaela keeps an outpost on the bluffs above Windshear Crag, where she watches the Venture Company’s widespread devastation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Sentinel Thenysil, a night elf sentinel in Astranaar, Ashenvale, offers it.",al={"quest giver","where to start","who starts on guard in stonetalon"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Kaela Shadowspear?",a="Kaela Shadowspear is encamped on a rocky ridge overlooking the valley entrance to Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"kaela location","find kaela","kaela shadowspear spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Sentinel Thenysil worried about Kaela?",a="Kaela went to investigate dangerous hostile incursions in Stonetalon and has sent no word back. Thenysil is also wary of the gnome mage assigned to accompany her, a pairing she sees as an omen of trouble.",al={"why worry","thenysil concern"},it="motive"},{q="What threats are active in the Stonetalon Mountains?",a="The unscrupulous Venture Company, a goblin mining and logging cartel, is tearing up the wilderness. Aggressive native beasts and rival Horde forces are also pressing in from the south.",al={"stonetalon enemies","who is in stonetalon"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Tara?",a="Tara is Sentinel Thenysil’s first name. When you meet Kaela, she fondly calls her old friend Tara and takes pride in her work coordinating scouts and adventurers.",al={"who is tara","tara mentioned"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after finding Kaela Shadowspear?",a="Reaching Kaela completes the journey and leads to further work helping her and her gnome partner watch the threats encroaching on Windshear Crag.",al={"next quest","what comes next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Sentinel Thenysil need an adventurer to find Kaela?",a="Sentinel Thenysil is stationed on duty in Ashenvale and cannot simply abandon her post to ride into neighboring lands. When she sees a capable traveler displaying wanderlust, she seizes the chance to recruit an independent scout who can slip across the border into Stonetalon without disrupting local Sentinel defenses.",al={"why send me","why doesnt thenysil go","why an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="96da069b"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This marks Alliance frontier security moving south, from Ashenvale’s defense outposts to isolated scouting perches in the Stonetalon Mountains.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the strain between traditional Sentinels and the arcane and mechanical ways of their Eastern Kingdom allies, especially gnomes.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may find Sentinels’ deep skepticism toward gnomish magic and contraptions a hard welcome. They see a gnome mage in Kalimdor’s wilderness as an odd, unpredictable presence."},kw={"ashenvale","kaela shadowspear","on guard in stonetalon","sentinel thenysil","stonetalon mountains","venture co","windshear crag"},rel={"npc:sentinel-thenysil","npc:kaela-shadowspear","zone:stonetalon","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:ashenvale","topic:sentinels","topic:gnome","quest:764"},m={start="Sentinel Thenysil",["end"]="Kaela Shadowspear",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1070},src={"On Guard in Stonetalon"}}
E["quest:1071"] = {t="quest",n="A Gnome's Respite",z="stonetalon",s="At Windshear Crag, Gaxim Rustfizzle struggles to slow the Venture Company's push into the forest. He asks travelers to drive back its workers so he can prepare new defenses.",h="At Windshear Crag, Gaxim Rustfizzle struggles to slow the Venture Company's push into the forest.",sec={{t="A Clashing Alliance",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle represents the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences. Among Stonetalon's ancient groves, he is meant to show the nature-worshipping night elves that gnomish invention can protect their threatened lands. He combines magic, chemical brews and mechanics, but the Venture Company's relentless pace leaves him little time to build defensive devices.",sp=0},{t="Buying Time in Windshear Crag",b="Gaxim sends travelers into the smoking works at Windshear Crag to turn back the Venture Co. Loggers and Deforesters. Their retreat would give him time to organize his workshop and devise his next defense: controlled, strategic high explosives.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an Alliance gnome mage and tinkerer in the Stonetalon Mountains. He works for the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences and seeks to aid the night elves against industrial invaders.",al={"gaxim","who is gaxim rustfizzle","quest giver gaxim"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a gnome trying to protect night elf forests?",a="Gaxim believes he must prove to skeptical night elves that gnomish sciences can coexist with nature and defend their wilderness. He draws on arcanology, alchemy and engineering against unchecked industrial exploitation.",al={"why gnome in stonetalon","why help night elves","gnome ecology"},it="why_here"},{q="Who are the Venture Company in Windshear Crag?",a="The Venture Company is a goblin-run merchant syndicate cutting timber and strip-mining Windshear Crag. Its loggers, deforesters and heavy machinery have overrun the valley in pursuit of profit.",al={"venture co stonetalon","who are venture co","windshear crag goblins"},it="target"},{q="Where can the loggers and deforesters be found?",a="The loggers and deforesters work throughout Windshear Crag, the industrial basin directly east of Gaxim's position along the main road in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"where are loggers","where to find deforesters","windshear crag location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Gaxim plan to do once he gets time to think?",a="Once the goblin workers are driven back, Gaxim plans to replenish his high explosives. He intends to use targeted mountain blasts to herd and frighten the Venture Company away from the groves.",al={"gaxim plan","gnome respite continuation","explosives plan"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences?",a="The Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences is a gnomish academic society. It explores how arcane spellcraft, chemical mixtures and mechanical engineering can solve practical problems across Azeroth.",al={"gnomish assembly","arcanology assembly","what is enlightened assembly"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Gaxim Rustfizzle want the Venture Company culled?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle feels it is his duty as a member of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences to prove that gnomish ingenuity can protect the night elves' sacred forests. The Venture Company's relentlessly rapid deforestation keeps him constantly overwhelmed, leaving him no breathing room to devise, organize, and assemble the inventive devices and explosives he needs to turn the tide.",al={"why kill loggers","gaxim motive","why cull venture co"},it="motive",add="8136de5d"},{q="Why does Gaxim Rustfizzle need you to fight the goblins?",a="Gaxim is an inventor and researcher rather than an army of one, and he is working without major Alliance military support in Stonetalon. Between keeping his camp secure and attempting to draft new mechanical schematics, he simply cannot fight off the endlessly swarming Venture Company loggers alone. He relies on capable adventurers like you to thin their ranks so he can focus on building his countermeasures.",al={"why me gaxim","why does gaxim need help","why send an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="7aed6e2a"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see Gaxim's ambition at work: he seeks to meet the conflict between nature and civilization with ingenuity and high explosives.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know gnomish machinery draws deep suspicion from Kaldorei sentinels. In Stonetalon, the Venture Company's advance makes any effective deterrent welcome.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you may appreciate Gaxim's faith in mechanisms and chemistry to address environmental crises, along with his fondness for high explosives."},kw={"deforester","explosives","gaxim rustfizzle","gnome","logger","stonetalon","venture co","windshear crag"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","topic:goblin","quest:1070"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1071},src={"A Gnome's Respite"}}
E["quest:1072"] = {t="quest",n="An Old Colleague",z="stonetalon",s="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Gaxim Rustfizzle seeks a powerful device and the means to fuel it. The gnome engineer sends you across the sea to Ironforge, where his old acquaintance Lomac Gearstrip can make a hazardous explosive compound called Nitromirglyceronium.",h="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Gaxim Rustfizzle seeks a powerful device and the means to fuel it.",sec={{t="A Volatile Recipe",b="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Gaxim Rustfizzle plans his most ambitious engineering work yet. A mechanism of that scale needs fuel stronger than ordinary gunpowder or crude oil. He needs Nitromirglyceronium, also called NG-5, an explosive mix potent enough to ensure destruction if all goes according to plan.",sp=0},{t="Tinker Town Connection",b="Only one person Gaxim knows can refine NG-5: his old acquaintance Lomac Gearstrip. Lomac lives far to the east, in Tinker Town, the gnome quarter deep inside Ironforge. You make the long journey as Gaxim's courier, but Lomac greets you with immediate suspicion and paranoid questions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest An Old Colleague?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle, a gnome engineer in the Stonetalon Mountains, sends you to Ironforge.",al={"quest giver","who starts an old colleague","gaxim quest"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Lomac Gearstrip?",a="Lomac Gearstrip lives in Tinker Town, the gnome quarter in the eastern part of Ironforge.",al={"where is lomac","lomac gearstrip location","ironforge lomac"},gp=true},{q="What is Nitromirglyceronium?",a="Nitromirglyceronium, or NG-5, is an extremely volatile chemical explosive that Lomac Gearstrip can make and Gaxim Rustfizzle wants for his powerful devices.",al={"what is ng-5","nitromirglyceronium","ng 5"},it="item"},{q="Why does Gaxim send me all the way to Ironforge?",a="Gaxim says Lomac Gearstrip is the only person who can make the specialized NG-5 compound his experimental device needs for fuel.",al={"why travel to ironforge","why lomac","why go to tinker town"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after finding Lomac Gearstrip?",a="After you confirm Gaxim's request, the suspicious Lomac gives you Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun, which calls for hazardous reagents to mix the batch.",al={"next quest","what comes after an old colleague","followup quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Which faction can undertake this task?",a="Only Alliance adventurers can take on this work. It begins with the Alliance gnome Gaxim in Stonetalon and leads to the Alliance capital of Ironforge.",al={"is this alliance only","horde version","can horde do this"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Why does Gaxim Rustfizzle need you instead of going to Ironforge himself?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is busy in the Stonetalon Mountains scouting and preparing the tactical placement for his experimental devices. Because fabricating the high-grade explosive Nitromirglyceronium requires a long trek back across the sea to Tinker Town in Ironforge, he relies on a capable traveler to handle the legwork while he stays on-site to ready the operation.",al={"why does gaxim need me","why send an adventurer to ironforge","why can't gaxim go to lomac"},it="why_me",add="bce9e2b8"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you travel across a continent from Kalimdor's embattled crags to the safety of Ironforge.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you know the long reach of scholarly connections, eccentric rivalries, and explosive compounds that can turn dangerously unstable.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate Gaxim and Lomac's drive for maximum firepower, despite the hazardous logistics."},kw={"explosives","gaxim rustfizzle","ironforge","lomac gearstrip","ng-5","nitromirglyceronium","stonetalon","tinker town"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","npc:lomac-gearstrip","quest:1073","subzone:tinker-town","zone:ironforge","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",["end"]="Lomac Gearstrip",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1072},src={"An Old Colleague"}}
E["quest:1073"] = {t="quest",n="Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun",z="stonetalon",s="Across the sea, Alliance adventurers reach Ironforge seeking an explosive answer to the Venture Company in Stonetalon. Lomac Gearstrip agrees to brew Nitromirglyceronium if you bring him the needed alchemical reagents.",h="Across the sea, Alliance adventurers reach Ironforge seeking an explosive answer to the Venture Company in...",sec={{t="A Volatile Solution",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle needs powerful explosives for his most advanced device against the Venture Company. He is stationed high in the craggy passes of the Stonetalon Mountains, far from his eccentric former colleague Lomac Gearstrip in Ironforge. Lomac created Nitromirglyceronium, a compound so unstable and destructive that he finds the thought of anyone using it hilarious, no matter who gets blown apart.",sp=0},{t="Potions for Pyrotechnics",b="Lomac is eager to see goblin machinery, and perhaps you, blown to pieces, but his Ironforge workshop has run out of Nitromirglyceronium. Before brewing another batch, he asks for Minor Mana Potions and Elixirs of Minor Fortitude. The draughts supply the raw reagents for his mixture, and gathering them lets Lomac judge whether you have even a shred of respect for alchemy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lomac Gearstrip?",a="Lomac Gearstrip is an eccentric gnomish alchemist and tinkerer in Ironforge, the dwarven capital. He is Gaxim Rustfizzle's former colleague and created the volatile explosive Nitromirglyceronium.",al={"lomac gearstrip","who is lomac","ironforge gnome"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Lomac want potions instead of standard engineering parts?",a="Lomac combines alchemy with his mechanical knowledge to make volatile reactions. Minor Mana Potions provide magical energy, while Elixirs of Minor Fortitude provide stabilizing bodily humors; both serve as base reagents for his Nitromirglyceronium mixture.",al={"why potions","alchemical ingredients","why mana potions"},it="item"},{q="Why send an adventurer all the way to Ironforge for this?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is isolated in the Stonetalon wilds, without access to heavy industrial or chemical workshops. Lomac Gearstrip in Ironforge is the only associate Gaxim trusts, or fears enough, to have an explosive potent enough for his most advanced device.",al={"why ironforge","why travel so far","gaxim to ironforge"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Nitromirglyceronium?",a="Nitromirglyceronium is Lomac Gearstrip's explosive chemical brew, notoriously volatile and, as Lomac calls it, his greatest creation.",al={"nitromirglyceronium","what is the explosive","gnome bomb juice"},it="origin"},{q="Is Lomac worried about the Venture Company or the forest?",a="Lomac has no concern for the Venture Company or the forest. He laughs at the idea of using explosives to save trees and wants to watch either the goblins or the courier get blasted to pieces.",al={"does lomac care about nature","lomac motives"},it="side"},{q="Do you need to be an alchemist to complete this task?",a="No. Lomac speaks of testing your alchemical skill, but he accepts reagents obtained through trade, merchants, or other crafters, as long as he gets the draughts his recipe requires.",al={"need alchemy","alchemy required"},gp=true},{q="Why does Lomac Gearstrip want this done?",a="Lomac cares little for the Venture Company, the fate of Stonetalon's forests, or his old acquaintance Gaxim Rustfizzle. What delights him is sheer chaos and explosive potential. He agrees to brew his volatile Nitromirglyceronium simply for the twisted amusement of watching either you or the goblins blow up into tiny pieces, provided you supply the reagents to replenish his stock.",al={"lomac gearstrip motive","why help lomac","why make nitromirglyceronium"},it="motive",add="04ca68af"},{q="What is the Minor Mana Potion for?",a="The Minor Mana Potions are essential liquid reagents in Lomac's unstable concoction. Along with the fortitude elixirs, their magical energy serves as a vital catalyst required to synthesize a fresh batch of Nitromirglyceronium, his volatile and prideful alchemical invention.",al={"minor mana potion use","why minor mana potion","mana potion nitromirglyceronium"},it="item",add="23e9865b"},{q="What is the Elixir of Minor Fortitude for?",a="Lomac requires the Elixirs of Minor Fortitude as key components for brewing Nitromirglyceronium. In his eccentric chemical recipe, the fortifying mixture forms part of the reactive base needed to create the explosive compound.",al={"elixir of minor fortitude use","why elixir of minor fortitude","fortitude elixir nitromirglyceronium"},it="item",add="2bdc95b5"},{q="Why does Lomac need you to fetch the potions instead of getting them himself?",a="Lomac is completely out of supplies and feels no urgency to help you or Gaxim on his own dime. By making you fetch or brew the ingredients yourself, he forces you to prove your resourcefulness and alchemical competence before he entrusts you with his prized, dangerous creation.",al={"why does lomac need me","why do i need to get the potions","why cant lomac get his own potions"},it="why_me",add="ba2add0a"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Lomac represents the unrestrained, madcap edge of gnomish ingenuity, putting chemical yield and theory ahead of safety or diplomatic caution.",["faction:Alliance"]="The long journey from Stonetalon to Ironforge shows the strain of supporting remote Alliance outposts scattered across hostile Kalimdor.",["profession:Engineering"]="When ordinary blasting powder fails against Venture Company steel, alchemy joined with engineering can bring far greater destruction."},kw={"elixir of minor fortitude","gaxim rustfizzle","ironforge","lomac gearstrip","mana potion","nitromirglyceronium","stonetalon","venture company"},rel={"npc:lomac-gearstrip","quest:1072","zone:stonetalon","zone:ironforge","topic:goblin"},m={start="Lomac Gearstrip",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1073,ri={"Elixir of Minor Fortitude","Minor Mana Potion"}},src={"Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun"}}
E["quest:1074"] = {t="quest",n="Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun",z="stonetalon",s="Lomac Gearstrip sends volatile NG-5 to Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon Mountains. Gaxim needs the chemical to ignite several wagons packed with dynamite, creating a distraction for Alliance operations in the disputed crags.",h="Lomac Gearstrip sends volatile NG-5 to Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Volatile Delivery",b="Lomac Gearstrip hands over Nitromirglyceronium, or NG-5, an unstable compound born of gnomish engineering. He warns you to handle it with extreme care. Mishandled, the chemical could blow you to pieces on the road back to Gaxim Rustfizzle.",sp=0},{t="A Recipe for Distraction",b="Once Gaxim Rustfizzle receives the canister intact, he explains what he intends to do with it. NG-5 can ignite entire wagons packed with dynamite. Gaxim plans a great explosion to sow chaos and draw enemies away in Stonetalon while the Alliance pursues its goals in the region.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is NG-5?",a="NG-5, short for Nitromirglyceronium, is a highly volatile chemical compound made by Lomac Gearstrip. It is needed to ignite heavy explosives.",al={"what is nitromirglyceronium","ng-5","what did lomac give me"},it="item"},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is a gnome mage in the Stonetalon Mountains. He directs Alliance demolition efforts and uses explosions to distract regional threats.",al={"gaxim","who is gaxim rustfizzle"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Lomac Gearstrip?",a="Lomac Gearstrip is an engineer and associate of Gaxim Rustfizzle. He prepares the dangerous NG-5 compound and hands it over to couriers.",al={"lomac","who is lomac gearstrip"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gaxim need so much explosive power?",a="Gaxim has arranged several wagons packed with dynamite. NG-5 can ignite them in a single blast, creating a powerful diversion.",al={"why wagons of dynamite","gaxim plan","why the explosion"},it="motive"},{q="Is the chemical dangerous to transport?",a="Yes. Lomac warns that NG-5 is unstable and could detonate if mishandled. Handle it carefully on the way to Gaxim.",al={"does ng5 explode","is ng-5 safe"},it="danger"},{q="Where does this delivery take place?",a="The delivery ends at Gaxim Rustfizzle's post in the passes of the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"where is gaxim","stonetalon location"},it="place"},{q="Why does Lomac Gearstrip give you the NG-5?",a="Lomac is fulfilling a request from his associate Gaxim Rustfizzle, providing the volatile Nitromirglyceronium as asked. He does not pry into the details—if you truly are Gaxim's ally, he sends along his greetings, and if you are an imposter, he is content letting the explosive compound blow you to pieces.",al={"why does lomac help","lomac gearstrip motive","why give ng5"},it="motive",add="cbbf8960"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Gnomish ambition puts Nitromirglyceronium to work igniting wagons of explosives as a distraction.",["profession:Engineering"]="Handling NG-5 calls for care with volatile chemicals to avoid an early detonation.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stonetalon is contested, and a massive explosion gives Alliance operatives room to pursue their goals."},kw={"dynamite","engineering","gaxim rustfizzle","gnome","lomac gearstrip","ng-5","nitromirglyceronium","stonetalon"},rel={"quest:1073","npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","npc:lomac-gearstrip","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Lomac Gearstrip",["end"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1074},src={"Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun (2)"}}
E["quest:1077"] = {t="quest",n="Special Delivery for Gaxim",z="stonetalon",s="In Stonetalon, Gaxim Rustfizzle awaits a scroll from Stormwind. Collin Mauren provides the Scroll of Messaging, whose arcane power is needed to build a remote explosive against the Venture Company's deforestation.",h="In Stonetalon, Gaxim Rustfizzle awaits a scroll from Stormwind.",sec={{t="Arcane Deliveries",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle seeks to hinder the Venture Company's destructive work in the Stonetalon Mountains. He has made an explosive compound called NG-5, but lacks a reliable way to set it off from afar. Rather than use crude fuses, Gaxim enlisted help across the Great Sea. He contacted Collin Mauren in Stormwind's Mage Quarter to obtain an enchanted Scroll of Messaging.",sp=0},{t="A Remote Distraction",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle plans to bind the Scroll of Messaging's magic to his unstable NG-5 mixture. Its power to carry messages across long distances can trigger the explosive from afar. Gaxim means to create a devastating distraction, giving operatives a chance to slip into the Venture Company compound unseen.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Scroll of Messaging used for?",a="The Scroll of Messaging carries words across long distances, but Gaxim Rustfizzle can bind its magic to NG-5 as a remote trigger. That lets him set off explosives from a safe distance.",al={"why scroll of messaging","what does the scroll do","scroll of messaging purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Collin Mauren?",a="Collin Mauren is an Alliance wizard in Stormwind City's Mage Quarter. He helps with arcane matters and crafts the enchanted scroll Gaxim needs in Stonetalon.",al={"collin mauren lore","who is collin"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Gaxim Rustfizzle sabotaging the Venture Company?",a="The Venture Company is ruthlessly clear-cutting the Stonetalon Mountains' pristine forests. Gaxim aims to slow the deforestation by causing chaos, destroying their operations, and stealing their engineering plans and correspondence.",al={"why attack venture co","gaxim motivation","venture co stonetalon"},it="conflict"},{q="Where does this delivery take the adventurer?",a="The delivery takes you from Stormwind City across the sea to the Alliance camp in the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains on Kalimdor.",al={"delivery destination","where is gaxim","stonetalon location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after the scroll is delivered?",a="With the scroll and NG-5 in hand, Gaxim prepares a remote explosive distraction. It clears the way for an operative to enter the Windshear Crag operations and recover logging letters and schematics.",al={"next quest","what after delivery","venture co distraction"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Collin Mauren want this done?",a="Collin Mauren is acting as a helpful arcane colleague and friend to Gaxim Rustfizzle. While Collin remains safely in Stormwind conducting his magical studies, he is intrigued by Gaxim's daring scheme against the Venture Company in Kalimdor and gladly provides the necessary spell, looking forward to hearing all about the adventure once it is finished.",al={"collin mauren motive","why help gaxim collin","collin mauren why send scroll"},it="motive",add="89640f85"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Gaxim's scheme joins gnomish engineering with wizardry, pairing volatile NG-5 explosives with arcane triggers.",["class:Mage"]="Collin Mauren's craft shows how clever tinkerers can turn a simple parchment enchantment into a working arcane relay.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the ties between Stormwind and remote outposts resisting industrial exploitation in Kalimdor."},kw={"collin mauren","gaxim rustfizzle","ng-5","remote explosive","scroll of messaging","stonetalon","venture co"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","npc:collin-mauren","zone:stonetalon","quest:764"},m={start="Collin Mauren",["end"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1077},src={"Special Delivery for Gaxim"}}
E["quest:1078"] = {t="quest",n="Retrieval for Mauren",z="stonetalon",s="In Stormwind, Collin Mauren asks travelers bound for Kalimdor to bring him rare basilisk scales. He wants scales from the Charred Vale in Stonetalon to grind into dust for his spellcraft.",h="In Stormwind, Collin Mauren asks travelers bound for Kalimdor to bring him rare basilisk scales.",sec={{t="A Mage's Curious Reagents",b="Collin Mauren, a wizard in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, listens to tales from wandering adventurers. He has heard that travelers are venturing deep into Kalimdor, where Stonetalon draws those seeking wild wyverns, unruly elementals, or deals and clashes with the Venture Company. Mauren is not after riches or glory. He wants to learn what rare natural wonders survive in the region's harshest corners.",sp=0},{t="The Glassy Beasts of the Vale",b="The Charred Vale lies deep in Stonetalon, an ash-choked basin scarred by the Venture Company's devastation. Mauren's studies say a peculiar breed of basilisk once lived there. Their scales, crushed to a fine powder, can catalyze specialized arcane spells he has developed. He does not know whether the basilisks survived the Vale's harsh transformation, so he asks explorers to bring back fresh crystallised scales and learn whether the breed endures.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Collin Mauren?",a="Collin Mauren is a wizard in Stormwind's Mage Quarter who studies arcane spellcraft and seeks rare reagents from distant lands.",al={"collin mauren","who gives retrieval for mauren","mauren stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Collin Mauren need basilisk scales?",a="Mauren grinds crystallised basilisk scales into fine dust to use as a catalyst for spells he has devised.",al={"why scales","what are scales for","crystallized scales use"},it="item"},{q="Where is the Charred Vale located?",a="The Charred Vale is a ruined basin in southwestern Stonetalon Mountains, on Kalimdor.",al={"where charred vale","find charred vale","charred vale location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Charred Vale charred?",a="The Venture Company's goblins devastated the Charred Vale. Their destruction enraged the vale's spirits and loosed elementals, leaving the ground blackened and smoldering, with hardy, twisted beasts roaming it.",al={"what happened to charred vale","charred vale fire","charred vale destruction"},it="history"},{q="What creatures drop the scales needed for this task?",a="Basilisks in the Charred Vale of Stonetalon Mountains have the scales Mauren seeks.",al={"which basilisks","who drops crystallized scales","scale mobs"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why send an adventurer all the way across the sea for this?",a="Mauren needs the crystalline properties found on basilisks native to the Charred Vale. Crossing the Great Sea is perilous, so he asks seasoned travelers already bound for Kalimdor.",al={"why kalimdor","why stonetalon for scales"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Collin Mauren want the basilisk scales?",a="Collin Mauren is an inventive mage residing in Stormwind who crafts his own original spells. He discovered that the crystallized scales of basilisks native to Stonetalon's Charred Vale, once ground into fine dust, serve as an ideal magical reagent. Because he remains in the city conducting arcane studies, he relies on venturing travelers to replenish his rare stock.",al={"collin mauren motive","why does mauren want scales","why collect scales for mauren"},it="motive",add="ae0c8dc0"},{q="What creatures are you hunting in the Charred Vale?",a="You are sent into the scorched depths of the Charred Vale to track down the local basilisks that dwell among the ash and elemental ruins. Mauren remembers their unique crystal-crusted hides from past reports, though he is uncertain whether the hardy beasts have survived the catastrophic burning of the valley.",al={"what basilisks in charred vale","who do i fight for mauren","stonetalon basilisk targets"},it="target",add="c10c105c"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know that gathering rare reagents for other wizards supports arcane research. Exotic magical wildlife can provide what is needed to develop new incantations.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you see Stormwind's interests and supply lines reaching deep into Kalimdor's wild territories."},kw={"basilisk scales","charred vale","collin mauren","crystallized scales","mage quarter","retrieval for mauren","stonetalon mountains","stormwind"},rel={"npc:collin-mauren","subzone:charred-vale","zone:stonetalon","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:764"},m={start="Collin Mauren",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=1078,ri={"Crystalized Scales"}},src={"Retrieval for Mauren"}}
E["quest:1079"] = {t="quest",n="Covert Ops - Alpha",z="stonetalon",s="Alliance agents work under Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon Mountains. From the peaks, they enter the Venture Company lumber mill in Windshear Crag to recover engineering schematics.",h="Alliance agents work under Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Sabotage and Espionage",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle directs a covert effort from Windshear Crag against the Venture Company's aggressive logging. Goblin loggers cut timber south of Cragpool Lake, but destruction alone cannot stop them. Plan Alpha sends agents past the loggers and overseers to take the mill's technical schematics.",sp=0},{t="Reverse Engineering",b="The Venture Company's schematics interest gnomes for more than the night elves' forests. The plans show how goblin loggers, mechanical cutters and mechanized transports work. Alliance engineers can use them to find structural flaws and break up future operations, while adapting goblin designs for their own projects in Ironforge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the primary goal of Covert Ops - Alpha?",a="Recover the Venture Company's engineering plans from its lumber mill in Windshear Crag, south of Cragpool Lake. Explosives are part of the wider covert effort, but success depends on bringing back the blueprints.",al={"what is covert ops alpha","alpha mission goal","what does gaxim want"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives the quest Covert Ops - Alpha?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle, an Alliance gnome tinker in the Stonetalon Mountains, directs sabotage against goblin industry.",al={"who starts covert ops alpha","gaxim rustfizzle quest","covert ops quest giver"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Where are the engineering plans located?",a="The Venture Company Engineering Plans are inside the operational lumber mill in Windshear Crag, south of Cragpool Lake, guarded by goblin loggers.",al={"where are the venture co plans","engineering plans location","windshear crag lumber mill plans"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gaxim Rustfizzle want the Venture Co. blueprints?",a="Gaxim wants to study the structural weaknesses of goblin logging machines. Their flaws can guide more effective sabotage of future machinery, and their useful designs can improve Alliance devices.",al={"why steal venture co plans","what will gaxim do with plans","reason for covert ops alpha"},it="motive"},{q="Is sheer destruction the point of the mission?",a="No. Gaxim says success depends on recovering the schematics intact, not on how much destruction the agents cause.",al={"do i blow up the mill","should i destroy machines","mission destruction focus"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Alliance fighting the Venture Company here?",a="The Venture Company cuts forests and pollutes the land in Stonetalon. Alliance agents work to disrupt its industry and protect strategic territory in Kalimdor.",al={"why fight venture company in stonetalon","alliance venture co conflict","stonetalon logging war"},it="conflict"},{q="What are the Venture Co. Engineering Plans for?",a="These detailed schematics outline the internal mechanisms and layout of the Venture Company's heavy logging machinery in Windshear Crag. By recovering them, Gaxim Rustfizzle aims to pinpoint critical design flaws in their equipment to sabotage future operations, while also stealing their best concepts to improve Alliance engineering innovations.",al={"venture co engineering plans use","what are the blueprints for","engineering plans purpose"},it="item",add="f4c6420b"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome tinker, you can study goblin plans, spot flaws in their designs and take their lucrative mechanical tricks.",["profession:Engineering"]="The schematics reveal the gritty, high-combustion mechanisms used by the Venture Company and offer insight into industrial motor works.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the Venture Company's logging in Windshear Crag wound Stonetalon's ancient forests. Sabotaging its logging works is urgent.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure footholds and curb industrial extraction across Kalimdor, maintaining tactical parity against rival powers pressing into contested wilderness."},kw={"alpha","covert ops","cragpool lake","engineering plans","gaxim rustfizzle","lumber mill","stonetalon","venture co","windshear crag"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:cragpool-lake","zone:stonetalon","quest:764"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1079,ri={"Venture Co. Engineering Plans"}},src={"Covert Ops - Alpha"}}
E["quest:1080"] = {t="quest",n="Covert Ops - Beta",z="stonetalon",s="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Gaxim Rustfizzle sends an agent into the Venture Company’s mine. Explosives will draw the goblins away while the agent takes letters that reveal the company’s plans and help defend the Sentinels’ lands.",h="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Gaxim Rustfizzle sends an agent into the Venture Company’s mine.",sec={{t="Sabotage in the Depths",b="After the first blows against the Venture Company’s logging at Windshear Crag, Gaxim Rustfizzle turns to the company’s supply heart. The plan follows the same pattern as before: an explosive diversion scatters goblin workers and mercenaries while an agent searches the mine for written orders and records.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on Windshear Mine",b="At the eastern edge of Windshear Crag, Windshear Mine is the Venture Company’s base beneath the mountain. Its goblins dig for rock and cut timber, keeping records of supply routes and orders from their leaders. An agent slips inside, sets Gaxim’s explosive packs, and takes the Venture Co. Letters. The blast disrupts the mine’s guard, and the letters reveal more of the company’s plans in Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="A Pragmatic Partnership",b="Gaxim takes pleasure in clever devices and explosions, but the work also matters to the night elves. In Stonetalon, the Sentinels face the Horde as well as the companies cutting and digging through their lands. Letters from the mine give commanders such as Kaela Shadowspear information they can use to anticipate threats to the sacred woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the goal of Covert Ops - Beta?",a="An agent enters Windshear Mine at the eastern end of Windshear Crag, sets Gaxim Rustfizzle’s explosive pack as a diversion, and takes the Venture Co. Letters about the company’s operations.",al={"covert ops beta objective","what do i do in covert ops beta","plan beta goal"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is a gnome engineer in the Stonetalon Mountains. He uses his engineering and explosives to aid the night elf Sentinels against the Venture Company’s logging and mining.",al={"gaxim rustfizzle","who gives covert ops beta"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Windshear Mine located?",a="Windshear Mine lies at the eastern end of Windshear Crag, within the Venture Company’s logged lands.",al={"windshear mine location","where is the mine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gaxim want the Venture Co. Letters?",a="The Venture Co. Letters detail supply routes, orders from leaders, and plans for the region. They help the Alliance and the Sentinels anticipate the company’s actions and hinder its work in the forest.",al={"why steal letters","what are the venture co letters"},it="motive"},{q="How does this mission benefit the night elves?",a="The Sentinels have too few forces to watch all of Stonetalon. Gaxim’s blasts delay the logging, and the letters give commanders such as Kaela Shadowspear useful intelligence about their foes.",al={"why do night elves care","sentinels covert ops"},it="ties"},{q="What was Plan Alpha?",a="Plan Alpha was Gaxim’s earlier operation at the Venture Company lumber mill south of Cragpool Lake. An agent used an explosive diversion to steal the company’s engineering plans, and Plan Beta uses the same approach at Windshear Mine.",al={"plan alpha","covert ops alpha","previous mission"},it="history"},{q="What are the Venture Co. Letters for?",a="These documents contain vital communications and plans from the Venture Company's leadership inside Windshear Mine. By seizing them, Gaxim Rustfizzle and the local night elf Sentinels hope to uncover the defilers' operations, disrupt their aggressive logging and mining efforts across Stonetalon, and hand a critical tactical advantage back to Kaela's defenders.",al={"venture co letters use","why venture co letters","what are the letters"},it="item",add="c7fb3974"},{q="Who are you infiltrating at Windshear Mine?",a="You are striking at the Venture Company, an unscrupulous goblin-run commercial cartel infamous for ruthless resource exploitation. They have entrenched themselves within Windshear Crag, gouging out the earth, harvesting the sacred forests, and ignoring the sacred land claims of the night elves, turning the entire region into an industrial blight.",al={"windshear mine enemies","who is at windshear crag","venture co stonetalon"},it="target",add="2e3cb5f9"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see engineering skill and careful planning put to military use in Gaxim Rustfizzle’s explosive devices and covert work.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the Venture Company is cutting down the ancient woods. Gaxim’s operations give Sentinel commanders information to help defend the mountain.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how Gaxim’s Covert Ops Pack uses a clever explosive diversion to open a path through guarded ground.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see gnomish devices aid the night elves’ defense of their lands in central Kalimdor."},kw={"covert ops - beta","gaxim rustfizzle","sentinels","stonetalon mountains","venture co.","venture co. letters","windshear crag","windshear mine"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","subzone:windshear-crag","quest:764","topic:sentinels","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1080,ri={"Venture Co. Letters"}},src={"Covert Ops - Beta"}}
E["quest:1081"] = {t="quest",n="Reception from Tyrande",z="stonetalon",s="Sentinel Thenysil sends you from Astranaar to Darnassus for an audience with Tyrande Whisperwind. After you help the Sentinels hold their ground against the Venture Company in Stonetalon, Tyrande receives you at the Temple of the Moon.",h="Sentinel Thenysil sends you from Astranaar to Darnassus for an audience with Tyrande Whisperwind.",sec={{t="A Foothold in Stonetalon",b="The Venture Company puts pressure on night elf outposts across the Stonetalon Mountains. Sentinel Thenysil coordinates the defense from Astranaar, but the remote bases are hard to sustain. Supply lines and intelligence help the Sentinels keep an Alliance presence in Kalimdor's interior, and your aid strengthens their position.",sp=0},{t="Audience with the High Priestess",b="After your help bolsters the Sentinels in Stonetalon, Sentinel Thenysil sends you back to Teldrassil. Tyrande Whisperwind, the High Priestess, grants you an audience at the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. She recognizes your deeds across Kalimdor and welcomes you as an ally fighting alongside the kaldorei.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this quest start?",a="Sentinel Thenysil gives you this work in Astranaar, Ashenvale, after you complete 'Update for Sentinel Thenysil'.",al={"where do i get reception from tyrande","quest giver","sentinel thenysil location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where can I find Tyrande Whisperwind?",a="Tyrande Whisperwind is in the Temple of the Moon, in Darnassus's central district on Teldrassil.",al={"where is tyrande","find tyrande","temple of the moon location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Tyrande want to see me?",a="Your efforts in Stonetalon help preserve the Kaldorei foothold in contested mountain territory. Sentinel Thenysil believes your service merits appreciation from the night elves' spiritual and military leader.",al={"why tyrande wants to talk","purpose of audience"},it="motive"},{q="What is the strategic value of the Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Stonetalon forms a rugged buffer between Ashenvale and Kalimdor's southern plains. Holding its outposts helps the night elves watch Horde movements from the Barrens and protect sacred lands.",al={"why care about stonetalon","stonetalon lore"},it="place"},{q="Do other Alliance races get recognized here?",a="Yes. Any Alliance adventurer who helps Sentinel Thenysil can travel to Darnassus, reflecting the growing defense shared by the night elves and the wider Alliance.",al={"can non night elves do this","is this for humans"},it="allies"},{q="Is there a follow-up quest after meeting Tyrande?",a="Meeting Tyrande concludes the Stonetalon courier and support work for Sentinel Thenysil. You can seek further orders in Darnassus.",al={"what comes next","next quest in chain"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Thenysil send you to Darnassus?",a="Sentinel Thenysil believes your efforts have laid the groundwork to secure the night elves' foothold in the embattled Stonetalon Mountains. Recognizing your dedication in standing against the atrocities unfolding in the peaks, she wants you to receive formal recognition and gratitude directly from the night elf leader, High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind.",al={"why does thenysil send me","thenysil reason tyrande","why go to tyrande"},it="motive",add="e0e9e6b4"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="An audience with Tyrande Whisperwind links the night elves of Kalimdor with the wider Alliance, bringing recognition in Darnassus for service in the wilderness.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, reporting to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind in the Temple of the Moon is a homecoming and a sign of your devotion to defending your ancestral lands."},kw={"darnassus","kaldorei","reception from tyrande","sentinel thenysil","stonetalon mountains","teldrassil","temple of the moon","tyrande whisperwind"},rel={"npc:tyrande-whisperwind","npc:sentinel-thenysil","quest:1082","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","zone:stonetalon","quest:2519"},m={start="Sentinel Thenysil",["end"]="Tyrande Whisperwind",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1081},src={"Reception from Tyrande"}}
E["quest:1082"] = {t="quest",n="Update for Sentinel Thenysil",z="stonetalon",s="Word of relief travels from Stonetalon to Astranaar. After helping Kaela Shadowspear and Gaxim Rustfizzle against the Venture Company, you are sent to reassure Sentinel Tara Thenysil that their outpost still holds.",h="Word of relief travels from Stonetalon to Astranaar.",sec={{t="A Dispatch from the Peaks",b="Stonetalon's jagged passes leave the night elf frontier isolated and exposed. The Venture Company cuts down the crags and pollutes the waterways, threatening the outpost where Kaela Shadowspear and the gnome tinkerer Gaxim Rustfizzle serve. With the immediate danger blunted, Kaela sends you northeast across the border into Ashenvale to report that they remain safe.",sp=0},{t="Relief in Astranaar",b="In Astranaar, Sentinel Tara Thenysil watches Ashenvale's interior roads and worries over scouts sent into harsher lands. Word that Kaela and her engineering partner are alive and working to heal the land brings welcome relief. The report shows that, despite dwindling forces and threats on several fronts, cooperation with Alliance allies can slow the destruction.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Thenysil?",a="Tara Thenysil is an officer of the night elf Sentinels stationed in Astranaar, the main Alliance hub in Ashenvale. She keeps watch on scouts and patrols sent into the surrounding wilds and nearby regions.",al={"sentinel thenysil","tara thenysil","thenysil astranaar"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Kaela Shadowspear in Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Kaela Shadowspear was sent to Stonetalon to oppose the Venture Company's destructive exploitation of the land. She works with the gnome Gaxim Rustfizzle to sabotage goblin machinery and restore the land.",al={"kaela shadowspear","kaela mission","why is kaela in stonetalon"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Gaxim?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an Alliance gnome engineer stationed with Kaela Shadowspear in Stonetalon. His noisy trade clashes with traditional elven ways, but his skill helps disrupt goblin logging machinery.",al={"gaxim","gaxim rustfizzle","the gnome with kaela"},it="people"},{q="Where do I find Sentinel Thenysil?",a="Sentinel Thenysil is in Astranaar, along Ashenvale's central road, northeast of the path down from the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"where is thenysil","thenysil location","where is astranaar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting back to Sentinel Thenysil?",a="Reporting success in Stonetalon to Sentinel Thenysil opens further opportunities within the night elf military and leads to higher-level communications with Darnassus leadership.",al={"next quest after thenysil","where do i go next","reception from tyrande"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Venture Company a threat in Stonetalon?",a="The Venture Company clear-cuts sacred groves, runs massive logging machinery, and poisons Stonetalon's waterways, threatening the natural balance guarded by the night elves.",al={"venture co stonetalon","why fight venture co"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Kaela Shadowspear want this update delivered?",a="Operating deep within the contested Stonetalon Mountains, Kaela and Gaxim have been cut off while working to stop the Venture Company's environmental devastation. Kaela needs word carried back to Astranaar so the Sentinel leadership knows their mission is alive and succeeding, rather than lost to the wilderness or goblin machinery.",al={"why send update to thenysil","kaela shadowspear motive","why report to astranaar"},it="motive",add="be49c188"},{q="Why does Kaela send you instead of going herself?",a="Kaela and Gaxim cannot abandon their post. The Venture Company's deforestation and mining operations pose an active and immediate threat to the Crag and the surrounding peaks. Leaving now would surrender the hard-won ground you just helped secure, so they rely on an able traveler like you to carry the message north.",al={"why not send a sentinel","why can't kaela report back","why does kaela need me"},it="why_me",add="9e9209a2"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can reassure the Sentinels that Kaela survived and their hold over Kalimdor's borderlands has not broken under industrial pressure.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can take pride that even Sentinel Thenysil is relieved Gaxim Rustfizzle is safe. Gnomish ingenuity can earn respect among traditionalist elves.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help keep communication open between Stonetalon's frontier posts and Ashenvale's strongholds, securing the Alliance presence in central Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","gaxim rustfizzle","kaela shadowspear","sentinel thenysil","stonetalon","update for sentinel thenysil","venture co"},rel={"npc:sentinel-thenysil","npc:kaela-shadowspear","subzone:astranaar","quest:1081","quest:764","zone:stonetalon","zone:ashenvale","topic:sentinels"},m={start="Kaela Shadowspear",["end"]="Sentinel Thenysil",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1082},src={"Update for Sentinel Thenysil"}}
E["quest:1083"] = {t="quest",n="Enraged Spirits",z="stonetalon",s="In the Charred Vale, spirits of flame and stone rage after the Venture Company’s destruction. Fire and heavy machinery laid waste to the basin, and the freed elementals overran it. Alliance champions are asked to quell them so the wounded land may heal under Elune’s grace.",h="In the Charred Vale, spirits of flame and stone rage after the Venture Company’s destruction.",sec={{t="A Scorched Tragedy",b="The Charred Vale was once a lush haven in Stonetalon. The Venture Company’s greed turned it to ash as goblins drove to log the forest and strip its resources. They used incendiary devices and heavy machinery, setting the canopy ablaze. Their actions destroyed the trees and shattered the fragile elemental balance beneath the earth.",sp=0},{t="Unleashed Fury",b="The Venture Company’s work stirred ancient spirits of fire, stone, and fury from the depths. The enraged elementals turned on the goblins, drove them back, and claimed the smoldering crater. Kaela Shadowspear says nature cannot begin to recover while these chaotic elementals remain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Enraged Spirits?",a="Kaela Shadowspear, a night elf sentinel in the Stonetalon Mountains, gives this charge to Alliance adventurers seeking to aid the land.",al={"quest giver","where to get enraged spirits","who starts enraged spirits"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the fire elementals rampaging in the Charred Vale?",a="The Venture Company clear-cut and burned the forest with destructive machinery. Their methods disrupted the earth and freed dormant spirits of flame, stone, and rage, which overran the area.",al={"why are there elementals here","what caused the fire elementals","charred vale fire spirits"},it="origin"},{q="What happened to the Venture Company in the Charred Vale?",a="The goblins set the forest ablaze, and their actions unleashed elementals more dangerous than they expected. The furious beings overwhelmed their operations, leaving ruined camps and blazing wreckage.",al={"venture co fate","did goblins die in charred vale","venture co charred vale"},it="history"},{q="What are Smoldering Embers?",a="Smoldering Embers are burning remnants collected from fire elementals destroyed in the Charred Vale. They are brought to Kaela Shadowspear as proof that the elementals have been culled.",al={"smoldering embers lore","what are embers for","embers of enraged spirits"},it="item"},{q="Can the Charred Vale ever recover?",a="Kaela Shadowspear believes the land cannot recover or feel Elune’s blessing while hostile elementals roam the ashes. Removing them is the first step toward healing.",al={"will charred vale heal","healing the charred vale","can the vale be saved"},it="today"},{q="Where is the Charred Vale located?",a="The Charred Vale lies in the southwestern Stonetalon Mountains, among blackened earth, burned timber, and roaming elemental spirits.",al={"charred vale location","how to find charred vale","where are the elementals"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Kaela Shadowspear want the enraged spirits culled?",a="The devastation of the Charred Vale breaks Kaela Shadowspear's heart. The reckless defilement unleashed violent burning spirits of flame, stone, and rage across the land. As a night elf, she believes the scarred earth has no hope of receiving Elune's grace or beginning to heal as long as these chaotic elemental forces roam free. Culling them is the first step toward restoring peace to the wounded vale.",al={"why cull the spirits","kaela shadowspear motive","why does kaela want this done"},it="motive",add="db30736e"},{q="What creatures are you fighting in the Charred Vale?",a="You are hunting the burning spirits—elementals born of fire, molten stone, and raw fury—that now haunt the scorched wasteland of the Charred Vale. Awakened and agitated when the Venture Company set the woodlands ablaze and tore the earth apart with machinery, these hostile entities violently overrun the ruins and attack anyone who dares approach.",al={"charred vale elementals","what are the burning spirits","who am i fighting enraged spirits"},it="target",add="3905caa9"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the Charred Vale’s devastation as a heartbreaking wound to Kalimdor’s sacred wildlands, inflicted by unchecked industrial greed.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the rampaging fire elementals as a grave disruption of nature’s balance. Active intervention is needed before life can return to the soil.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know the elementals’ wrath is an agonizing reaction to mortal miners and loggers recklessly exploiting the earth.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you work through night elf sentinels in Stonetalon to contain the chaos caused by goblin cartels and restore safety to the mountain passes."},kw={"charred vale","elune","enraged spirits","fire elementals","kaela shadowspear","smoldering embers","stonetalon mountains","venture co"},rel={"subzone:charred-vale","npc:kaela-shadowspear","quest:764","zone:stonetalon","topic:elune"},m={start="Kaela Shadowspear",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=1083,ri={"Smoldering Embers"}},src={"Enraged Spirits"}}
E["quest:1084"] = {t="quest",n="Wounded Ancients",z="stonetalon",s="In the Stonetalon Mountains, the treants have turned against the land they once guarded. Kaela Shadowspear suspects goblin munitions are to blame and asks you to recover shrapnel from the corrupted guardians for Gaxim Rustfizzle to examine.",h="In the Stonetalon Mountains, the treants have turned against the land they once guarded.",sec={{t="Blighted Protectors",b="The treants once guarded the groves of Stonetalon, gentle yet fierce, bound to the health of the land. When the Venture Company arrived with buzzsaws, explosives, and strip-mining, the forest fought back. The treants drove the invaders from parts of the vale, but their victory came at a cost. They did not return to their peaceful watch. Instead, they became hostile and maddened.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Investigation",b="Kaela Shadowspear, an Alliance scout in the mountains, believes the treants suffer from no natural sickness. Gaxim Rustfizzle, a gnome engineer, suspects the goblins' weapons and chemicals harmed them during the Venture Company's chaotic retreat. He hopes to learn whether Venture Company ordnance is poisoning Stonetalon's ancient protectors by studying corroded shrapnel from the wounded treants.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Wounded Ancients?",a="Kaela Shadowspear, an Alliance scout in the Stonetalon Mountains, offers this work. She watches the growing conflict and harm to the land.",al={"wounded ancients questgiver","who gives wounded ancients","kaela shadowspear quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the treants corrupted?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle suspects Venture Company munitions lodged in the treants during the goblins' chaotic retreat. He believes the weapons are poisoning and maddening the forest guardians.",al={"why are treants mad","stonetalon treants corrupted","treant corruption source"},it="threat"},{q="What item must be retrieved for this task?",a="You need to recover a piece of Corroded Shrapnel from the bark and flesh of the wounded treants wandering the area.",al={"wounded ancients item","corroded shrapnel quest"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is a gnome engineer allied with the Alliance who assists Kaela Shadowspear. He uses his mechanical skill to study Venture Company weapons and how they harm natural life.",al={"gaxim","gnome in stonetalon","gaxim rustfizzle role"},it="allies"},{q="What is the Venture Company's presence in Stonetalon?",a="The Venture Company is a goblin logging and mining syndicate that invaded Stonetalon. It cuts down sacred woodlands and plunders mineral deposits without regard for the land's balance.",al={"venture co stonetalon","why are goblins in stonetalon"},it="conflict"},{q="Does collecting the shrapnel heal the treants?",a="No. The shrapnel is a sample for Gaxim to examine so he can learn the toxin's nature and origin. It does not immediately cure the corrupted guardians.",al={"can you cure treants","do treants recover"}},{q="Why does Kaela Shadowspear want the corroded shrapnel?",a="Kaela is deeply troubled by the corruption warping the protectors of the Charred Vale. After the Venture Company was driven back, the ancient treants were left violent and maddened. She promised Gaxim Rustfizzle she would obtain a sample of the goblins' munitions embedded in the wounded ancients, hoping the gnome can study it and confirm whether the invaders' cruel weaponry is truly responsible for poisoning the land's defenders.",al={"kaela shadowspear motive","why help treants stonetalon","why does kaela want shrapnel"},it="motive",add="6c6333aa"},{q="What is the Corroded Shrapnel?",a="Corroded Shrapnel consists of jagged metal fragments fired into the treants by the retreating Venture Company. Gaxim Rustfizzle suspects the toxic or explosive residue clinging to the iron caused the ancients' tragic descent into madness. Kaela needs the specimen brought back so Gaxim can examine its chemical composition and devise a way forward.",al={"what is corroded shrapnel","corroded shrapnel stonetalon","shrapnel lore"},it="item",add="4feb3a85"},{q="Why are you sent against the wounded treants?",a="The wounded treants were once peaceful guardians of the Charred Vale before the Venture Company's logging operations and warfare devastated the valley. During their retreat, the goblins struck the defenders with foul munitions, leaving them scarred, maddened, and hostile to anyone who draws near. To recover the shrapnel lodged in their bark, you must confront these agonizingly corrupted creatures.",al={"why kill wounded treants","who are the wounded ancients","charred vale treants"},it="target",add="2aa0bc4f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a Kaldorei sworn to protect Kalimdor's wilds, seeing ancient woodland guardians twisted by goblin industry is an outrage.",["race:Gnome"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle shows how mechanical skill can help uncover and understand the harm caused by reckless engineers.",["class:Druid"]="Treants carry nature's life within them. Removing the foreign metal poisoning their flesh is a grim necessity as you confront the Venture Company's destruction.",["profession:Engineering"]="The corroded metal in the treants reveals the careless work behind Venture Company munitions beside the precision of gnomish craft."},kw={"corroded shrapnel","corruption","gaxim rustfizzle","kaela shadowspear","stonetalon","treants","venture co","wounded ancients"},rel={"npc:kaela-shadowspear","zone:stonetalon","quest:764","topic:gnome","topic:goblin"},m={start="Kaela Shadowspear",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1084,ri={"Corroded Shrapnel"}},src={"Wounded Ancients"}}
E["quest:1085"] = {t="quest",n="On Guard in Stonetalon",z="stonetalon",s="At a camp near Windshear Crag, Kaela Shadowspear sends Alliance travelers to Gaxim Rustfizzle for help against the Venture Company. The cautious night elf sentinel and eccentric gnome tinkerer join forces to guard the mountain pass from the company's rampant despoilment.",h="At a camp near Windshear Crag, Kaela Shadowspear sends Alliance travelers to Gaxim Rustfizzle for help...",sec={{t="An Unlikely Alliance",b="In the crags of Stonetalon Mountains, the rapacious Venture Company cuts into wilderness and fells ancient trees. Kaela Shadowspear, a night elf sentinel, sees that martial skill alone cannot stop its industrialized pillaging. She turns to gnome ingenuity, though night elves and gnomes rarely agree on technology or the natural world. Their unlikely alliance shows how precarious the struggle has become.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Philosophy",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle brings the eccentric pragmatism of the Alliance's smaller allies. Night elf society turned away from arcane excess millennia ago, but Gaxim believes that abstaining from magic and technical innovation leaves the night elves vulnerable. He hopes to convince his Kaldorei hosts that practical science can defend nature as well as bow and glaive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are a night elf and a gnome working together here?",a="The Venture Company's deforestation and resource extraction in Stonetalon have become so severe that Kaela Shadowspear accepts outside aid. Gaxim brings engineering and alchemical expertise the night elves typically lack, offering technical support against modern industrial machinery.",al={"why is gaxim with kaela","kaela and gaxim","gnome night elf alliance"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an adventurous gnome engineer and tinkerer at a camp near Windshear Crag. He believes abstaining from arcane magic leaves night elves at a disadvantage, and seeks to prove that engineering, alchemy, and controlled magic together can answer dire threats.",al={"gaxim rustfizzle lore","who is gaxim","gnome at stonetalon peak"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Kaela Shadowspear?",a="Kaela Shadowspear is a night elf sentinel charged with watch and defense over the Stonetalon Mountains. As a regional commander, she coordinates resistance against the Venture Company.",al={"kaela shadowspear","who is kaela"},it="identity"},{q="What threat is the Venture Company posing in Stonetalon?",a="The Venture Company is an unscrupulous mercantile syndicate cutting sacred forests, running destructive drilling rigs, and polluting Stonetalon's pristine lands for rapid commercial profit.",al={"venture co stonetalon","why fight venture co"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Tara, mentioned by Kaela?",a="Tara is Sentinel Tara Thenysil, Kaela's friend in Astranaar, who sent you to check on her. Kaela is proud that Tara is doing well enough among the Sentinels to send adventurers on errands.",al={"tara stonetalon","send you back to tara"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this task lead next?",a="After you speak with Gaxim Rustfizzle, he offers 'A Gnome's Respite' and asks for your aid holding back the Venture Company's loggers in Windshear Crag while he plans his next inventions.",al={"quest after on guard in stonetalon","next quest after gaxim"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Kaela Shadowspear want you to speak with Gaxim?",a="The Venture Company has severely devastated Stonetalon, consuming nearly all of Kaela's time and attention in an effort to curb their destruction. Desperate for assistance, she has set aside traditional night elf reluctance to ally with the gnome engineer Gaxim Rustfizzle. To mount an effective resistance and safeguard the mountains, she needs you to coordinate directly with Gaxim and lend your strength to their combined efforts.",al={"why talk to gaxim","kaela shadowspear motive","why does kaela send you to gaxim"},it="motive",add="6de32c22"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see Gaxim Rustfizzle put gnomish ingenuity to work in Kalimdor, where science, engineering, and magic can meet the region's challenges.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may feel pride give way when Kaldorei sentinels trust a gnome tinkerer who favors engineering and magic. The Venture Company's logging has become devastating.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how engineering helps with frontline reconnaissance and ecosystem defense. Cogwheels can aid conservation when turned against unchecked exploitation.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Eastern Kingdoms expertise join Kalimdor sentinels against threats shared across the frontier."},kw={"engineering","gaxim rustfizzle","gnome","kaela shadowspear","night elf","stonetalon","stonetalon peak","venture co"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","npc:kaela-shadowspear","quest:1071","quest:1070","quest:764","zone:stonetalon","topic:gnome","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Kaela Shadowspear",["end"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1085},src={"On Guard in Stonetalon (2)"}}
E["quest:1086"] = {t="quest",n="The Flying Machine Airport",z="stonetalon",s="Apothecary Zamah sends you to silence The Flying Machine Airport above Stonetalon. Carry her Toxic Fogger into the Venture Company’s logging grounds and strike at the cartel’s link to the outside world.",h="Apothecary Zamah sends you to silence The Flying Machine Airport above Stonetalon.",sec={{t="A Silent Delivery",b="Apothecary Zamah prepares Apothecary Lydon’s toxin for the Venture Company. The tauren seek to protect Stonetalon from deforestation and ravaging machinery, while the Forsaken answer with a different approach. Zamah targets the cartel’s connection beyond the mountains instead of its foot soldiers or loggers. A rumored copter pad carries light cargo and messages between Stonetalon and distant corporate offices.",sp=0},{t="Cragpool's Sky Port",b="The Venture Company’s copter pad sits high in the Cragpool Lake area, south of the great waterwheel. The small platform serves lightweight flying machines, not massive zeppelins. You are sent to set off the Toxic Fogger there, filling the pad with toxic vapor before a pilot, courier, or mechanic can alert the company’s commanders.",sp=0},{t="Forsaken Pragmatism",b="Apothecary Zamah makes no apology for using chemical warfare against the goblins. She believes the Venture Company deserves worse for what it does to the land. Her lesson from Undercity doctrine is plain: the Horde must not shy from dark paths when they lead to victory.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the flying machine airport located?",a="The Venture Company copter pad sits in the Cragpool Lake area of the Stonetalon Mountains, south of the massive industrial waterwheel. Its raised wooden platform overlooks the lake’s southern bend.",al={"where is the airport","copter pad location","where is sky port","venture co landing pad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Zamah want this site poisoned?",a="Zamah wants to sever the Venture Company’s communications and light supply lines between Stonetalon and its remote headquarters. She hopes poisoning the pad will cripple goblin flight crews and carry the toxin back to their corporate leaders.",al={"why bomb the airport","why toxic fogger","zamah motive"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Apothecary Zamah?",a="Apothecary Zamah is an emissary of the Royal Apothecary Society, stationed in the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff. She studies Kalimdor’s flora and fauna and develops alchemical weapons for the Forsaken and the Horde.",al={"zamah identity","who is zamah","undead in thunder bluff"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Horde using chemical weapons here?",a="The Forsaken use chemical weapons with ruthless pragmatism. Zamah believes the Venture Company’s destructive greed warrants merciless tactics, while her tauren allies favor spiritual healing and direct defense of the earth. To her, victory matters more than restraint.",al={"horde using plague","why poison goblins","is this plague"},it="purpose"},{q="What kind of aircraft does the Venture Company use here?",a="The Venture Company uses small goblin flying machines and gyro-copters, not full-sized zeppelins. These agile craft carry high-priority messages and cargo over Stonetalon’s rugged mountain passes.",al={"venture co copters","what flying machine","goblin aircraft stonetalon"}},{q="What happens after the fogger is deployed?",a="After you release the fogger atop the pad, you flee before the vapors overtake you. Zamah considers the deployment a success and expects the poison to disrupt goblin logistics.",al={"fogger outcome","after placing fogger"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who are you targeting at the airport and why are they here?",a="You are targeting the Venture Company, a ruthless goblin cartel strip-mining and clear-cutting Stonetalon Mountains for profit. They operate a clandestine sky port to ferry messages and light cargo back to their distant headquarters. By striking their landing pad with Apothecary Zamah's toxic fogger, the Horde aims to cut off their logistical lifeline and spread the poison directly back to their leadership.",al={"venture company airport target","who are we attacking in stonetalon","why is the venture co here"},it="target",add="ee15b44c"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you see the Toxic Fogger as familiar work: Undercity’s alchemical skill can solve problems brute force cannot.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you abhor the Venture Company’s destruction of Stonetalon. Using toxins at a Forsaken apothecary’s urging tests the balance between reverence for the earth-mother and battlefield pragmatism.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see the crude, practical design of the goblin copter pad, built for the Venture Company’s rapid travel across rugged mountains.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help cut off the Venture Company from outside aid. Striking its air transit deals a critical blow to its supply lines."},kw={"airport","apothecary zamah","copter pad","cragpool lake","flying machine","stonetalon","thunder bluff","toxic fogger","venture co"},rel={"quest:1067","quest:853","subzone:cragpool-lake","topic:venture-company","zone:stonetalon","zone:thunderbluff","topic:forsaken","topic:goblin"},m={start="Apothecary Zamah",level="23",faction="Horde",id=1086},src={"The Flying Machine Airport"}}
E["quest:1087"] = {t="quest",n="Cenarius' Legacy",z="stonetalon",s="Near Sun Rock Retreat, Cenarius' Legacy turns Braelyn Firehand's grievance into a call to arms. The blood elf mage says the night elves and Cenarius's children suppress the land's magic. She wants them culled at Stonetalon Peak so raw arcane power can flow freely, while their defeat weakens the Alliance presence in the mountains.",h="Near Sun Rock Retreat, Cenarius' Legacy turns Braelyn Firehand's grievance into a call to arms.",sec={{t="Stifled Currents",b="Braelyn Firehand lives in the hills near Sun Rock Retreat, frustrated by Stonetalon's natural wards. She says the druids of the Cenarion Circle and the offspring of the demigod Cenarius choke the land's arcane currents. To Braelyn, channeling power here is like drawing water with a perforated bucket. She wants to strip away those defenses and let raw magical energy surge freely again.",sp=0},{t="A Strike at Stonetalon Peak",b="Braelyn sends Horde champions north to Stonetalon Peak to break the wardens' hold. Ancient kaldorei groves and temple grounds there are patrolled by Cenarion Botanists and the proud Sons and Daughters of Cenarius. Striking them down would weaken the wards that muffle Braelyn's spellcraft. It would also deal a bloody blow to the night elf enclave that threatens the Horde's foothold in the mountains.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Shadow Council",b="Braelyn Firehand longs to return to Jaedenar, a corrupted stronghold of the Shadow Council hidden in Felwood to the north. Her unseen master forbids her return until her work in Stonetalon is done. The Horde aids her for territorial advantage, often unaware of the sinister cult directing her.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Braelyn Firehand?",a="Braelyn Firehand is a blood elf spellcaster in the crags near Sun Rock Retreat. She accepts the Horde's aid in clearing the night elves from Stonetalon.",al={"braelyn firehand lore","who is the quest giver","braelyn"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Why does Braelyn want the children of Cenarius dead?",a="Braelyn says the druidic magic of the kaldorei botanists and Cenarius's offspring suppresses raw arcane power across the mountains. She wants to eliminate them so the grove's wards weaken and the freed magic flows into her grasp.",al={"why kill sons of cenarius","why hate cenarion botanists","why does braelyn hate them"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the targets located?",a="The Sons of Cenarius, Daughters of Cenarius, and Cenarion Botanists are far to the north at Stonetalon Peak. They guard the ancestral ruins, groves, and moonwells maintained by the night elves.",al={"where are sons of cenarius","stonetalon peak mob locations","where to find cenarion botanists"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is Jaedenar, which Braelyn mentions?",a="Jaedenar is a deep canyon and cave complex in Felwood, heavily corrupted by the Burning Legion. It is the Shadow Council's central base of operations in Kalimdor.",al={"what is jaedenar","braelyn master jaedenar","jaedenar connection"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Horde willing to help Braelyn attack Cenarion defenders?",a="The night elves at Stonetalon Peak are aligned with the Alliance and contest the Horde's expansion through the mountains. Weakening their grove helps secure the region for the Horde, whatever Braelyn's personal motives.",al={"why does horde kill cenarion circle","horde conflict stonetalon peak"},it="side"},{q="What happens after completing Cenarius' Legacy?",a="Afterward, Braelyn's next target is Ordanus, a keeper of the grove at Raynewood Retreat in Ashenvale. He is atop the great tree there.",al={"quest after cenarius legacy","what is next in the chain","ordanus questline"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who are you sent to kill in Cenarius' Legacy?",a="Braelyn sends you against the Sons and Daughters of Cenarius, along with the Cenarion botanists stationed atop Stonetalon Peak. These keepers, dryads, and night elf caretakers tend to the sacred grove and work tirelessly to cultivate the land, shielding the region from the chaotic, burning arcane magic that Braelyn seeks to harness.",al={"cenarius legacy targets","who do you kill cenarius legacy","who are the sons and daughters of cenarius"},it="target",add="9bca5a54"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Tauren druid, killing Cenarius's offspring and Cenarion Circle botanists is a painful divide between faction loyalty and the sacred ways of nature.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may understand the tension between ancient kaldorei wards and free-flowing ley energies. Braelyn's reckless zeal borders on obsession.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Stonetalon Peak is the mountain chain's largest bastion of Alliance and kaldorei strength. Clearing its defenders helps safeguard Sun Rock Retreat and the Greatwood Vale."},kw={"braelyn firehand","cenarion botanist","cenarius' legacy","daughter of cenarius","jaedenar","ordanus","son of cenarius","stonetalon peak","sun rock retreat"},rel={"npc:braelyn-firehand","quest:1088","quest:1089","subzone:stonetalon-peak","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:jaedenar","topic:cenarius","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Braelyn Firehand",level="25",faction="Horde",id=1087},src={"Cenarius' Legacy"}}
E["quest:1088"] = {t="quest",n="Ordanus",z="stonetalon",s="At Sunrock Retreat, Braelyn Firehand uses arcane sight to hunt Keeper Ordanus, an elder son of Cenarius who fled Stonetalon Peak. She believes his people desecrated ancient Highborne ruins, so she sends Horde champions across the border into Ashenvale to take his head.",h="At Sunrock Retreat, Braelyn Firehand uses arcane sight to hunt Keeper Ordanus, an elder son of Cenarius who...",sec={{t="A Hunt Driven by Ancient Grudges",b="Braelyn Firehand came to Stonetalon Mountains on her master's orders to reclaim the sacred ruins of Azshara's ancient temples. She found night elves already at the peak, treating relics of her Highborne forebears as wilderness to be contained. Her chief target, Keeper Ordanus, escaped before she could corner him and crossed into Ashenvale. Braelyn used arcane vision to find his hiding place high in a wooden refuge at Raynewood Retreat, then enlisted the Horde to finish the hunt.",sp=0},{t="The Scion of the Forest God",b="Among Cenarius's sons, Keeper Ordanus is counted as one of the eldest, with deep ties to Kalimdor's wild magics. Night elf guardians moved him from Stonetalon Peak to Raynewood Retreat to shield him from arcane forces encroaching on sacred groves. Loyal Cenarion Vindicators and summoned woodland treants defend him. For Braelyn, the keeper carries the forest demigod's ancient authority and blocks her vengeance.",sp=0},{t="Highborne Vengeance",b="Braelyn Firehand seeks Ordanus's head for a personal grievance as well as her cause. She recalls knowing him centuries ago, when Cenarius's offspring looked down on the Highborne and their mastery of the arcane. Taking his head would avenge those old slights and clear a path for her master's deeper designs in Kalimdor's wilderness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Keeper Ordanus?",a="Keeper Ordanus is a keeper of the grove and one of Cenarius's eldest sons. He was first stationed near Stonetalon Peak, then fled into Ashenvale to escape Highborne vengeance.",al={"ordanus lore","who is ordanus","who is keeper ordanus"},it="target"},{q="Where can Keeper Ordanus be found?",a="Keeper Ordanus lives at the top of a massive hollow tree structure at Raynewood Retreat, along the road through central Ashenvale.",al={"ordanus location","where is ordanus","raynewood retreat tree"},gp=true},{q="Why does Braelyn Firehand want Ordanus dead?",a="Braelyn sees the night elves' presence in Stonetalon as a desecration of ancient Highborne temple ruins. She also hates Ordanus for what she remembers as his arrogance and contempt for her people in ages past.",al={"why kill ordanus","braelyn grudge","why does braelyn want ordanus"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Braelyn Firehand's master?",a="Braelyn says her master sent her to Stonetalon Peak to reclaim Azshara's ancient temple ruins, but she guards the master's exact identity.",al={"braelyn master","who sent braelyn","braelyns master"},it="identity"},{q="How does this conflict fit into the Horde's presence in Stonetalon?",a="Horde forces at Sunrock Retreat often clash with night elf sentinels and Cenarion protectors over territory and resources across Stonetalon and Ashenvale. Braelyn's strike against a Cenarion leader serves both sides' aims.",al={"why does horde help braelyn","stonetalon horde motives"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after Ordanus is slain?",a="After Ordanus dies, Braelyn rewards you and points you toward The Den, where threats across the Stonetalon peaks await.",al={"what next after ordanus","quest after ordanus","the den next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Ordanus' Head for?",a="Braelyn Firehand demands the head of Keeper Ordanus as absolute proof of his demise and to satisfy an ancient grudge. Having once known Ordanus long ago, Braelyn despises the keeper's arrogance and his belief that his kind stood above even the Highborne. Bringing his severed head not only confirms that the night elves' defenses in Ashenvale have suffered a critical blow, but also humbles the son of Cenarius precisely as Braelyn envisioned.",al={"why ordanus head","ordanus head purpose","what does braelyn do with ordanus head"},it="item",add="ec9312c1"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you weaken night elf authority across the Ashenvale-Stonetalon border by striking down an elder son of Cenarius, aiding Horde expansion into contested timberlands.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may see Braelyn Firehand embody the Highborne's unyielding arcane pride and belief in arcane mastery over Cenarion natural philosophy.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid of the Horde, you face a grim choice: take the life of a direct son of Cenarius to fulfill a blood elf's ancient feud."},kw={"ashenvale","braelyn firehand","cenarius","highborne","ordanus","raynewood retreat","stonetalon","sunrock retreat"},rel={"npc:braelyn-firehand","quest:1087","quest:1089","subzone:raynewood-retreat","zone:ashenvale","zone:stonetalon","topic:cenarius","topic:highborne"},m={start="Braelyn Firehand",level="29",faction="Horde",id=1088,ri={"Ordanus' Head"}},src={"Ordanus (quest)"}}
E["quest:1089"] = {t="quest",n="The Den",z="stonetalon",s="Braelyn Firehand sends Horde champions into the Talon Den's hidden barrow chambers to seize the druids' relics. This infiltration campaign reaches its climax as they face layered defenses beneath Stonetalon Peak.",h="Braelyn Firehand sends Horde champions into the Talon Den's hidden barrow chambers to seize the druids'...",sec={{t="Subterranean Secrets",b="High on the Stonetalon Mountains, the Talon Den shelters night elf druids in halls carved deep into living stone. The barrow chambers protect meditating guardians and keep sacred treasures from prying eyes. Knowing the value of what lies within, Braelyn Firehand questions a captured druid to learn how the defenses work.",sp=0},{t="The Layered Locks",b="The druids protect their relics with a chain of locks. A lantern at the barrow entrance hides the Gatekeeper's Key, which opens three caches deeper inside. Those caches hold the Sleepers' Key, the Claw Key, and the Barrow Key. Turning all three carved stones in the central hoard breaks the druidic seals and leaves the ancient items in Horde hands.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Talon Den?",a="The Talon Den is a night elf barrow complex carved into the heights of Stonetalon Peak. Its halls shelter resting druids and guard their sacred relics.",al={"where is talon den","what is the den","stonetalon barrow den"},it="place"},{q="Who orders the infiltration of the Talon Den?",a="Braelyn Firehand, a Sin'dorei operative working alongside the Horde in the Stonetalon Mountains, directs the infiltration. After questioning a captured druid about the sanctuary's defenses, she sends Horde agents toward its hoard.",al={"who gives the den quest","braelyn firehand purpose","who sent me to the den"},it="in_charge"},{q="How do the keys inside the Den work?",a="The primary Gatekeeper's Key lies inside a lantern near the entrance. It opens three caches in the barrow, which hold the Sleepers' Key, the Claw Key, and the Barrow Key. Turning all three carved stones in the hoard dissolves its wards.",al={"how to open talon den hoard","gatekeepers key use","three keys stonetalon"},gp=true},{q="Why are the druids on Stonetalon Peak being targeted?",a="Braelyn Firehand wants the area's flow of magic restored and blames the druids of Stonetalon Peak and the sons of Cenarius for blocking it. She has the druids slain, including their leader Keeper Ordanus, whom she says she once knew, then sends you to strip the Den of its powerful items.",al={"why attack stonetalon druids","horde reason for killing ordanus","why loot the den"},it="conflict"},{q="What is inside the Talon Den Hoard?",a="The Talon Den Hoard holds powerful relics and treasures gathered by the night elf druids. Its wards kept them safe from foreign intrusion until Braelyn coerced the security sequence.",al={"talon den hoard loot lore","what is in the hoard","what did the druids hide"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened right before this quest?",a="Before you break into the Den, Horde adventurers are assigned to investigate the night elf presence in Cenarius' Legacy and assassinate Keeper Ordanus, weakening the defenders' command.",al={"den quest chain","what leads to the den","prerequisites for the den"},it="history"},{q="Why does Braelyn Firehand want the hoard plundered?",a="Braelyn Firehand wants the flow of magic around Stonetalon Peak restored, and she blames the druids and the sons of Cenarius for blocking it. Having seen Keeper Ordanus slain and extracted the secrets of the Den's wards from one of the druids, she sends you to strip the Talon Den of the powerful items they keep hidden there.",al={"braelyn motive","why rob the den","why steal from talon den"},it="motive",add="48aeb852"},{q="What is the Sleepers' Key for?",a="The Sleepers' Key is one of three keys the night elf druids hid to safeguard their most prized relics. Stashed away in a cache deep within the Talon Den, it must be slotted, along with its sister keys, into the ancient stone locking mechanism to unseal the Talon Den Hoard.",al={"sleepers key use","sleepers key purpose","what does sleepers key open"},it="item",add="6c65008b"},{q="What is the Claw Key for?",a="The Claw Key is one of the three keys the Stonetalon druids hid around the Den, kept in a torch-like cache that only the Gatekeeper's Key can open. It serves as the second component of the threefold lock securing the central Talon Den Hoard.",al={"claw key use","claw key purpose","what does claw key open"},it="item",add="1086853e"},{q="What is the Barrow Key for?",a="The Barrow Key is the third piece of the elaborate security scheme devised by the Stonetalon druids. Hidden within a torch cache among the deep roots and barrows, it works in tandem with the Claw and Sleepers' keys to dispel the protective enchantments surrounding the hoard's chest.",al={"barrow key use","barrow key purpose","what does barrow key open"},it="item",add="6ca48c55"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Raiding the Talon Den weakens the night elves' defenses atop Stonetalon Peak, secures the mountain approaches, and puts potent magical relics in Horde hands.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the Talon Den desecrated: the ancient sleep of Cenarion guardians is disturbed, and their ward-locked relics are plundered.",["class:Druid"]="As a tauren druid of the Horde, you face a bitter irony: keys named for Sleepers, Claws, and Barrows turn the barrow defenses against fellow Cenarion keepers.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you rely on keen infiltration and subterfuge to navigate the shadowy halls and lift keys from hidden lanterns and torch brackets."},kw={"barrow key","braelyn firehand","cenarius' legacy","claw key","gatekeeper's key","ordanus","sleepers' key","stonetalon peak","talon den","talon den hoard"},rel={"quest:1088","quest:1087","npc:braelyn-firehand","subzone:stonetalon-peak","zone:stonetalon","topic:druid","topic:cenarius"},m={start="Braelyn Firehand",["end"]="Talon Den Hoard",level="29",faction="Horde",id=1089,ri={"Barrow Key","Claw Key","Sleepers' Key"}},src={"The Den (quest)"}}
E["quest:1090"] = {t="quest",n="Gerenzo's Orders",z="stonetalon",s="At the Venture Company dig site in Stonetalon, Piznik works against his new boss, Gerenzo. The ousted goblin hopes to expose the ore operation by digging a sample while an ally guards him from camp patrols.",h="At the Venture Company dig site in Stonetalon, Piznik works against his new boss, Gerenzo.",sec={{t="Corporate Betrayal in the Crag",b="At Windshear Crag, the Venture Company rewards ruthlessness over loyalty. Piznik once served as second-in-command at the excavation, until Gerenzo seized power, fired supervisor Ziz Fizziks, and sent Piznik back to the mines with a pick. Piznik did not leave. Under Ziz's instructions, he stayed on as an informant, watching Gerenzo's every move and waiting for a chance to strike back at the supervisor who displaced him.",sp=0},{t="Unearthing the Gold-Green Vein",b="Gerenzo's takeover springs from an obsession with a strange gold-green ore in the Stonetalon rock. He believes the mineral is worth an extraordinary sum, and has ordered miners to tear it from the earth in huge quantities. Ziz Fizziks has a mysterious new employer who may pay well for news of the venture. Piznik risks discovery to dig out a sample, relying on an ally to hold off aggressive diggers, vermin, and overseers policing the operation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Piznik?",a="Piznik is a goblin laborer at the Windshear Crag operation in the Stonetalon Mountains. He once ranked second under Ziz Fizziks, but Gerenzo seized control and demoted him to mine labor.",al={"piznik","who is the goblin miner","piznik stonetalon"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Piznik mining this ore secretly?",a="Piznik is secretly gathering a sample of the strange gold-green ore Gerenzo ordered mined in huge quantities. His former boss, Ziz Fizziks, says a new employer will pay well for information about Gerenzo's valuable operation.",al={"why mine ore","mysterious ore","gold green ore"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Gerenzo?",a="Gerenzo is the ruthless Venture Company supervisor who took control of the Stonetalon excavation by firing Ziz Fizziks. He turned company resources toward digging up unfamiliar gold-green ore found throughout the crag.",al={"gerenzo","who is gerenzo","gerenzo venture co"}},{q="Who does Ziz Fizziks work for now?",a="Gerenzo fired Ziz Fizziks, who then allied with new backers interested in monitoring Venture Company activity in the region. Ziz pays operatives and informants like Piznik to sabotage Gerenzo and learn what the company is unearthing.",al={"ziz new boss","who hired ziz","ziz employer"},it="allies"},{q="What attacks Piznik while he digs?",a="Venture Company workers attack Piznik as he digs, including Windshear Tunnel Rats, Windshear Vermin, diggers, geomancers, stonecutters, and overseers.",al={"piznik ambush","who attacks piznik","windshear patrols"},it="threat"},{q="What happens once the sample is mined?",a="After Piznik extracts the ore sample, he gives it to his protector to deliver directly to Ziz Fizziks. He hopes the sample will give Ziz leverage to thwart Gerenzo's plans.",al={"where to take ore","what to do with the sample"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Piznik need your help rather than mining the ore himself?",a="Piznik is watched by Venture Company workers at the dig site. He needs an ally to hold off the patrols while he extracts an ore sample for Ziz Fizziks.",al={"why does piznik need me","why help piznik","why can't piznik mine alone"},it="why_me",add="0d43f256"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The strange gold-green ore found by Venture Company miners in Stonetalon matches neither iron nor tin veins, drawing the interest of prospectors curious about rare minerals.",["faction:Horde"]="The Venture Company's reckless, invasive mining despoils Stonetalon's natural landscape. Monitoring, disrupting, or exploiting the company's operations can aid Horde forces nearby."},kw={"gerenzo","gold-green ore","mysterious ore","piznik","stonetalon mountains","venture company","windshear crag","ziz fizziks"},rel={"npc:piznik","quest:1483","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Piznik",level="22",id=1090},src={"Gerenzo's Orders"}}
E["quest:1091"] = {t="quest",n="Kaela's Update",z="stonetalon",s="Gaxim Rustfizzle sends you back to Kaela Shadowspear with letters taken from the Venture Company. Their contents help the Sentinels follow the goblin cartel's work in Stonetalon.",h="Gaxim Rustfizzle sends you back to Kaela Shadowspear with letters taken from the Venture Company.",sec={{t="A Messenger in the Mountains",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle sends you back to Kaela Shadowspear with captured letters. After you helped the gnome mage uncover Venture Company movements, he gathered correspondence detailing the cartel's operations. Kaela, a night elf Sentinel coordinator near Windshear Crag, is waiting for the letters. Gaxim also wants you to mention how his magic helped the investigation.",sp=0},{t="Eyes of the Sentinels",b="The Sentinels watch Stonetalon's crags with concern. Horde forces contest the lower trails, while the Venture Company cuts trees and mines the land. Its letters give Kaela a look at the cartel's communications and help the Alliance plan its defenses along the ridges.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kaela Shadowspear?",a="Kaela Shadowspear is a night elf Sentinel officer at a camp near Windshear Crag. She oversees scouting and defenses against the Horde and goblin mining companies in the mountains.",al={"kaela shadowspear","who is kaela","kaela stonetalon"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is a gnome mage in the Stonetalon Mountains. He uses magic to investigate and disrupt Venture Company operations, working with the local night elf Sentinels.",al={"gaxim","gaxim rustfizzle","gnome mage stonetalon"},it="identity"},{q="What is in the Venture Company letters?",a="The letters contain Venture Company communications intercepted during operations against its camps. They give Kaela Shadowspear and the Sentinels information about the cartel's local logistics, excavations, and resource stripping.",al={"venture co letters","what are the letters","letters for kaela"},it="item"},{q="Why are the Sentinels concerned about the Venture Company?",a="The Venture Company cuts sacred forests and mines the earth with heavy machinery. The Sentinels see its industrial work as a threat to nature and the sanctity of Stonetalon.",al={"why care about goblins","sentinels venture co","venture company stonetalon"},it="conflict"},{q="Where does this quest start and end?",a="You begin with Gaxim Rustfizzle along the mountain pathways and finish with Kaela Shadowspear at her camp near Windshear Crag.",al={"quest location","turn in kaela update","where is kaela"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does this quest lead to further investigations?",a="Delivering the letters keeps the Sentinels informed about the cartel's activity. Kaela can use that knowledge to plan further military responses and scouting across Stonetalon.",al={"next quest","what comes after kaela update","follow up quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Gaxim Rustfizzle want you to deliver the letters?",a="Gaxim wants to ensure the night elf Sentinels are informed about the Venture Company's plans, but he is equally eager to take credit for the success. He urges you to tell Kaela Shadowspear that the mission succeeded thanks to his magical tinkering.",al={"why deliver letters","gaxim rustfizzle motive","why send letters to kaela"},it="motive",add="94a820b1"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, carrying intercepted Venture Company letters strengthens its fragile foothold in Stonetalon against the cartel's pillaging.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, each scrap of intelligence against the Venture Company helps the Sentinels protect Kalimdor's scarred wilderness from industrial harm.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can take pride in Gaxim Rustfizzle's arcane skill as he makes sure his night elf allies see the value of gnome magic."},kw={"gaxim rustfizzle","kaela shadowspear","kaela's update","letters","sentinels","stonetalon peak","venture co"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","npc:kaela-shadowspear","quest:764","topic:sentinels","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",["end"]="Kaela Shadowspear",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1091},src={"Kaela's Update"}}
E["quest:1092"] = {t="quest",n="Gerenzo's Orders",z="stonetalon",s="Piznik sends Gerenzo's Orders ore sample to Ziz Fizziks, his contact beyond the dig site. The delivery closes a dangerous act of espionage inside the Venture Company workings at Windshear Crag.",h="Piznik sends Gerenzo's Orders ore sample to Ziz Fizziks, his contact beyond the dig site.",sec={{t="A Ticket Out",b="Piznik's cover at Windshear Crag is blown, and he knows he cannot stay with the Venture Company crew. Management in Undermine punishes sabotage within its ranks, so the nervous goblin arranges to slip away and find another employer. Before he goes, he gives an outsider the Unidentified Ore mined under Gerenzo's orders. The specimen must reach its destination without drawing suspicion to Piznik.",sp=0},{t="Corporate Curiosities",b="Ziz Fizziks waits at a secret outpost on the western rim of Windshear Crag. He sees value in the mineral and plans to send it south to Undermine engineers, while quietly keeping a valuable portion for himself. His plan reflects the fierce trade and engineering disputes simmering beneath the Stonetalon Mountains.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Piznik need to flee Windshear Crag?",a="Piznik's cover was blown when the site's overseers caught him secretly mining an ore sample for Ziz. He fears swift retribution when the Venture Company's higher-ups learn of it, so he needs to slip away and find new employment.",al={"why is piznik leaving","piznik runaway","why piznik scared"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Ziz Fizziks?",a="Ziz Fizziks is a goblin operator camped on Windshear Crag's western ridge. He placed Piznik inside the Venture Company to steal corporate intelligence and rare mineral samples.",al={"who is ziz","ziz fizziks role","where is ziz"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Unidentified Ore?",a="The Unidentified Ore is a sample of the mysterious gold-green ore Chief Engineer Gerenzo ordered mined in large amounts. Ziz plans to send it to Undermine engineers and researchers to study its industrial uses.",al={"unidentified ore lore","what is the ore","gerenzo ore"},it="item"},{q="Where can Ziz Fizziks be found?",a="Ziz Fizziks is at a small encampment on the western edge overlooking Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"ziz fizziks location","find ziz","where to turn in gerenzo orders"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens to the ore once Ziz receives it?",a="Ziz plans to send most of the ore sample to Undermine engineers, while secretly keeping a small shard for himself.",al={"what does ziz do with the ore","ziz keep the ore"},it="next_step"},{q="Is Piznik loyal to the Venture Company?",a="Piznik worked for the Venture Company only to serve Ziz's interests. He has no loyalty to the syndicate and fears retribution from its leadership.",al={"piznik faction","is piznik venture co","who does piznik work for"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Piznik have you deliver the ore instead of taking it himself?",a="Piznik cannot leave immediately because he needs time to cover his tracks and clean up the mess left behind before sneaking away from the Venture Company. Since word of the incident will reach his superiors quickly, he entrusts the Unidentified Ore to you so it safely reaches Ziz Fizziks without delay.",al={"why piznik send me","why cant piznik deliver the ore","why me piznik"},it="why_me",add="692a35ea"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The Unidentified Ore mined under Gerenzo's orders shows that the Venture Company's work in Windshear Crag reaches beyond deforestation: it also searches the mountains for unknown subterranean wealth.",["profession:Engineering"]="Goblin engineers in Undermine pay well for unrefined exotic ores that can power volatile new mechanisms and prototypes."},kw={"gerenzo's orders","piznik","stonetalon","undermine","unidentified ore","venture company","windshear crag","ziz fizziks"},rel={"quest:1090","quest:1483","npc:piznik","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Piznik",["end"]="Ziz Fizziks",level="22",faction="Neutral",id=1092},src={"Gerenzo's Orders (2)"}}
E["quest:1093"] = {t="quest",n="Super Reaper 6000",z="stonetalon",s="At Windshear Crag, Ziz Fizziks seeks favor with his new boss, Sputtervalve. He wants the Venture Company’s plans for a great woodcutting machine designed by his rival, Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle.",h="At Windshear Crag, Ziz Fizziks seeks favor with his new boss, Sputtervalve.",sec={{t="Industrial Espionage in Windshear Crag",b="At Windshear Crag, the Venture Trading Company cuts deep into the Stonetalon Mountains to feed its logging operation. Ziz Fizziks, a goblin engineer recently cast out of the company, now works for Sputtervalve. He hopes to prove his worth to his new boss by taking the plans for the company’s massive automated woodcutting machine, the Super Reaper 6000.",sp=0},{t="Goblins vs. Gnomish Engineering",b="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle’s appointment as the Venture Company’s local engineering lead rankles Ziz. The company is mostly goblin-run, yet it put a gnome in charge of its engineering. When the Venture Company machine operators’ schematics reach Ziz, their intricate design leaves him frustrated. He is used to brute force, cheap parts, and volatile combustion, and finds Gerenzo’s careful plans hard to understand.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ziz Fizziks?",a="Ziz Fizziks is a goblin engineer in the Stonetalon Mountains. The Venture Company recently fired him, and Sputtervalve soon hired him. Now Ziz seeks payback against his former employers.",al={"ziz fizziks","who is the quest giver","ziz"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Super Reaper 6000?",a="The Super Reaper 6000 is a huge mechanical woodcutting machine designed for the Venture Company’s logging operation at Windshear Crag.",al={"super reaper 6000","what is the super reaper","what machine is this"},it="threat"},{q="Who designed the Super Reaper 6000?",a="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a gnome tinkerer hired by the Venture Company, designed the Super Reaper 6000. His appointment deeply offends the goblin engineers who once ran the site.",al={"who made the super reaper","who built the machine","gerenzo wrenchwhistle"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Sputtervalve want the blueprints?",a="Sputtervalve wants the Venture Company’s heavy logging technology. Ziz hopes to bring him the plans and prove his usefulness to his new employer.",al={"why steal the plans","sputtervalve blueprints"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are the blueprints found?",a="Venture Company machine operators carry the schematics as they supervise the harvesting machinery in Windshear Crag.",al={"where do i find the plans","who drops the blueprints"},gp=true},{q="Why does Ziz struggle to read the blueprints once retrieved?",a="Ziz struggles with the plans because goblin and gnomish engineering philosophies differ. Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle’s meticulous diagrams are too confusing for Ziz to decipher at a glance.",al={"why cant ziz read the plans","gnome blueprints goblin"},sp=1},{q="Why does Ziz Fizziks want this done?",a="Ziz was recently kicked out of the Venture Company, but Sputtervalve hired him right afterward. By securing the blueprints to the Venture Company's massive new woodcutting machine, Ziz hopes to prove his loyalty to his new employer and convince Sputtervalve to finally put his engineering genius to use.",al={"why does Ziz want the blueprints","Ziz Fizziks motive","why help Sputtervalve"},it="motive",add="1ca65bff"},{q="What are the Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints for?",a="The blueprints detail the inner workings and design of the Super Reaper 6000, an immense woodcutting machine engineered for the Venture Company's logging operations. Sputtervalve wants them stolen to understand the technology, and Ziz needs to study them to deliver on that contract.",al={"what are the blueprints for","Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints purpose","why steal the blueprints"},it="item",add="f1f026be"},{q="Why can't Ziz Fizziks steal the blueprints himself?",a="Ziz is a persona non grata at the Venture Company's logging grounds. Their head engineer, a gnome named Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, has ordered him killed on sight. Walking into the camp himself would mean immediate execution, making a capable adventurer the only viable option for the heist.",al={"why doesn't Ziz steal them","why does Ziz need me","why can't Ziz go"},it="why_me",add="c62989dc"},{q="Who is carrying the Super Reaper blueprints?",a="The Venture Company operators overseeing the logging operation carry the schematics. These workers operate the machinery and direct the clear-cutting efforts in the Cragpool Lake area under Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle's direction, keeping the plans close at hand to manage and maintain the reapers.",al={"who has the blueprints","who do I fight for the blueprints","who carries the super reaper plans"},it="target",add="6f0e6bcb"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Goblin engineering favors speed and rough pragmatism; gnomish design prizes precision and complexity. Their rivalry runs deep.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may recognize why Ziz doubts that a goblin syndicate would trust one of your kind with its flagship machinery. Gerenzo’s technical designs leave him baffled.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the Super Reaper 6000 cutting ancient trees in Stonetalon to feed industrial profit, a stark sign of mortal disregard for nature."},kw={"blueprints","gerenzo wrenchwhistle","sputtervalve","stonetalon mountains","super reaper 6000","venture company","windshear crag","ziz fizziks"},rel={"npc:sputtervalve","quest:1483","quest:1094","topic:venture-company","topic:goblin","topic:gnome","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Ziz Fizziks",level="21",id=1093,ri={"Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints"}},src={"Super Reaper 6000 (quest)"}}
E["quest:1094"] = {t="quest",n="Further Instructions",z="stonetalon",s="Ziz Fizziks sends stolen Venture Company plans from Windshear Crag to Ratchet. The documents may give his rival Sputtervalve an edge.",h="Ziz Fizziks sends stolen Venture Company plans from Windshear Crag to Ratchet.",sec={{t="Corporate Espionage",b="After the Venture Company cast Ziz Fizziks out of its logging operations at Windshear Crag, he took sensitive documents, internal manuals, and technical schematics with him. Bitter over his dismissal, he sealed them in an envelope bound for Ratchet. Among the papers are blueprints for the experimental Super Reaper 6000. Fizziks hopes to find a buyer or ally willing to use what he stole.",sp=0},{t="The Ratchet Connection",b="Sputtervalve, an engineer, waits in the neutral port of Ratchet in the Barrens. He has little affection or trust for Fizziks, but the rivalry with the Venture Company makes the offer hard to refuse. The Steamwheedle-aligned goblins seek ways to weaken their ruthless competitor and eagerly reverse-engineer superior mechanical inventions they encounter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Sealed Envelope?",a="The envelope holds Venture Company documents, technical manuals, and blueprints for the Super Reaper 6000. Ziz Fizziks stole them when he was driven from the company's logging operation.",al={"envelope contents","what is fizziks sending","stolen documents"},it="item"},{q="Who is Sputtervalve?",a="Sputtervalve is a goblin engineer in Ratchet, in the Barrens. He distrusts Ziz Fizziks, but wants to weaken the Venture Company and study its machines.",al={"sputtervalve identity","who is the recipient","ratchet engineer"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Ziz Fizziks working against the Venture Company?",a="The Venture Company drove Fizziks from its ranks in Stonetalon. Bitter and seeking revenge, he began passing its trade secrets to rivals.",al={"why fizziks betrayed venture co","fizziks motive"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Sputtervalve be found?",a="Sputtervalve is in Ratchet, a neutral port town on the eastern coast of the Barrens.",al={"where is sputtervalve","sputtervalve location","find sputtervalve"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does Sputtervalve trust Ziz Fizziks?",a="No. Sputtervalve admits he distrusts Fizziks, but the manuals and blueprints are worth more to him than his wariness of the messenger.",al={"does sputtervalve trust fizziks","fizziks and sputtervalve relationship"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Super Reaper 6000?",a="The Super Reaper 6000 is an advanced industrial shredder the Venture Company developed to clear forests and process lumber quickly. Its blueprints are highly coveted.",al={"super reaper 6000","what is the machine","venture co reaper"}},{q="Why does Ziz Fizziks need an adventurer to deliver the envelope?",a="Ziz Fizziks is in hiding in Stonetalon Mountains after being cast out by the Venture Company. Stripped of his position and surrounded by hostile former colleagues and the dangers of the Crag, he cannot safely make the journey across Kalimdor to Ratchet himself. Entrusting the sensitive blueprints and stolen documents to an able traveler ensures the information reaches Sputtervalve without risking his own neck.",al={"why me further instructions","why does ziz need me","why can't ziz deliver the envelope"},it="why_me",add="98641ea6"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The envelope carries the marks of goblin industry: corporate espionage, patent theft, and reverse-engineering complex lumber harvesters.",["faction:Horde"]="Carrying stolen Venture Company plans to Ratchet feeds trade rivalries that challenge industrial expansion near Horde territory."},kw={"barrens","further instructions","ratchet","sputtervalve","stonetalon","super reaper 6000","venture company","ziz fizziks"},rel={"quest:1093","npc:sputtervalve","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:venture-company","zone:stonetalon","quest:1483"},m={start="Ziz Fizziks",["end"]="Sputtervalve",level="21",id=1094},src={"Further Instructions"}}
E["quest:1095"] = {t="quest",n="Further Instructions",z="stonetalon",s="Sputtervalve carries an order from Undermine to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains. Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, the gnome engineer hired by Mogul Razdunk, must be eliminated.",h="Sputtervalve carries an order from Undermine to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Corporate Disapproval",b="The Venture Company’s hiring of Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle has stirred trouble among Undermine’s rulers. Mogul Razdunk brought the gnome engineer into the company, and word of it reached the Trade Princes. Director Riddlevox told Sputtervalve to intervene quietly. Sputtervalve believes the order comes from the highest trade authorities, so he passes the work to Ziz Fizziks, the operative nearest the scene.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of Dun Morogh",b="Ziz Fizziks welcomes the order to kill Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle. Goblin engineers disdain their gnome rivals, and Gerenzo has a past that makes him especially volatile. Before joining the Venture Company, he was a head engineer in Gnomeregan and worked on a top-secret project that Undermine’s spies could not fully uncover. The project reportedly ended in catastrophe, exploding in the engineers’ faces. Now Gerenzo sells his dangerous expertise to the Venture Company in Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sputtervalve?",a="Sputtervalve is a goblin operative under Director Riddlevox. He carries directives from Undermine and passes contracts to field agents like Ziz Fizziks.",al={"sputtervalve","who gives quest","quest giver sputtervalve"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the Trade Princes care about Gerenzo?",a="The Trade Princes of Undermine disapprove of Mogul Razdunk hiring an outside gnome engineer. They see the hire as a threat to goblin industrial dominance and a source of unwelcome scrutiny.",al={"why do trade princes care","undermine anger","gerenzo trade princes"}},{q="What secret project did Gerenzo work on?",a="Gerenzo worked as a lead engineer on a classified project in Gnomeregan. Goblin spies could not uncover its purpose, and it reportedly ended in disaster, exploding in the engineers’ faces.",al={"gerenzo secret project","gnomeregan explosion","gerenzo past"},it="history"},{q="Where is Ziz Fizziks located?",a="Ziz Fizziks is in the Stonetalon Mountains, watching the Venture Company’s local logging and mining efforts while carrying out corporate contracts.",al={"ziz fizziks location","where is ziz","where to deliver orders"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Ziz Fizziks eager to kill Gerenzo?",a="Ziz Fizziks shares the goblins’ professional hatred of gnomes and sees Gerenzo as a dangerous rival. Gerenzo’s experiments in Dun Morogh ended in disaster.",al={"why ziz hate gerenzo","fizziks reaction","why kill gerenzo"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Mogul Razdunk?",a="Mogul Razdunk leads the Venture Company. He hired Gerenzo, defying trade etiquette in Undermine and prompting the Trade Princes to push for Gerenzo’s elimination.",al={"mogul razdunk","who is razdunk","venture company boss"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Sputtervalve want this done?",a="Sputtervalve received directives straight from Director Riddlevox, who is answering pressure from Undermine's Trade Princes. Mogul Razdunk's decision to hire the gnome Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle has scandalized goblin leadership. To protect his own standing and fulfill his superiors' demands, Sputtervalve must see Gerenzo eliminated, and he views dispatching the orders to Ziz Fizziks as the ideal way to carry out Undermine's will while testing Fizziks's capabilities.",al={"why send orders","sputtervalve motive","why kill gerenzo"},it="motive",add="36e39e8c"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you hear that Gerenzo was a senior engineer in Gnomeregan. His secret experiment ended in a catastrophic explosion that struck the engineers involved.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you see the rivalry between gnome and goblin engineering turn from disputes over design patents to corporate assassination."},kw={"further instructions","gerenzo wrenchwhistle","gnomeregan","razdunk","riddlevox","sputtervalve","stonetalon","undermine","venture company","ziz fizziks"},rel={"quest:1483","quest:1094","npc:sputtervalve","zone:stonetalon","topic:venture-company","zone:gnomeregan","zone:dunmorogh","topic:gnome"},m={start="Sputtervalve",["end"]="Ziz Fizziks",level="27",id=1095},src={"Further Instructions (2)"}}
E["quest:1096"] = {t="quest",n="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle",z="stonetalon",s="High above Cragpool Lake, Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle awaits a bounty in the Stonetalon Mountains. The rogue gnome overseer has replaced much of his decaying flesh with gears, clockwork machinery, and artificial limbs. Ziz Fizziks wants his mechanical arm as proof of his death, hoping it will win him a promotion.",h="High above Cragpool Lake, Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle awaits a bounty in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Monstrous Hybrid",b="Gerenzo’s body bears the marks of his transformations. Those who have seen him say his natural flesh is rotting beneath grafted gears, iron plating, and whirring clockwork limbs. He watches operations from near the great water wheel above Cragpool Lake, with no concern for his failing flesh.",sp=0},{t="Goblin Ambitions",b="Ziz Fizziks works for Sputtervalve and hopes Gerenzo’s fall will carry him out of Stonetalon. Ziz cannot climb the cliffs and defeat the augmented overseer himself, so he asks you to bring back Gerenzo’s mechanical arm. With it, he hopes to prove his worth and earn a transfer to the Tinkers’ Union workshops in Gadgetzan or Undermine.",sp=0},{t="Clashing Philosophies",b="Gerenzo’s mechanical arm reflects a sharp divide between gnome and goblin engineering. He cut away failing flesh to make room for complex prosthetics, a choice goblins find baffling. As Ziz sees it, goblin ingenuity would keep the natural limb and add an explosive third arm beside it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle?",a="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle is a renegade gnome overseer. He replaces parts of his decaying body with gears and mechanical limbs, and watches operations high above Cragpool Lake.",al={"gerenzo","who is gerenzo","gerenzo lore"},it="target"},{q="Where can Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle be found?",a="Gerenzo is northeast of Ziz Fizziks, high above Cragpool Lake near a large industrial water wheel.",al={"gerenzo location","find gerenzo","where is gerenzo"},gp=true},{q="Why does Ziz Fizziks want Gerenzo dead?",a="Sputtervalve has ordered Ziz Fizziks to eliminate Gerenzo. Ziz hopes that proving his competence will earn him a transfer to a Tinkers’ Union workshop in Gadgetzan or Undermine.",al={"why kill gerenzo","ziz motive","ziz fizziks goal"},it="motive"},{q="What proof does Ziz require?",a="Ziz wants Gerenzo’s mechanical arm as proof that the overseer is dead.",al={"what proof","gerenzo proof","quest objective item"},it="item"},{q="Why is Gerenzo partly mechanical?",a="Gerenzo’s flesh was rotting, so he grafted gears, iron plates, and mechanical limbs onto his body to sustain and augment himself.",al={"why is gerenzo a cyborg","gerenzo robot","gerenzo body"}},{q="Who is Sputtervalve?",a="Sputtervalve is a goblin supervisor who oversees operations and directs underlings like Ziz Fizziks from elsewhere in Kalimdor.",al={"sputtervalve","who is sputtervalve"}},{q="Why does Ziz Fizziks need you to deal with Gerenzo?",a="Ziz Fizziks is an engineer, not a frontline fighter. Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle is holed up high above Cragpool Lake, surrounded by the Venture Company's logging operations and machinery. Ziz admits he stands no chance of fighting through the hostile logging site on his own, much less defeating the heavily augmented gnome atop the works. He needs a capable adventurer to cut through the defenses and finish the job.",al={"why me gerenzo","why doesnt ziz kill gerenzo","why hire an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="94dcbf90"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Gerenzo’s mechanical arm shows how far gnomish bionic engineering can go, in sharp contrast with goblin practical design.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, Gerenzo takes eccentric and macabre measures to preserve his failing body with radical self-augmentation.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help goblin contractors in Stonetalon secure resources and territory while disrupting dangerous rogue engineers in the crags."},kw={"cragpool lake","cyborg","gerenzo","mechanical arm","sputtervalve","stonetalon","wrenchwhistle","ziz fizziks"},rel={"npc:sputtervalve","quest:1483","quest:1094","subzone:cragpool-lake","zone:stonetalon","topic:gnome","subzone:gadgetzan"},m={start="Ziz Fizziks",level="27",id=1096,ri={"Gerenzo's Mechanical Arm"}},src={"Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle (quest)"}}
E["quest:1483"] = {t="quest",n="Ziz Fizziks",z="stonetalon",s="On the western ridge of Windshear Crag, Ziz Fizziks has left the Venture Company for the Tinkers' Union. A gnome engineer's arrival drove him away, though his new superior works him just as hard.",h="On the western ridge of Windshear Crag, Ziz Fizziks has left the Venture Company for the Tinkers' Union.",sec={{t="A Matter of Professional Pride",b="The Venture Company brought Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a gnome engineer, into its employ, and Ziz Fizziks took it as an insult. He could not bear working beside a gnomish rival, so he looked for a way out. Ziz contacted Sputtervalve, who represented the Tinkers' Union, and begged for a transfer away from Gerenzo's oversight.",sp=0},{t="Out of the Frying Pan",b="The Tinkers' Union gave Ziz Fizziks a new position, but not the easy life he expected. On the western edge of Windshear Crag, he found that Sputtervalve drove him as hard as any Venture Company foreman. Still, Ziz would rather labor under a demanding goblin superior than share an engineering workshop with a gnome.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ziz Fizziks?",a="Ziz Fizziks is a goblin engineer who once worked for the Venture Company in Stonetalon Mountains. He left after the company hired a gnomish engineer and joined the Tinkers' Union.",al={"who is ziz","ziz fizziks npc","about ziz fizziks"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Ziz Fizziks leave the Venture Company?",a="The Venture Company hired Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a gnome engineer, and Ziz Fizziks refused to work beside him. Ziz begged Sputtervalve for a new position.",al={"why did ziz quit","why leave venture co","ziz venture co"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Ziz Fizziks be found?",a="Ziz Fizziks works along the western edge of Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. From there, he overlooks the Venture Company logging and excavation operations.",al={"ziz fizziks location","where is ziz","find ziz fizziks"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Sputtervalve?",a="Sputtervalve is a goblin operative with the Tinkers' Union. He recruits skilled engineers from the Venture Company to work on competing projects.",al={"who is sputtervalve","sputtervalve role"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle?",a="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle is a gnome engineer hired by the Venture Company to work at Windshear Crag. His arrival outraged Ziz and sparked a fierce professional rivalry.",al={"gerenzo wrenchwhistle","who is the gnome engineer"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Tinkers' Union?",a="The Tinkers' Union is an established goblin engineering trade association. It competes with the Venture Company and recruits or reclaims top talent.",al={"tinkers union","goblin tinkers union"},it="history"},{q="Why does Sputtervalve want you to check on Ziz Fizziks?",a="The Venture Company routinely poaches top goblin talent, but Sputtervalve jumped at the chance to win an engineer back when Ziz quit in protest over the hiring of a gnome rival. Now representing the Tinkers' Union, Sputtervalve put Ziz straight to work out in Windshear Crag. He wants to ensure their newly acquired tinkerer is actually delivering results rather than foundering alone in hostile territory.",al={"why check on ziz fizziks","sputtervalve motive","why send to ziz"},it="motive",add="39c75067"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see the fierce feud between Ziz and Gerenzo in the long-running, volatile rivalry between goblin and gnomish engineering philosophies.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer in Stonetalon Mountains, you may help Tinkers' Union operatives like Sputtervalve and Ziz disrupt the Venture Company's hold on Windshear Crag."},kw={"gerenzo wrenchwhistle","sputtervalve","stonetalon","tinkers union","venture company","windshear crag","ziz fizziks"},rel={"npc:sputtervalve","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","quest:1096","topic:venture-company","topic:goblin","topic:gnome"},m={start="Sputtervalve",["end"]="Ziz Fizziks",level="21",id=1483},src={"Ziz Fizziks (quest)"}}
E["quest:1510"] = {t="quest",n="News of Dogran",z="stonetalon",s="In Stonetalon's foothills, Dogran's life hangs on a healing draught from Malaka'jin. The first runner sent to fetch it never returned, and you travel deep into the foothills to find Ken'zigla, a Darkspear troll.",h="In Stonetalon's foothills, Dogran's life hangs on a healing draught from Malaka'jin.",sec={{t="A Plea Across the Frontier",b="Dogran, a Horde grunt at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens, was badly wounded fighting entrenched quilboar. His fellow grunts brought him back, but his wounds had festered. They feared moving him without first treating him. Taurajo sent word north to the Crossroads for a traditional healing draught made by the jungle trolls of Malaka'jin.",sp=0},{t="Bloodshed at Malaka'jin",b="At Malaka'jin, you learn the first courier sent for the medicine was killed by goblins before he could bring it back. Ken'zigla still has the draught Dogran needs. Getting it means facing the dangers along the Stonetalon passes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dogran and why is he hurt?",a="Dogran is a Horde grunt at Camp Taurajo. He was badly wounded fighting quilboar in the southern Barrens, and his wounds festered until moving him seemed too dangerous without treatment.",al={"who is dogran","why is dogran hurt","dogran story"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Malaka'jin located?",a="Malaka'jin is a Darkspear troll outpost in the rocky base of the Stonetalon Mountains, just beyond the Barrens' northwestern border.",al={"malakajin location","where is malakajin","find ken'zigla"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to the first messenger sent for the draught?",a="Goblins killed the first courier from the Crossroads near Malaka'jin before he could bring back Ken'zigla's draught. Ken'zigla says only that the goblins killed him.",al={"first runner","what happened to the messenger","dead courier"}},{q="Why do warlock trainers care about Dogran's fate?",a="Warlock initiates receive an errand for Blind Cazul and Gazrog under the guise of helping Dogran. The ordeal leads them to an artifact tied to love and heartbreak, needed to summon and bind a succubus.",al={"warlock quest connection","succubus dogran","why warlocks do this"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Who is Ken'zigla?",a="Ken'zigla is a Darkspear troll alchemist and herbalist at Malaka'jin in Stonetalon. He knows how to brew potent wilderness draughts.",al={"who is kenzigla","kenzigla stonetalon","ken'zigla"},it="target"},{q="Why could Dogran not be moved directly to a city?",a="After the fight with the quilboar, Dogran's wounds festered badly. His fellow soldiers feared the rough Barrens roads to a major healer would kill him before he arrived.",al={"why not move dogran","dogran wounds","why camp taurajo left him"}},{q="Why does Gazrog want this done?",a="Gazrog is responsible for coordinating the defense and troops across the Barrens. Dogran was wounded fighting quilboar near Camp Taurajo, and his festering injuries make moving him impossible without aid. With the first messenger sent to Malaka'jin overdue, Gazrog needs you to secure the troll healing draught before Dogran succumbs to his wounds.",al={"gazrog motive","why help dogran gazrog","why send to malakajin"},it="motive",add="643120b9"},{q="Why does Gazrog send an adventurer instead of his own grunts?",a="The Horde's forces in the Barrens are stretched thin holding back constant quilboar raids and securing outpost routes. Gazrog already dispatched one messenger to the Stonetalon foothills who failed to return, leaving him with no spare soldiers to risk on another errand when an able adventurer is right in front of him.",al={"why me news of dogran","why not send a guard gazrog","why gazrog needs me"},it="why_me",add="79033db9"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you face what seems to be a military mercy mission. Cazul and Orgrimmar's warlocks have set a trial that leads you toward the feelings needed to bind a succubus.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see how fragile the supply routes are between Camp Taurajo and the isolated camp at Malaka'jin, with quilboar and goblins threatening the way."},kw={"camp taurajo","dogran","gazrog","ken'zigla","malaka'jin","quilboar","stonetalon"},rel={"quest:1509","quest:1511","npc:gazrog","subzone:malaka-jin","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:stonetalon","npc:cazul","quest:1471"},m={start="Gazrog",["end"]="Ken'zigla",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1510},src={"News of Dogran (2)"}}
E["quest:1511"] = {t="quest",n="Ken'zigla's Draught",z="stonetalon",s="In the Horde warlock chain to summon a succubus, Ken'zigla's Draught is bound for Camp Taurajo. The troll apothecary prepared it in the Stonetalon Mountains to save Dogran, a missing operative.",h="In the Horde warlock chain to summon a succubus, Ken'zigla's Draught is bound for Camp Taurajo.",sec={{t="A Life-Saving Brew",b="Ken'zigla prepared a second dose after trouble with the first courier. The troll apothecary in the Stonetalon Mountains feared the emissary sent to find medicine for the missing scout Dogran had never returned. His draught is volatile and powerful. Half a dose gives a mortally wounded soldier strength to move without making the wounds bleed anew. The rest must wait until the next day, when it completes the recovery.",sp=0},{t="Rendezvous at Camp Taurajo",b="You carry Ken'zigla's draught from the mountains to Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo. Logmar has vital intelligence about Dogran's whereabouts, but foraging expeditions have left his garrison short of grunts. Dogran is trapped and bleeding in hostile territory; the draught's arrival at Taurajo brings a rescue operation close.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Ken'zigla's Draught meant to do?",a="Ken'zigla's draught is a potent medicine meant to revive the injured orc operative Dogran. Given in two doses, the first gives a wounded fighter strength to move without reopening mortal wounds, and the second completes the healing.",al={"what is the draught","kenziglas draught purpose","why make draught"},it="item"},{q="Who is Ken'zigla?",a="Ken'zigla is a troll apothecary in the Stonetalon Mountains. He prepares specialized alchemical mixtures for Horde agents in the region.",al={"kenzigla lore","who is kenzigla"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Grunt Logmar waiting at Camp Taurajo?",a="Grunt Logmar is stationed at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. He tracks local scout movements and holds the last known intelligence about where Dogran disappeared, but lacks the grunts to mount a rescue alone.",al={"who is grunt logmar","logmar taurajo","grunt logmar role"},it="why_here"},{q="How does this quest connect to summoning a succubus?",a="Horde warlocks in Orgrimmar need Dogran's pendant, an artifact suffused with passion and devotion, to summon and bind a succubus. They must find Dogran and save his life with Ken'zigla's draught to secure it.",al={"why succubus quest draught","succubus chain dogran"},it="purpose"},{q="Why didn't the first courier bring the draught?",a="The first messenger sent to Stonetalon never completed the mission. Ken'zigla prepared a backup dose for the next traveler searching for Dogran.",al={"what happened to first messenger","previous courier"},it="history"},{q="Where does the trail go after Camp Taurajo?",a="After receiving the draught, Grunt Logmar directs you to Dogran's captors in the southern Barrens, where the dying scout is held hostage.",al={"where is dogran","next step after logmar"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Ken'zigla want this done?",a="Ken'zigla already prepared the restorative brew anticipating another courier would arrive on Dogran's behalf. As a healer living among the trolls of Malaka'jin in the Stonetalon Mountains, brewing potent remedies is his trade, and he has no desire to see an injured warrior succumb when a simple draught could save him.",al={"kenzigla motive","why make the draught","why does kenzigla help"},it="motive",add="0e638b4a"},{q="Why does Ken'zigla need you to deliver the draught?",a="Ken'zigla is an apothecary stationed at Malaka'jin in the Stonetalon Mountains, far removed from the Barrens. Delivering the brew down through the mountains to Camp Taurajo is a long and perilous trek that he cannot make himself, especially while Dogran's life hangs by a thread.",al={"why send me","why not deliver draught herself","why must player deliver draught"},it="why_me",add="ff24236d"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you must show patience and resourcefulness on this leg of your journey. Before you can command a creature of raw desire and seduction, you must mend the injured mortal who carries the token of binding.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see how isolated outposts in Stonetalon and the Barrens rely on travelers to carry vital messages and medical aid across central Kalimdor."},kw={"barrens","dogran","draught","ken'zigla","logmar","stonetalon","succubus","taurajo"},rel={"npc:grunt-logmar","quest:1509","quest:1515","quest:1512","quest:1471","quest:1472","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Ken'zigla",["end"]="Grunt Logmar",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1511},src={"Ken'zigla's Draught (quest)"}}
E["quest:5881"] = {t="quest",n="Calling in the Reserves",z="stonetalon",s="At Sun Rock Retreat, Calling in the Reserves sends you south to relieve a weary sentry at the Great Lift. Maggran Earthbinder gives you a letter for Grish Longrunner, who has stood watch far from home.",h="At Sun Rock Retreat, Calling in the Reserves sends you south to relieve a weary sentry at the Great Lift.",sec={{t="A Long-Awaited Relief",b="Maggran Earthbinder keeps troop welfare and supplies in hand at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. Across central Kalimdor, the Horde strains to keep its garrisons staffed, even in the years after the Third War. Maggran knows that endless watch duty wears seasoned soldiers down. He sends a reassignment letter south to the Great Lift, where Grish Longrunner has stood guard far from home.",sp=0},{t="Watching the Lift",b="The Great Lift links the high southern Barrens to the canyons of Thousand Needles. When Grish receives Maggran's letter, he can leave his lonely watch over the lift mechanisms and return to his family. Fresh reserves can take his place.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Maggran Earthbinder gives you the letter at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"quest giver","where to get calling in the reserves","maggran earthbinder location"},gp=true},{q="Where do I deliver Maggran's letter?",a="Take Maggran's Reserve Letter south through the Barrens to the Great Lift, on the border above Thousand Needles.",al={"grish longrunner location","where is grish","where is the great lift"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Grish Longrunner need relief?",a="Grish Longrunner has stood alone watch over the lift mechanisms for a long time. He asked to be relieved so he could travel home and visit his family.",al={"grish backstory","why grish leaves","great lift sentry duty"},it="purpose"},{q="Is there any combat required for this quest?",a="No combat is required. You carry a message south toward Thousand Needles.",al={"do i have to fight","peaceful quest","courier task"},gp=true},{q="Which faction gains reputation from completing this?",a="Delivering the letter to Grish grants you reputation with Thunder Bluff, whose tauren oversee the route.",al={"rep reward","what rep does this give","thunder bluff rep"},it="allies",gp=true},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="The delivery brings you to the top of the Great Lift. You can ride it down into the canyons of Thousand Needles and explore more Horde outposts.",al={"next quest","where to go after","thousand needles breadcrumb"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Maggran Earthbinder want this done?",a="Maggran takes pride in the Horde's prosperity and its dedication to rotating and refreshing its soldiers. Grish Longrunner requested leave some time ago to return to his family, and Maggran finally has a reserve warrior prepared to replace him at his remote post atop the Great Lift.",al={"why send the letter","maggran reserve letter purpose","why send relief to grish"},it="motive",add="39c5e94c"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see commanders rotate sentries across the Kalimdor frontier to keep morale and watchposts steady.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you help keep the Great Lift passage open toward Thunder Bluff's wider territories."},kw={"calling in the reserves","great lift","grish longrunner","maggran earthbinder","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","the barrens","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:maggran-earthbinder","npc:grish-longrunner","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:great-lift","zone:stonetalon","zone:barrens","zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde"},m={start="Maggran Earthbinder",["end"]="Grish Longrunner",level="28",faction="Horde",id=5881},src={"Calling in the Reserves"}}
E["quest:6282"] = {t="quest",n="Harpies Threaten",z="stonetalon",s="In the Charred Vale, Bloodfury harpies threaten the routes west of Sun Rock Retreat. Maggran Earthbinder sends Horde warriors to cull their growing ranks and protect travel through Stonetalon.",h="In the Charred Vale, Bloodfury harpies threaten the routes west of Sun Rock Retreat.",sec={{t="Protectors of the Land",b="Tauren at Sun Rock Retreat protect Stonetalon and its peaceful travelers. Maggran Earthbinder, the retreat’s elder leader, has watched the harpy numbers rise. The Bloodfury coven has spread through the scorched Charred Vale, harrying beasts and choking off routes. If their flocks keep growing, Sun Rock Retreat could be isolated.",sp=0},{t="Scouring the Charred Vale",b="The Charred Vale lies west of Sun Rock Retreat, a wasteland of ash, scorched earth, and smoldering trees left by catastrophic fires. Bloodfury harpies nest high in the charred remains of ancient woods and have made the vale their stronghold. Maggran sends Horde warriors into the hostile caldera to cull dozens of harpies: Bloodfury ambushers, slayers, and roguefeathers. Thinning the flock weakens the coven’s immediate grip on the vale and clears the way to confront its matriarchal lineage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Harpies Threaten?",a="Maggran Earthbinder gives the request at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains, near the settlement’s central pool.",al={"quest giver harpies threaten","where to pick up harpies threaten","maggran earthbinder quest"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Where are the Bloodfury harpies located?",a="Bloodfury harpies dwell throughout the Charred Vale, west of Sun Rock Retreat. A mountain path behind the retreat leads down into the vale.",al={"where are bloodfury harpies","bloodfury harpy location","charred vale harpies"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the tauren want the harpies culled?",a="The tauren see themselves as guardians of Stonetalon’s natural balance. Maggran Earthbinder fears the Bloodfuries are spreading aggressively across Kalimdor, attacking innocents and blocking creatures from traveling freely.",al={"why kill harpies","tauren harpy conflict","why maggran hates harpies"},it="motive"},{q="What comes after completing Harpies Threaten?",a="Completing this work unlocks Bloodfury Bloodline, where Maggran Earthbinder sends you to eliminate the Bloodfury coven’s ruling leadership.",al={"next quest harpies threaten","harpies threaten follow up","what after harpies threaten"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is this quest Horde only?",a="Yes. Only Horde members can receive this work at Sun Rock Retreat.",al={"can alliance do harpies threaten","harpies threaten horde only","alliance harpies threaten"},it="side",gp=true},{q="What kinds of harpies must be slain?",a="You must slay seven Bloodfury Harpies, seven Bloodfury Ambushers, seven Bloodfury Slayers, and seven Bloodfury Roguefeathers throughout the Charred Vale.",al={"which harpies to kill","harpy types charred vale","harpies threaten objectives"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who are the Bloodfury harpies and why are they a threat?",a="The Bloodfuries are a vicious coven of harpies infesting the Charred Vale. According to Maggran Earthbinder, they are the driving source behind the surging harpy populations throughout Kalimdor. Their aggressive expansion encroaches upon the surrounding wilderness and traps innocent travelers and wildlife within their boundaries.",al={"bloodfury harpies","who are bloodfuries","why kill bloodfury harpies"},it="target",add="34ac97e1"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, culling the encroaching Bloodfuries is an honorable way to fulfill your ancestral promise to protect Kalimdor’s wilderness.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, clearing the skies over the Charred Vale strengthens your foothold at Sun Rock Retreat against Stonetalon’s dangerous wild factions.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the Bloodfury coven’s twisted presence defiling the Charred Vale’s fragile, fire-ravaged ecology.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you answer Maggran Earthbinder’s call to purge aggressive defilers who upset the natural elemental balance."},kw={"ambushers","bloodfury","charred vale","coven","harpies threaten","maggran earthbinder","roguefeathers","slayers","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat"},rel={"quest:6283","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","npc:maggran-earthbinder","topic:harpy","topic:tauren","zone:stonetalon","quest:6301"},m={start="Maggran Earthbinder",level="26",faction="Horde",id=6282},src={"Harpies Threaten"}}
E["quest:6283"] = {t="quest",n="Bloodfury Bloodline",z="stonetalon",s="In the Charred Vale, Maggran Earthbinder seeks to end the harpies’ hold. He sends you to kill their leader, Bloodfury Ripper, and bring back proof.",h="In the Charred Vale, Maggran Earthbinder seeks to end the harpies’ hold.",sec={{t="Striking the Matron",b="Harpies at the edge of the Charred Vale keep threatening Sun Rock Retreat. Maggran Earthbinder believes their attacks will only end when their matriarch, Bloodfury Ripper, is dead. The flock treats her like a queen, and her leadership gives them the unity and boldness they show along the craggy western ridge.",sp=0},{t="Peace in the Earth",b="Bloodfury Ripper’s remains are the proof Maggran asks you to bring back. With the brood queen gone, the harpies lose their order and become easier to keep at bay, easing the threat to Sun Rock Retreat. Her death also lifts Maggran’s burden of anger and constant watchfulness, leaving him free to seek the harmony and balance the tauren value.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Bloodfury Bloodline?",a="Maggran Earthbinder gives it. He leads Sun Rock Retreat and can be found near its pool of water.",al={"quest giver bloodfury bloodline","who starts bloodfury bloodline","maggran earthbinder quest"},gp=true},{q="What prerequisite must be finished before this hunt unlocks?",a="You must first complete Harpies Threaten, in which Maggran sends you into the Charred Vale to thin the Bloodfury harpies’ ranks.",al={"bloodfury bloodline prequest","prereq for bloodfury bloodline","harpies threaten follow up"},gp=true},{q="Where is Bloodfury Ripper located?",a="Bloodfury Ripper stalks the rocky hills along the northwestern edge of the Charred Vale. Her blue coloring sets her apart from the flock.",al={"where is bloodfury ripper","find bloodfury ripper","bloodfury ripper spawn"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Maggran want Bloodfury Ripper dead?",a="Maggran sees Bloodfury Ripper as the queen guiding the harpies’ fierce expansion into the territory. He believes killing her will break their leadership and weaken their grip on the vale.",al={"why kill bloodfury ripper","harpy leader charred vale lore","maggran earthbinder motive"},it="motive"},{q="How does Bloodfury Ripper's death affect the tauren of Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Bloodfury Ripper’s death gives Maggran peace of mind. Freed from anger and dread of an attack, he can focus on healing the land.",al={"stonetalon harpy threat lore","what happens when bloodfury ripper dies","maggran reaction"},sp=1},{q="What is the quickest path to reach the Charred Vale from Sun Rock Retreat?",a="A mountain trail leads from the back of Sun Rock Retreat straight down into the Charred Vale, avoiding Stonetalon’s winding main roads.",al={"how to get to charred vale from sun rock","sun rock retreat back way","charred vale shortcut"},gp=true},{q="What are Bloodfury Ripper's Remains for?",a="Maggran Earthbinder asks for Bloodfury Ripper's physical remains purely as proof of your deed. Because the harpy queen commands the Bloodfury flock from deep within the Charred Vale, Maggran needs tangible evidence that she has truly fallen before he can rest easy knowing the threat to Sun Rock Retreat has ended.",al={"bloodfury ripper remains purpose","why keep harpy remains","bloodfury remains use"},it="item",add="174da5a4"},{q="Who is Bloodfury Ripper?",a="Bloodfury Ripper is the leader and matriarch of the Bloodfury harpies roosting among the western hills of the Charred Vale. Treated as a queen by her flock, she directs the vicious creatures menacing Stonetalon Mountains, ensuring their aggression persists despite the Horde's efforts to cull their numbers.",al={"who is the bloodfury leader","bloodfury ripper lore","bloodfury queen"},it="target",add="0ac0712d"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Stonetalon’s scarred land pains the tauren. With the violent harpy queen gone, elders like Maggran can turn their thoughts back to harmony and healing.",["faction:Horde"]="Protecting Sun Rock Retreat’s perimeter safeguards the Horde’s lone haven deep in the contested Stonetalon Mountains."},kw={"bloodfury bloodline","bloodfury ripper","charred vale","harpies","maggran earthbinder","stonetalon","sun rock retreat"},rel={"quest:6282","npc:maggran-earthbinder","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","topic:tauren"},m={start="Maggran Earthbinder",level="26",faction="Horde",id=6283,ri={"Bloodfury Ripper's Remains"}},src={"Bloodfury Bloodline"}}
E["quest:6284"] = {t="quest",n="Arachnophobia",z="stonetalon",s="A Horde bounty sends you west of Windshear Crag after Besseleth, the ancient spider haunting southern Stonetalon Mountains. Claim her fang for Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat, and the mountain roads may grow safer for travelers after dark.",h="A Horde bounty sends you west of Windshear Crag after Besseleth, the ancient spider haunting southern...",sec={{t="The Roadside Warning",b="A weathered wanted poster warns travelers on the main road south of Windshear Crag of dangers to the west. Sishir Canyon and Webwinder Path are overrun by spiders. At the heart of the threat is Besseleth, an unusually large orange spider who commands her brood. After sunset, she ambushes anyone who strays from the path.",sp=0},{t="The Earthbinder's Grievance",b="Maggran Earthbinder, a tauren at Sun Rock Retreat, has posted the bounty on Besseleth. He nearly died in an earlier encounter, when her massive two-foot fang struck him. Maggran fought her off and limped to safety, but the wound still reminds him of the danger in the canyon shadows. He hopes an adventurer will bring him Besseleth's Fang and secure the passes, so trade and travel to Sun Rock Retreat can continue without fear.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the quest Arachnophobia begin?",a="Inspect the wanted poster on the west side of the main road in Stonetalon Mountains, just south of the entrance to Windshear Crag.",al={"where to get arachnophobia","wanted poster besseleth location","how to start arachnophobia"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Where can Besseleth be found?",a="Besseleth lairs in Sishir Canyon, west of the roadside wanted poster. She roams the canyon's web-choked ground among her spider offspring.",al={"besseleth location","where is besseleth","find besseleth spider"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who is Maggran Earthbinder?",a="Maggran Earthbinder is a tauren at Sun Rock Retreat in Stonetalon Mountains. He survived a venomous strike from Besseleth and posted the bounty to rid the canyon of her threat.",al={"who is maggran","maggran earthbinder role","who turned in arachnophobia"},it="people"},{q="Why is Besseleth such a threat to the region?",a="Besseleth is an exceptionally large, ruthless spider who stalks Sishir Canyon and nearby Webwinder Path. At night, she and her brood prey on travelers heading toward Sun Rock Retreat.",al={"why kill besseleth","what did besseleth do"},it="threat"},{q="What proof is required to claim the bounty?",a="Slay Besseleth and take one of her enormous two-foot fangs. Bring Besseleth's Fang to Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat to claim the bounty.",al={"besseleth proof","besseleth quest item","what drops from besseleth"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Is this quest available to the Alliance?",a="No. Arachnophobia is exclusive to the Horde, since Maggran Earthbinder at the Horde encampment of Sun Rock Retreat offers the bounty.",al={"can alliance do arachnophobia","alliance arachnophobia quest"},gp=true},{q="Why is a bounty placed on Besseleth?",a="Besseleth and her brood have overrun Sishir Canyon, preying upon innocent travelers who venture along the nearby paths at night. Maggran Earthbinder himself was attacked and wounded by her fangs, barely escaping with his life. He posted the bounty to eliminate the threat so travelers can reach Sun Rock Retreat safely.",al={"why kill besseleth","why does maggran want besseleth dead","besseleth bounty motive"},it="motive",add="28337efe"},{q="What is Besseleth's Fang used for?",a="The fang serves as undeniable physical proof of the giant spider's demise. Maggran Earthbinder requires you to bring back this venomous trophy before he will grant you the bounty reward and declare you a champion of the forest.",al={"besseleths fang purpose","why collect besseleths fang","what is the fang for"},it="item",add="4849c04d"},{q="Why does Maggran Earthbinder need an adventurer to hunt Besseleth?",a="Maggran already attempted to face the great spider himself and was nearly killed, suffering a lingering wound from her venomous bite. Nursing his injuries at Sun Rock Retreat, he posted an open bounty along the road in hopes that a capable hunter could succeed where he failed.",al={"why doesn't maggran kill besseleth","why me arachnophobia","why hire an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="9c85495e"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, clearing out Besseleth helps secure travel to Sun Rock Retreat and protect your foothold in central Stonetalon's crags.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can help Maggran Earthbinder, who bears the painful scar of Besseleth's venom, in his hunt.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking a colossal spider through the shadowed crags of Sishir Canyon tests your skill at stalking in the mountains."},kw={"arachnophobia","besseleth","bounty","maggran earthbinder","sishir canyon","spider","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","webwinder path"},rel={"subzone:sishir-canyon","npc:maggran-earthbinder","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:webwinder-path","zone:stonetalon","subzone:windshear-crag"},m={start="Wanted Poster: Besseleth",["end"]="Maggran Earthbinder",level="21",faction="Horde",id=6284,ri={"Besseleth's Fang"}},src={"Arachnophobia (quest)"}}
E["quest:6301"] = {t="quest",n="Cycle of Rebirth",z="stonetalon",s="At Sun Rock Retreat, Tammra Windfield seeks Gaea seeds to help heal Stonetalon. She asks the Horde to gather the rare seeds from Mirkfallon Lake, hoping to bless them and restore the mountain’s damaged soil.",h="At Sun Rock Retreat, Tammra Windfield seeks Gaea seeds to help heal Stonetalon.",sec={{t="A Scarred Wilderness",b="Stonetalon’s peaks bear wounds from commercial exploitation and regional conflict. Logging and clashes between rival factions have left forests scorched, cut down, or reduced to ash. For the tauren stationed at Sun Rock Retreat, the rapid destruction of the natural world is a grievous wound. Shamans like Tammra Windfield seek the Earthmother’s restorative cycle as they work to mend the land.",sp=0},{t="The Seeds of Mirkfallon",b="Tammra seeks rare Gaea seeds around Mirkfallon Lake, north of Sun Rock Retreat. The lake’s banks nurture sturdy seed pods along the water’s edge. These seeds have a resilience unique to Stonetalon, though danger surrounds the region. Once they are gathered, Tammra channels ancestral shamanistic blessings into each kernel, awakening its power to speed its growth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of collecting Gaea seeds?",a="Gaea seeds have the vitality Tammra Windfield seeks for restoring damaged land. She gathers them to bless with the Earthmother’s power, preparing them to sprout quickly and replenish parts of Stonetalon ruined by industry and war.",al={"why gaea seeds","what are gaea seeds for","cycle of rebirth purpose"},it="item"},{q="Where are the Gaea seeds located?",a="Gaea seeds lie along Mirkfallon Lake’s shoreline, north of Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. They can be found in the dirt near the water’s edge around the lake.",al={"gaea seed location","where to find gaea seeds","mirkfallon lake seeds"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Tammra Windfield?",a="Tammra Windfield is a tauren shaman at Sun Rock Retreat. Logging and wartime conflict have devastated Stonetalon, and she works to heal the land with Earthmother blessings.",al={"who is tammra","tammra windfield lore"},it="identity"},{q="What does Tammra do once the seeds are returned?",a="When Tammra receives the ten Gaea seeds, she chants to infuse them with shamanistic energy and quicken their growth, preparing them for planting in devastated places.",al={"what happens to seeds","turn in cycle of rebirth"},it="next_step"},{q="What quest follows Cycle of Rebirth?",a="Cycle of Rebirth leads to New Life, when the blessed seeds are carried into the devastated Charred Vale to begin restoring plant life.",al={"cycle of rebirth follow up","next quest after cycle of rebirth","what is after cycle of rebirth"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is the land of Stonetalon in need of healing?",a="The Stonetalon Mountains have suffered damage from warfare and extensive clear-cutting by industrial lumber ventures. Scorched wastelands and scarred valleys struggle to regrow naturally.",al={"why is stonetalon ruined","what happened to stonetalon"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Tammra Windfield want Gaea seeds collected?",a="Tammra is deeply pained by the relentless destruction wrought by industrial greed and warfare across the Stonetalon Mountains. Loggers and battle have scarred the landscape, and she believes only the Earthmother's restorative power can heal such deep wounds. By gathering and blessing the seeds, she hopes to renew the natural cycle of rebirth and replenish the broken wilderness.",al={"tammra motive","why collect seeds tammra","tammra windfield reason"},it="motive",add="a7be4203"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Tammra’s work reflects the shamanic calling to mend ecological imbalance. The spirits and the Earthmother can restore what industrial exploitation tears down.",["race:Tauren"]="For the Shu'halo, healing Stonetalon’s wounded soil is a spiritual duty to the Earthmother, answering the damage caused by reckless logging and factional warfare.",["class:Druid"]="Druids may recognize the focus on natural cycles and seed cultivation. Restoring barren earth echoes Cenarion stewardship."},kw={"charred vale","cycle of rebirth","earthmother","gaea seed","mirkfallon lake","new life","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","tammra windfield"},rel={"npc:tammra-windfield","quest:6381","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","subzone:charred-vale","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Tammra Windfield",level="23",faction="Horde",id=6301,ri={"Gaea Seed"}},src={"Cycle of Rebirth"}}
E["quest:6381"] = {t="quest",n="New Life",z="stonetalon",s="Tammra Windfield sends travelers west from Sun Rock Retreat to plant Gaea seeds in the Charred Vale. She hopes the scorched land can begin to heal.",h="Tammra Windfield sends travelers west from Sun Rock Retreat to plant Gaea seeds in the Charred Vale.",sec={{t="Healing the Scorched Earth",b="Tammra Windfield sends you into the Charred Vale, where soot, fire elementals, and harpies haunt the ruined ground. She trusts in the Earth Mother's resilience and asks you to find Gaea Dirt Mounds, where fertile soil survived the fire.",sp=0},{t="A Foothold for the Future",b="Gaea seeds can take root despite the lingering elemental corruption. Their roots form an ecological anchor against decay and invite plants back into the valley. Tammra hopes that, as life reclaims the basin, the fire spirits will settle, the harpies will lose their desolate roost, and the Venture Company's logging will eventually be driven out.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of planting the Gaea seeds?",a="The enchanted Gaea seeds can take root in the Charred Vale's scarred earth and resist corruption. They give plant life a foothold from which the forest can gradually regrow and heal.",al={"why plant seeds","new life purpose","what do gaea seeds do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do I need to go to plant the seeds?",a="Travel west from Sun Rock Retreat into the Charred Vale, where Gaea Dirt Mounds are scattered across the blackened basin.",al={"where is charred vale","where do i plant gaea seeds","seed locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Tammra Windfield?",a="Tammra Windfield is a tauren naturalist who lives in Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. She works to soothe the land's wounded spirits and restore places ravaged by elemental fury and industrial greed.",al={"who gives new life","tammra quest giver","tammra windfield lore"},it="identity"},{q="What threats roam the Charred Vale while planting?",a="Rogue fire elementals stirred by the devastation and aggressive Bloodfury harpies roam the Charred Vale. The harpies nest among the burnt trees.",al={"charred vale enemies","what attacks in charred vale","dangers in charred vale"},it="threat"},{q="What quest comes before New Life?",a="Cycle of Rebirth comes before New Life. You helped Tammra gather the materials needed to prepare the enchanted Gaea seeds.",al={"new life prerequisite","cycle of rebirth quest","what leads to new life"},gp=true},{q="What does Tammra hope will happen to Stonetalon long term?",a="Tammra hopes regrowth will calm the enraged fire elementals, drive away the predatory harpies, and outlast the Venture Company's logging operations. She wants the mountains restored to a lush, peaceful forest.",al={"future of stonetalon","tammra goal","what happens to charred vale"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Gaea Dirt Mound for?",a="These mounds are patches of fertile soil scattered across the otherwise scorched and blackened earth of the Charred Vale. Tammra Windfield needs you to bury the Enchanted Gaea Seeds within them so the seeds can take root, resist the local corruption, and spark new vegetation to slowly reclaim the ruined wasteland.",al={"gaea dirt mound purpose","what are gaea dirt mounds","why plant in dirt mounds"},it="item",add="c43560c5"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren, planting enchanted seeds in scarred soil joins them in communion with the Earth Mother and fulfills their sacred duty to heal wounded lands.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share Tammra's work to renew the Charred Vale and restore nature's delicate balance.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know the agitated fire elementals will never find peace until the battered land begins to heal.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you appreciate the seeds' power to bring thriving vegetation from deadened soil."},kw={"bloodfury harpies","charred vale","cycle of rebirth","dirt mounds","fire elementals","gaea seeds","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","tammra windfield"},rel={"quest:6301","npc:tammra-windfield","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","quest:6282","quest:764"},m={start="Tammra Windfield",level="25",faction="Horde",id=6381,ri={"Gaea Dirt Mound"}},src={"New Life"}}
E["quest:6401"] = {t="quest",n="Kaya's Alive",z="stonetalon",s="In Stonetalon, Kaya Flathoof has survived the Grimtotem attack and reached safety. Makaba Flathoof sends you to Sun Rock Retreat with the news for her worried aunt, Tammra Windfield.",h="In Stonetalon, Kaya Flathoof has survived the Grimtotem attack and reached safety.",sec={{t="A Breath of Relief",b="The Grimtotem strike along Stonetalon's contested trails. After their village fell under attack, young Kaya Flathoof was feared dead or captured by the renegades. Her rescue brings relief amid the fighting between tribes in the crags.",sp=0},{t="Reaching Sun Rock Retreat",b="Makaba Flathoof sends you from Kaya to Sun Rock Retreat with word of her safety. Kaya's aunt, Tammra Windfield, waits there anxiously for news from the trails. Your message brings comfort to the family and keeps the remote Horde outpost connected.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kaya Flathoof?",a="Kaya Flathoof is a young tauren who was separated from her people when rogue Grimtotem forces attacked her settlement in Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who is kaya","kaya flathoof","kaya"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Tammra Windfield?",a="Tammra Windfield is Kaya's aunt, who lives at Sun Rock Retreat in Stonetalon Mountains. She feared her niece had perished in the Grimtotem attack.",al={"tammra windfield","who is tammra","kaya aunt"},it="identity"},{q="Who attacked Kaya's village?",a="Grimtotem forces attacked Kaya's village. The isolationist tauren faction preys on rival tribes and travelers across the mountains.",al={"who attacked kaya","village attack","grimtotem attack"},it="threat"},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="You have just helped Kaya Flathoof flee her captors and return to safety in 'Protect Kaya'.",al={"prerequisite","protect kaya","escort quest"},it="history",gp=true},{q="Where is Sun Rock Retreat located?",a="Sun Rock Retreat lies high in the central Stonetalon Mountains. Follow the main road west through a narrow mountain defile into a sheltered basin.",al={"sun rock retreat location","where is sun rock","find sun rock retreat"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Makaba Flathoof send you instead of going himself?",a="Makaba remains at his camp near Stonetalon's southeastern edge. He sends you to carry news swiftly to his family at Sun Rock Retreat.",al={"why makaba stays","why send me"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Makaba Flathoof want this news delivered?",a="Their village suffered a brutal attack, and the survivors believed young Kaya Flathoof had been lost in the slaughter. Now that she is safe, Makaba wants word sent immediately to relieve the grief of Kaya's aunt, Tammra Windfield, who is waiting anxiously at Sun Rock Retreat without knowing her niece survived.",al={"why send news to tammra","makaba flathoof motive","why deliver the news"},it="motive",add="10e83b92"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="In Stonetalon's contested wilderness, Horde forces are stretched thin. News that survivors are safe helps scattered encampments hold together.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, the Grimtotem threat cuts into a painful rift among the Shu'halo. Keeping innocent family members like Kaya safe matters deeply."},kw={"flathoof","grimtotem","kaya","makaba","protect kaya","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","tammra","tauren","windfield"},rel={"quest:6523","npc:makaba-flathoof","npc:tammra-windfield","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Makaba Flathoof",["end"]="Tammra Windfield",level="18",faction="Horde",id=6401},src={"Kaya's Alive"}}
E["quest:6421"] = {t="quest",n="Boulderslide Ravine",z="stonetalon",s="Kobolds dig furiously for Resonite in Boulderslide Ravine, deep in the Stonetalon Mountains. From Sun Rock Retreat, Mor'rogal sends Horde scouts into the caves for samples, troubled by a growing tension in the earth.",h="Kobolds dig furiously for Resonite in Boulderslide Ravine, deep in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Tension in the Stone",b="At Sun Rock Retreat, Mor'rogal watches the Stonetalon peaks with concern. The earth feels disturbed, with an unnatural agitation rising from the southeast. In Boulderslide Ravine, kobolds have left their usual foraging to dig aggressively for Resonite, a rare mineral found beneath the surface. Mor'rogal sends Horde scouts past the kobolds and into the cave's deepest reaches to learn why they mine with such frenzy. He asks them to bring back raw samples.",sp=0},{t="Awakening the Ancients",b="Raw Resonite crystals hum with ancient Earthen magic. The kobolds have dug into a layer of the deep stone and uncovered an Earthen, one of the primordial stone-beings the Titans shaped to form Kalimdor's subterranean foundations. Their mining has disturbed a relic of primordial history. The tauren must act before the buried being breaks free.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Boulderslide Ravine located?",a="Boulderslide Ravine cuts into the Stonetalon Mountains southeast of Sun Rock Retreat. Its winding caves are overrun with Boulderslide kobolds.",al={"boulderslide ravine location","where is boulderslide ravine","how to find boulderslide ravine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest Boulderslide Ravine?",a="Mor'rogal, a tauren at Sun Rock Retreat, gives the task. Sun Rock Retreat is the main Horde outpost in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who starts boulderslide ravine","quest giver boulderslide ravine","mor'rogal quest"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="What are Resonite Crystals?",a="Resonite is a rare mineral from deep in the Boulderslide cave system. It carries traces of Titan-forged Earthen magic, a sign that the crystals formed near subterranean Earthen relics.",al={"what is resonite","resonite lore","resonite crystals"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Why are the kobolds mining Resonite so frantically?",a="The kobolds found Resonite while digging for shiny ores. Their digging carried them deep beneath the mountains, where they disturbed an ancient Earthen buried in the rock.",al={"why are kobolds mining","boulderslide kobolds goal","kobold plot stonetalon"},sp=1,it="wants"},{q="What is an Earthen according to tauren lore?",a="Mor'rogal's ancient lore calls the Earthen stone-hewn creatures the Titans forged long ago to carve and shape the world's bedrock.",al={"what are earthen","earthen titan connection","who are earthen"},it="history"},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="After finding Earthen magic in the Resonite crystals, Mor'rogal prepares an enchanted countermeasure. He sends you back into the cavern to face the awakened threat.",al={"next quest after boulderslide ravine","what follows boulderslide ravine","boulderslide ravine follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Mor'rogal want this investigated?",a="Mor'rogal senses an uneasy tension brewing in the Stonetalon Mountains and fears an unknown evil stirs beneath the peaks. The kobolds have begun frantically digging out strange Resonite crystals, and Mor'rogal needs samples and reconnaissance from the cavern depths to understand what ancient forces they might be disturbing.",al={"why investigate boulderslide ravine","mor'rogal motive","why does morrogal care"},it="motive",add="574c7326"},{q="Who are you sent against in Boulderslide Ravine?",a="You are sent against the Boulderslide kobolds infesting the ravine southeast of Sun Rock Retreat. Normally mere scavengers, these kobolds have been overtaken by a frantic obsession, tirelessly delving deep underground to mine Resonite ore for reasons that threaten the peace of the crags.",al={"who is in boulderslide ravine","boulderslide ravine enemies","kobolds in boulderslide ravine"},it="target",add="6ccd8309"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren who reveres the Earth Mother, you may see ancient Titan workings beneath the mountains as a dangerous disturbance in Stonetalon's natural balance.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman who listens to the earth, you can sense an unnatural resonance through the rock as kobolds uncover relics of primordial Titan elemental craft.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can tell that the Resonite from Boulderslide is no ordinary ore. Its matrix holds ancient arcane residue left by subterranean builders."},kw={"boulderslide ravine","earthen","kobold","mor'rogal","resonite","resonite crystal","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","titan"},rel={"npc:mor-rogal","quest:6481","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","topic:kobold","topic:titan","zone:thunderbluff"},m={start="Mor'rogal",level="18",faction="Horde",id=6421,ri={"Resonite Crystal"}},src={"Boulderslide Ravine (quest)"}}
E["quest:6461"] = {t="quest",n="Blood Feeders",z="stonetalon",s="In Malaka'jin, Blood Feeders begin with butchered game drawing Deepmoss spiders toward the trolls' camps. Xen'Zilla asks the Horde to drive the predators back from the settlement.",h="In Malaka'jin, Blood Feeders begin with butchered game drawing Deepmoss spiders toward the trolls' camps.",sec={{t="Unwanted Dinner Guests",b="The trolls founded Malaka'jin as a frontier outpost in southeastern Stonetalon Mountains, where they could hunt. The craggy slopes offer plenty of game, but its meat draws nocturnal predators into camp. Deepmoss spiders are aggressive arachnids native to the crags and canyons to the north. Under cover of darkness, they slip in to scavenge the trolls' stores or hunt the hunters themselves.",sp=0},{t="Clearing the Crags",b="Xen'Zilla asks you to track the predators north into the mountain passes. That will help keep Malaka'jin safe and protect its supplies. Deepmoss Creepers and Venomspitters gather thickest around the rocky ravines and webs of Sishir Canyon. Thin their numbers, and the brood will retreat from the settlement. Then the hunters can rest without fearing an ambush from the shadows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Blood Feeders?",a="Xen'Zilla, a Darkspear troll in Malaka'jin in southeastern Stonetalon Mountains, offers the hunting contract to traveling Horde champions.",al={"who gives blood feeders","blood feeders quest giver","xen'zilla quest"},gp=true},{q="Why are the spiders attacking Malaka'jin?",a="The scent of fresh kills and drying meat draws Deepmoss spiders down from the mountain passes at night. The trolls of Malaka'jin hunt local game, and the spiders come to steal provisions and hunt the villagers.",al={"why spiders attack","spider attacks malakajin","why are spiders invading"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the Deepmoss spiders located?",a="Deepmoss Creepers and Venomspitters roam the central passes and crags north of Malaka'jin. They gather especially thickly in the web-strewn ravine of Sishir Canyon.",al={"where are deepmoss spiders","deepmoss creepers location","deepmoss venomspitter location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Malaka'jin?",a="Malaka'jin is a Darkspear troll encampment at the southern entrance to Stonetalon Mountains, near the Barrens border. It is a hunting base and Horde outpost on the frontier.",al={"what is malaka'jin","malakajin lore","troll village stonetalon"},it="place"},{q="Is there a greater threat tied to these spiders?",a="A massive, lethal spider matriarch lives deep in Sishir Canyon among the webs. A warning sign outside the canyon alerts travelers to the danger and urges groups to bring her down.",al={"big spider stonetalon","sishir canyon elite spider","spider matriarch stonetalon"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after the spiders are culled?",a="Culling the Creepers and Venomspitters gives Malaka'jin breathing room. Troll hunters can secure their meat stores and walk their camps at night without constant ambush.",al={"blood feeders aftermath","does malakajin become safe"},it="next_step"},{q="What are the Deepmoss spiders doing in Stonetalon Mountains?",a="The Deepmoss creepers and venomspitters are native arachnids prowling the crags and canyons of the Stonetalon Mountains. Though they have always inhabited the crags, the scent of fresh game brought into Malaka'jin by troll hunters has lured them closer to civilization. Now emboldened, these aggressive predators actively stalk out of the craggy hills to raid the village camps under the cover of darkness.",al={"deepmoss spiders stonetalon","deepmoss creepers venomspitters","why are spiders here"},it="target",add="5b921468"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you share kinship with Malaka'jin's hunters. They strive to carve out self-sufficient territory in Kalimdor's rugged highlands without succumbing to the wilderness.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help safeguard Malaka'jin. The village anchors the Horde's access route into Stonetalon Mountains from the northern Barrens and protects the entire southern pass.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking dangerous predators that out-hunt and harass friendly settlements is natural work for a skilled tracker moving through the crags."},kw={"blood feeders","deepmoss creeper","deepmoss venomspitter","malaka'jin","sishir canyon","spiders","stonetalon","xen'zilla"},rel={"subzone:malaka-jin","zone:stonetalon","subzone:sishir-canyon","quest:6284","topic:troll"},m={start="Xen'Zilla",level="19",faction="Horde",id=6461},src={"Blood Feeders"}}
E["quest:6481"] = {t="quest",n="Earthen Arise",z="stonetalon",s="In Boulderslide Ravine, Mor'rogal finds Goggeroc asleep inside a Resonite cask. The tauren shaman fears what the ancient Earthen could do to Kalimdor, and sends a champion to break the cask and kill Goggeroc before its strength returns.",h="In Boulderslide Ravine, Mor'rogal finds Goggeroc asleep inside a Resonite cask.",sec={{t="A Slumber in Stone",b="Scouts searching Boulderslide Ravine for vermin found a strange relic among the kobolds: a Resonite cask filled with unearthly force. Mor'rogal, a tauren shaman in the Stonetalon Mountains, recognized it as both prison and sanctuary for Goggeroc, a dormant Earthen. These ancient beings of stone can outmatch mortal warriors, and Goggeroc's freedom could threaten the whole region.",sp=0},{t="The Resonite Crystal",b="Mor'rogal fears what Goggeroc could do if awakened at full strength. He alters the mixture of resonite crystals brought to him, infusing them with shamanistic magic. The enchanted crystal can shatter the Resonite cask and shock Goggeroc awake while he is still weak. Horde warriors must then strike down the disoriented titan-forged being before he shakes off centuries of slumber.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Mor'rogal?",a="Mor'rogal is a tauren shaman stationed in the Stonetalon Mountains. He studies disturbances in the region and uses elemental magic to assess the ancient artifacts and threats uncovered by local vermin.",al={"mor rogal","who is questgiver","orc shaman morrogal"},it="identity"},{q="What is an Earthen?",a="Earthen are ancient beings forged from living stone, left behind by the Titans at the world's dawn. They are bound to the earth and possess immense strength. For millennia, they have slept buried across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"what is earthen","earthen lore","who are earthen"},it="people"},{q="Why does Mor'rogal want Goggeroc dead?",a="Mor'rogal fears Goggeroc's strength could bring catastrophe to Stonetalon and all of Kalimdor. He believes the only way to protect the land is to destroy Goggeroc while he is weakened by slumber.",al={"why kill goggeroc","is goggeroc evil","why slay earthen"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Goggeroc located?",a="Goggeroc lies inside a Resonite cask deep in the caves of Boulderslide Ravine, in southeastern Stonetalon Mountains. Boulderslide kobolds dig through the caverns around it.",al={"where is cask","goggeroc location","find resonite cask"},it="target",gp=true},{q="How do you awaken Goggeroc?",a="You use Mor'rogal's Enchanted Resonite Crystal on the Resonite cask in the cave. Its magic breaks the container and forces the sleeping Earthen into the open.",al={"how to summon goggeroc","use enchanted resonite crystal","open cask"},gp=true},{q="What happens after Goggeroc is slain?",a="When you return to Mor'rogal with news of Goggeroc's death, the shaman's dread lifts. He hails you as a hero who averted a great disaster, earning you honor and standing among the Tauren of Thunder Bluff.",al={"quest reward story","morrogal reaction","turn in earthen arise"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Goggeroc and why is he in Stonetalon?",a="Goggeroc is an ancient Earthen, a being of living stone forged by the Titans long ago. Sealed within a Resonite cask deep inside the Boulderslide Ravine cave, he has rested in slumber beneath Stonetalon Mountains. Mor'rogal warns that should an Earthen awaken with full power, his unmatched might would pose a catastrophic threat to Stonetalon and all of Kalimdor. Smashing the cask catches him while still disoriented and weak from his long sleep, granting you the only chance to vanquish him.",al={"who is goggeroc","goggeroc lore","what is goggeroc"},it="target",add="7cc06600"},{q="Why does Mor'rogal need you to defeat Goggeroc instead of facing him himself?",a="Mor'rogal uses his shamanistic powers at Sun Rock Retreat to alter the Resonite crystals you gathered. He sends you back to the cave with the enchanted crystal to open Goggeroc's cask and strike while the Earthen is weakened from his long slumber.",al={"why doesn't mor'rogal fight goggeroc","why me","why send me against goggeroc"},it="why_me",add="9f2ce835"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see Mor'rogal use shamanistic power to alter resonite crystals and disrupt the elemental balance preserving Goggeroc inside the cask.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know Stonetalon as ancestral hunting ground for the tribes of Thunder Bluff. Defeating an ancient destructive being in its peaks protects the land from ruin.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure the faction's presence in Stonetalon's contested crags by defeating Goggeroc, earning the lasting respect of Thunder Bluff's leaders."},kw={"boulderslide ravine","earthen","earthen arise","goggeroc","mor'rogal","resonite cask","shaman","stonetalon mountains"},rel={"npc:mor-rogal","quest:6421","zone:stonetalon","zone:thunderbluff","topic:kobold"},m={start="Mor'rogal",level="20",faction="Horde",id=6481},src={"Earthen Arise"}}
E["quest:6523"] = {t="quest",n="Protect Kaya",z="stonetalon",s="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Kaya Flathoof is found captive among hostile Grimtotem tauren. Horde adventurers guide her along dangerous mountain trails to Camp Aparaje, then bring word of her survival to her anxious father, Makaba Flathoof.",h="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Kaya Flathoof is found captive among hostile Grimtotem tauren.",sec={{t="A Captive in the Crags",b="Kaya Flathoof was captured and held prisoner deep in Grimtotem territory in the Stonetalon Mountains. The tauren clans are divided by bitter rivalries, and few are sharper than the hostility surrounding the Grimtotem. Kaya has escaped captivity, but reaching friendly ground on foot means winding through trails watched by enemies and predators. An armed escort is her best hope of getting through.",sp=0},{t="Flight to Camp Aparaje",b="Camp Aparaje lies in the eastern Stonetalon Mountains, and Kaya knows the way home from there. She aims for the camp, where she can continue on her own. You guide her through paths where ambushes threaten, helping her avoid recapture on the way to safety.",sp=0},{t="A Father's Relief",b="Makaba Flathoof waits near Stonetalon's southeastern border, fearing the worst for his missing daughter. Runners bring confirmation that Kaya reached Camp Aparaje safely. Makaba's despair gives way to gratitude for the champions who stood between his child and her captors.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kaya Flathoof?",a="Kaya Flathoof is a young tauren captured by hostile Grimtotem forces in the Stonetalon Mountains. She depends on passing Horde adventurers to help her escape and reach safe ground.",al={"who is kaya","kaya flathoof lore","kaya"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Kaya need to be escorted?",a="Kaya needs an escort along the trails to Camp Aparaje in eastern Stonetalon, where she knows her way home.",al={"kaya escort destination","where to take kaya","where does kaya go"},it="place"},{q="Who is Makaba Flathoof?",a="Makaba Flathoof is Kaya's father, waiting anxiously near the southeastern entrance to the Stonetalon Mountains. He fears for his missing child until adventurers bring word that she has been rescued.",al={"who is makaba","makaba flathoof lore","kaya's father"},it="people"},{q="Who captured Kaya?",a="Hostile Grimtotem tauren captured Kaya. Their camps and ambushes lie across the crags of Stonetalon.",al={"who took kaya","who kidnapped kaya","kaya kidnappers"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after Kaya reaches Camp Aparaje?",a="Once Kaya reaches Camp Aparaje, she can find her own way home. You then return to Makaba Flathoof with the joyful news that she survived.",al={"after protect kaya","what next after escort","protect kaya follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest available to Alliance players?",a="No. The Flathoof family are peaceful tauren aligned with the Horde, so this rescue is exclusive to Horde adventurers.",al={"can alliance do protect kaya","is kaya horde only"},gp=true},{q="Why does Kaya Flathoof need your protection?",a="Kaya has just broken free from her captors, but she remains trapped behind hostile lines in the mountains. If her captors notice her escape before she reaches safe ground, she will be recaptured or killed. Reaching Camp Aparaje is her only chance to find safety and send word to her father, Makaba, who fears the worst for her survival.",al={"why protect kaya","kaya flathoof motive","why does kaya need escort"},it="motive",add="ee59f589"},{q="Why can't Kaya Flathoof escape on her own?",a="Kaya is weakened, unarmed, and completely surrounded by enemy territory. Without a capable fighter to shield her from roaming patrols while she flees, she cannot safely make the trek down the road toward Camp Aparaje before her absence is discovered.",al={"why does kaya need me","why can't kaya leave alone","why need escort"},it="why_me",add="87bb92ff"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you help a fellow of your kin caught in the Grimtotem clan's aggression.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help keep traveling families safe and reinforce the Horde's hard-won footholds and supply routes in Stonetalon."},kw={"camp aparaje","escort","grimtotem","kaya flathoof","makaba flathoof","protect kaya","stonetalon","tauren"},rel={"quest:6401","npc:makaba-flathoof","subzone:camp-aparaje","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Kaya Flathoof",["end"]="Makaba Flathoof",level="18",faction="Horde",id=6523},src={"Protect Kaya"}}
E["quest:6542"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Kadrak",z="stonetalon",s="At Malaka'jin, Darn Talongrip sends Horde warriors north to Kadrak's watch post. The dispatch carries them from defending Stonetalon's crags to the campaign in Ashenvale, where the Horde holds outposts at Splintertree Post and the Zoram Strand.",h="At Malaka'jin, Darn Talongrip sends Horde warriors north to Kadrak's watch post.",sec={{t="A Call to the Northern Front",b="Darn Talongrip watches the Horde's southern and mountain frontiers from Malaka'jin. The orc sees capable fighters passing through Stonetalon and directs them toward the northern Barrens watch tower. Ashenvale is the greater pressure point, where night elf sentinels clash with Warsong lumber gatherers. The Horde needs fighters there as the struggle over the forest continues.",sp=0},{t="Kadrak's Watch",b="Kadrak oversees Horde troop movements from a watch tower in the northern Barrens, where the savannah meets Ashenvale. The Horde holds outposts at the Zoram Strand in the west and Splintertree Post to the north. Kadrak coordinates supplies, troops, and urgent reports across the contested forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Kadrak from Stonetalon?",a="Darn Talongrip, an orc at the Horde outpost of Malaka'jin in the Stonetalon Mountains, sends capable adventurers toward the forest border.",al={"quest giver report to kadrak","who starts report to kadrak stonetalon","darn talongrip quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Kadrak located?",a="Kadrak is at the northern watch tower in the Barrens, guarding the main road north into Ashenvale.",al={"kadrak location","where is kadrak","find kadrak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde recruiting warriors for Ashenvale?",a="The Horde needs lumber to sustain Orgrimmar and holds fortified positions at the Zoram Strand and Splintertree Post. Night elf resistance means commanders need reinforcements to secure the territory.",al={"why go to ashenvale","horde ashenvale campaign","why fight in ashenvale"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after reporting to Kadrak?",a="Kadrak briefs you on Ashenvale and gives you reports to deliver and collect across the contested outposts in The Warsong Reports.",al={"what next after kadrak","the warsong reports","kadrak follow up quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest different from the Barrens version?",a="Both dispatches send you to Kadrak at the Ashenvale border. One comes from Crossroads in the Barrens, the other from the Stonetalon Mountains, and either leads into the Ashenvale campaign.",al={"barrens vs stonetalon kadrak","two report to kadrak quests","kadrak breadcrumb duplicate"},gp=true},{q="What is the Zoram Strand mentioned in the briefing?",a="The Zoram Strand is a coastal region in northwestern Ashenvale along the Veiled Sea. The Horde holds a fortified beach outpost there to support military movements and secure naval access.",al={"what is zoram strand","zoram strand outpost","ashenvale beach base"},it="place"},{q="Why does Darn Talongrip want you to report to Kadrak?",a="The Horde has recently established an outpost on the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale and needs recruits to defend its new fronts. Darn Talongrip, stationed at Malaka'jin, directs capable adventurers to Kadrak at the northern Barrens watch tower for further orders.",al={"why does darn send me to kadrak","darn talongrip motive","why report to kadrak"},it="motive",add="f0da3cc6"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warrior, you join the Warchief's wider war effort, sent from the frontier into the struggle for Ashenvale's resources.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you enter a campaign vital to the Warsong clan and Durotar's survival. Kadrak's post is a proving ground for young orc warriors.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you travel under the guidance of Horde lookouts like Darn Talongrip. They help travelers cross the mountain borders and keep communication open between bloodhoof lands and the Warchief's northern front."},kw={"ashenvale","barrens","darn talongrip","kadrak","splintertree","stonetalon mountains","warsong reports","zoram strand"},rel={"npc:kadrak","npc:darn-talongrip","quest:6543","zone:ashenvale","zone:stonetalon","subzone:zoram-strand","quest:6541","topic:horde"},m={start="Darn Talongrip",["end"]="Kadrak",level="19",faction="Horde",id=6542},src={"Report to Kadrak (Stonetalon Mountains)"}}
E["quest:6548"] = {t="quest",n="Avenge My Village",z="stonetalon",s="Makaba Flathoof asks Horde travelers to answer the Grimtotem assault on his village in southeastern Stonetalon. He barely survived, cut off from his kin and surrounded by the dead, and now seeks vengeance at the ruffians’ and hired sellswords’ encampment.",h="Makaba Flathoof asks Horde travelers to answer the Grimtotem assault on his village in southeastern...",sec={{t="Blood in the Crags",b="Near the Barrens border, Makaba Flathoof is the lone survivor of a massacre in the red stone passes of Stonetalon. Grimtotem raiders descended without warning and slaughtered nearly everyone in his settlement. Makaba fought back and brought down several attackers, but they drove him into hiding with little more than his life and his wrath.",sp=0},{t="The Grimtotem Menace",b="The Grimtotem have long troubled the tauren tribes united under High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof. Unlike the peaceful nomads of Mulgore, their warbands use ruthless ruffians and opportunistic mercenaries to seize territory and strike isolated settlements. Makaba has no thought of diplomacy or tribal kinship now. Only blood repaid with blood can answer his grief.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gave this quest?",a="Makaba Flathoof is a tauren survivor encamped near the southeastern pass into the Stonetalon Mountains. The Grimtotem clan sacked his nearby village, and he seeks retribution against the raiders.",al={"quest giver","makaba flathoof","who is makaba"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Grimtotem attacking other tauren?",a="The Grimtotem clan rejects unity under the Horde and Cairne Bloodhoof's vision of peace. Fiercely territorial, xenophobic, and aggressive, they raid rival settlements, kill outsiders, and use armed thugs and hired mercenaries to claim regions such as Stonetalon.",al={"why grimtotem hostile","tauren attacking tauren","grimtotem clan lore"},it="conflict"},{q="Where are the Grimtotem attackers located?",a="The Grimtotem ruffians and mercenaries are camped just west of Makaba Flathoof in southeastern Stonetalon, among rocky hills overlooking the pass.",al={"where are the mobs","grimtotem camp location","where to find ruffians"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are the Grimtotem Mercenaries?",a="The Grimtotem Clan hires ruthless fighters and sellswords to strengthen its warbands and terrorize and overrun isolated settlements.",al={"mercenaries","grimtotem sellswords","who are the mercs"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="After you cut down the frontline ruffians and mercenaries, Makaba asks you to strike at the leader behind the massacre, Grundig Darkcloud.",al={"next quest","what follows avenge my village","kill grundig darkcloud"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where was Makaba's village located?",a="Makaba's settlement was an isolated tauren encampment near the border passes of southeastern Stonetalon. The Grimtotem raid wiped it out, leaving Makaba as one of the few known survivors.",al={"flathoof village","where was the village","what village was destroyed"},it="place"},{q="Why does Makaba Flathoof want the Grimtotem killed?",a="Makaba Flathoof seeks vengeance after the Grimtotem Clan launched a brutal raid on his village, slaughtering nearly everyone who lived there. Having lost his home and his people, all that drives him now is retribution against the clan that massacred his family and neighbors.",al={"makaba flathoof motive","why avenge village","why does makaba want revenge"},it="motive",add="ee147ee3"},{q="Who are the Grimtotem targeting this area?",a="You are sent against the Grimtotem Ruffians and Mercenaries encamped to the west. The Grimtotem are an aggressive, isolationist tauren clan known for hostility toward other tribes and the Horde alike, raiding local settlements to expand their foothold in Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"grimtotem ruffians and mercenaries","who are you sent to kill","who attacked makaba village"},it="target",add="2ec07636"},{q="Why does Makaba Flathoof need your help?",a="Makaba fought desperately during the raid and killed as many Grimtotem as he could, but he barely escaped with his own life. Wounded, isolated, and left without allies or village guards to rally, he cannot face the remaining raiders alone.",al={"why cant makaba fight","why ask me","why does makaba need help"},it="why_me",add="bd5303e7"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see how Grimtotem treachery deepens the divide among the shu'halo. Their slaughter of their own kind shows the danger they pose to Cairne's united people.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you depend on open, secure passes between the Barrens and Stonetalon. A rogue Grimtotem band killing travelers and allied villagers threatens the Warchief's supply lines through the mountains."},kw={"avenge my village","grimtotem","grimtotem mercenary","grimtotem ruffian","grundig darkcloud","makaba flathoof","stonetalon mountains"},rel={"npc:makaba-flathoof","quest:6629","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Makaba Flathoof",level="18",faction="Horde",id=6548},src={"Avenge My Village"}}
E["quest:6629"] = {t="quest",n="Kill Grundig Darkcloud",z="stonetalon",s="At Grimtotem Post, Grundig Darkcloud leads the Grimtotem force that sacked Makaba Flathoof's home. After you strike down the ruffians and mercenaries, Makaba sends you after Grundig and his brutes.",h="At Grimtotem Post, Grundig Darkcloud leads the Grimtotem force that sacked Makaba Flathoof's home.",sec={{t="The Butcher of the Path",b="Makaba Flathoof survived the assault on his settlement along the Stonetalon trail, but his grief is still raw. After you prove yourself against Grimtotem foot soldiers, he points you toward Grundig Darkcloud, the one behind the bloodshed. Grundig commands a devoted band of brutes and led the slaughter that leveled the village.",sp=0},{t="Strike at Grimtotem Post",b="Grundig camps at Grimtotem Post, farther up the mountain road to the west. To avenge Makaba's kin and protect the pass from more violence, you climb to the stronghold, fight through Grundig's brutes, and kill him before his raiders can descend on other vulnerable camps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grundig Darkcloud?",a="Grundig Darkcloud is a Grimtotem commander at Grimtotem Post in southeastern Stonetalon Mountains. He led the attack that destroyed Makaba Flathoof's village.",al={"grundig darkcloud","who is grundig","grimtotem leader"},it="target"},{q="Where can Grundig Darkcloud be found?",a="Grundig Darkcloud is at Grimtotem Post, up the mountain trail to the west of Makaba Flathoof's camp near the Barrens border.",al={"grundig location","where is grundig","grimtotem post location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Makaba Flathoof's motive for this task?",a="Makaba Flathoof saw the Grimtotem slaughter his home and clanmates. After you strike down their ruffians and mercenaries, he asks you to kill their leader, Grundig Darkcloud, for retribution.",al={"why kill grundig","makaba story","makaba revenge"},it="motive"},{q="Why are the Grimtotem attacking peaceful settlements here?",a="The Grimtotem despise other tauren tribes, especially those allied with the Horde or following gentler paths. They use ambushes and raids to drive rival clans from lands they want to control.",al={"why grimtotem attack","grimtotem hostility"},it="conflict"},{q="What comes after killing Grundig Darkcloud?",a="After you kill Grundig Darkcloud and his brutes, Makaba Flathoof's vengeance is complete. Makaba can mourn his village knowing justice has been served.",al={"what next after grundig","flathoof chain continuation"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the prerequisite quest for this task?",a="First, complete Avenge My Village, where Makaba Flathoof tests your resolve by sending you against the Grimtotem ruffians and mercenaries camped just to the west.",al={"prereq kill grundig","quest before grundig"},gp=true},{q="Why does Makaba Flathoof need your help instead of fighting Grundig himself?",a="Makaba Flathoof is a lone survivor stranded on the mountain road, devastated by the butchery of his village. Grundig Darkcloud commands Grimtotem Post flanked by a personal vanguard of savage brutes, far too heavily defended for a solitary, wounded tauren to challenge directly. Having seen you cut down the rank-and-file raiders, Makaba places his hope for retribution entirely in your fighting prowess.",al={"why me makaba","why doesn't makaba flathoof fight grundig","why send me kill grundig darkcloud"},it="why_me",add="ce2e4f2e"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see how Grundig's slaughter deepens the discord among your people. The Grimtotem oppose unity under the Horde with cutthroat force.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Stonetalon matters to your advance into Kalimdor. Warlords like Grundig threaten the supply routes between the Barrens and Sun Rock Retreat."},kw={"brute","darkcloud","flathoof","grimtotem","grundig","makaba","post","stonetalon"},rel={"npc:makaba-flathoof","quest:6548","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Makaba Flathoof",level="18",faction="Horde",id=6629},src={"Kill Grundig Darkcloud"}}
E["subzone:blackwolf-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackwolf River",z="stonetalon",s="Blackwolf River runs from Cragpool Lake through Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. The Venture Company's logging and industrial work has fouled its waters.",h="Blackwolf River runs from Cragpool Lake through Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Industrial Runoff",b="Blackwolf River runs through Windshear Crag, fed by Cragpool Lake. Venture Company loggers cut the surrounding woods with heavy machinery and buzzsaws. Sludge, oil, and logging waste drain into the current. The river carries the cost of the company's work through the basin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Blackwolf River start and lead?",a="Blackwolf River flows down from Cragpool Lake through the logged basin of Windshear Crag.",al={"blackwolf river source","where is blackwolf river","blackwolf river location"},it="place"},{q="Why is the river water polluted?",a="The Venture Company logs across Windshear Crag with heavy machinery. Runoff, waste, and clear-cutting drain into the river.",al={"why is blackwolf river dirty","blackwolf river pollution","venture company pollution"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is currently operating along the river?",a="The Venture Company works along the river, harvesting lumber and operating machinery in the valley despite resistance from local wildlife and native inhabitants.",al={"who controls blackwolf river","who is at blackwolf river","enemies near blackwolf river"},it="residents"},{q="What is the history of the Blackwolf River?",a="The Blackwolf River once ran clear through the heart of the Stonetalon Mountains, flowing out from Cragpool Lake across Windshear Crag. That balance shattered when the Venture Company moved heavy industry into the crag. Their aggressive deforestation and mechanized logging quickly poisoned the waterway, turning a pristine mountain stream into a toxic, sludge-choked runoff for goblin industry.",al={"blackwolf river lore","history of blackwolf river","what happened to blackwolf river"},it="history",add="d14d2651"},{q="Is the Blackwolf River dangerous?",a="Yes, both the water and its banks pose serious hazards. The river itself carries toxic industrial runoff from Venture Company logging operations upstream. Furthermore, the surrounding crag is swarming with aggressive Venture Company laborers, loggers, and mechanized shredders fiercely guarding their machinery and clearing timber with no regard for anyone passing through.",al={"is blackwolf river safe","blackwolf river dangers","dangers of blackwolf river"},it="danger",add="476e6164"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see how goblin timber work fouls Blackwolf River, an affront to the Cenarion Circle and those who revere Kalimdor's untamed waters.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see the earth scarred and the waters fouled by outsiders seeking profit. It strengthens your resolve to cleanse Stonetalon of reckless industrial blight."},kw={"blackwolf river","cragpool lake","logging","pollution","stonetalon mountains","venture co","venture company","windshear crag"},rel={"subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:cragpool-lake","topic:venture-company","zone:stonetalon","quest:764"},src={"Blackwolf River"}}
E["subzone:boulderslide-cavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulderslide Cavern",z="stonetalon",s="Boulderslide kobolds dig deep in Boulderslide Cavern, at the far end of Boulderslide Ravine. They search the stone for glowing mineral formations.",h="Boulderslide kobolds dig deep in Boulderslide Cavern, at the far end of Boulderslide Ravine.",sec={{t="The Resonite Dig",b="Boulderslide kobolds have carved a stronghold into the Stonetalon crags. They dig frantically for resonite, a rare purple crystal embedded in the stone. Its glow carries traces of earthen magic, and the kobolds turn fiercely against anyone who approaches their excavation.",sp=0},{t="The Slumbering Giant",b="Goggeroc lies asleep inside a resonite cask deep in Boulderslide Cavern. The kobolds' digging has reached this ancient earthen, and their work around his resting place risks waking him. His primordial stone magic could bring sudden danger to the whole ravine.",sp=1,bt={"q6421.2"}}},faq={{q="What are the kobolds mining here?",a="The kobolds mine resonite, a rare purple crystal embedded in the cavern walls. Faint earthen magic hums through it, and the kobolds guard their stores fiercely.",al={"what is resonite","purple crystals stonetalon","why are kobolds mining"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Goggeroc?",a="Goggeroc is an ancient earthen who sleeps inside a resonite cask deep in the cavern. The kobolds' digging near his resting place risks disturbing his centuries-long slumber.",al={"goggeroc lore","earthen in boulderslide","sleeping giant in cave"},sp=1,it="identity",bt={"q6421.2"}},{q="Where is Boulderslide Cavern located?",a="Boulderslide Cavern lies at the far end of Boulderslide Ravine, in the craggy southern Stonetalon Mountains, just northeast of the path toward the Barrens.",al={"boulderslide cavern location","how to find boulderslide cavern","where is the cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde interested in this cavern?",a="The Horde watches the cavern to curb the aggressive kobolds spreading through the ravine and to study the magical properties of the resonite they mine.",al={"horde quests boulderslide","why send me to boulderslide"},it="motive"},{q="What is Boulderslide Cavern?",a="Boulderslide Cavern is a subterranean mine nestled deep at the end of Boulderslide Ravine in the Stonetalon Mountains. It serves as an active nesting ground and extensive dig site for local kobolds, who relentlessly excavate rare magical resonite crystals from its stony depths.",al={"what is boulderslide cavern","boulderslide cavern lore","about boulderslide cavern"},it="place",add="5c565568"},{q="Who lives in Boulderslide Cavern?",a="The cavern is inhabited entirely by the Boulderslide kobolds. These aggressive subterranean diggers have built their warrens here, working feverishly to extract resonite while violently defending their tunnels from any intruders who dare approach.",al={"who lives in boulderslide cavern","boulderslide cavern inhabitants","who is in boulderslide cavern"},it="residents",add="66cd11c1"},{q="Is Boulderslide Cavern dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely dangerous. The kobolds inside guard their mining operations with their lives and will swarm anyone trespassing in their warrens. Furthermore, their deep excavations have reached ancient relics, including a dormant earthen slumbering deep within the mine.",al={"is boulderslide cavern dangerous","danger boulderslide cavern","boulderslide cavern threats"},it="danger",add="babd5bca"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Boulderslide kobolds tunnel relentlessly through the cavern, seeking glowing veins of magical resonite.",["class:Shaman"]="Resonite and the sleeping earthen Goggeroc both carry primordial earth magic, an echo of the world's ancient stone shapers."},kw={"boulderslide","cavern","earthen","goggeroc","kobold","resonite","stonetalon"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","quest:6421","quest:6481","topic:kobold"},src={"Boulderslide Cavern"}}
E["subzone:boulderslide-ravine"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulderslide Ravine",z="stonetalon",s="Along Webwinder Path, secluded Boulderslide Ravine cuts through the central peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains. The ravine has seen little of the fighting between Horde and Alliance. Its rocky slopes lead toward Boulderslide Cavern, while wild mountain beasts still roam there.",h="Along Webwinder Path, secluded Boulderslide Ravine cuts through the central peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Quiet Mountain Pass",b="Boulderslide Ravine lies off Webwinder Path in the Stonetalon heights. Loggers, night elves, and the Horde battle over timber and sacred glades elsewhere in the region, but military forces rarely disturb this narrow pass. Mountain rams and crag beasts such as Cliff Stormers roam its ledges and sheer stone walls. Prospectors watch the slopes, where rich mineral veins often surface along the way toward the deeper cavern network.",sp=0},{t="Traces in the Stone",b="Across from Boulderslide Cavern's entrance, a small cave overlooks the ravine. Rough torches light its weathered supply barrels and primitive tribal paintings. The crude designs resemble ancient tauren art, suggesting native tribes once traveled through these crags or found temporary shelter here, long before modern conflict reached the mountains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Boulderslide Ravine located?",a="Boulderslide Ravine lies in the Stonetalon Mountains. Follow Webwinder Path into the higher crags to reach it.",al={"boulderslide ravine location","how to get to boulderslide ravine","where is boulderslide ravine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures inhabit Boulderslide Ravine?",a="Mountain rams and crag beasts inhabit the ravine. Cliff Stormers are among the dangerous crag beasts found there.",al={"boulderslide ravine mobs","what is in boulderslide ravine"},it="residents"},{q="What is the abandoned cave across from Boulderslide Cavern?",a="Across from Boulderslide Cavern's entrance, a small cave holds old barrels and burns with torchlight. Tribal pictographs cover its stone walls and resemble tauren art, suggesting local wanderers or hunters once used the shelter.",al={"abandoned cave boulderslide","cave in boulderslide ravine","tauren cave stonetalon"}},{q="Why is Boulderslide Ravine significant?",a="Boulderslide Ravine leads toward Boulderslide Cavern, a subterranean lair deep in the mountains. Its slopes also offer valuable mineral outcroppings to travelers passing through.",al={"what is boulderslide ravine for","boulderslide ravine purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Boulderslide Ravine?",a="Boulderslide Ravine is a rugged canyon nestled in the mountains of Stonetalon, accessed by way of Webwinder Path. It serves primarily as the approach to the deeper Boulderslide Cavern. While war between the Horde and Alliance consumes much of the surrounding peaks, this tucked-away ravine remains largely isolated from the clashes.",al={"what is boulderslide ravine","boulderslide ravine overview","boulderslide ravine lore"},it="place",add="92909b11"},{q="Why is the cave in Boulderslide Ravine abandoned?",a="Opposite the cavern entrance sits a secluded, abandoned shelter lit by crude torches and stocked with old barrels. Its walls bear faded tribal art reminiscent of tauren crafts, suggesting local tribes or wandering hunters once made camp here before vacating the ravine to wild beasts.",al={"why is the cave abandoned","boulderslide abandoned cave","who abandoned the cave"},it="ruin",add="846b0de4"},{q="Is Boulderslide Ravine dangerous?",a="While spared from organized military skirmishes, the ravine is far from safe. Native rams graze along the steep trails, and volatile elemental Cliff Stormers prowl the crags, making careless passage risky for travelers seeking its mining veins or heading toward the cavern.",al={"is boulderslide ravine dangerous","dangers in boulderslide ravine","boulderslide threats"},it="danger",add="2463d3df"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can look for veins exposed along the ravine's steep walls as the mountain's stone shifts.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you may recognize the faded tribal designs in the small side cave. They hint at ancestral paths through the Stonetalon heights."},kw={"boulderslide cavern","boulderslide ravine","cliff stormer","rams","stonetalon","webwinder path"},rel={"subzone:boulderslide-cavern","subzone:webwinder-path","quest:6421","zone:stonetalon","topic:tauren"},src={"Boulderslide Ravine"}}
E["subzone:camp-aparaje"] = {t="subzone",n="Camp Aparaje",z="stonetalon",s="Grimtotem warriors hold Camp Aparaje in the eastern heights of the Stonetalon Mountains. The tribe slaughtered the peaceful tauren who settled there and claimed the outpost.",h="Grimtotem warriors hold Camp Aparaje in the eastern heights of the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Tragic Downfall",b="Camp Aparaje lies among the Stonetalon crags, where peaceful tauren once sought a quiet life in the highlands. Raiders from nearby Grimtotem Post struck under Grundig Darkcloud's lead. The attackers butchered villagers or drove them away. Survivors such as Makaba Flathoof mourn the loss of their home and fear for kin taken captive.",sp=0},{t="Under Grimtotem Sway",b="Grimtotem warriors now occupy Camp Aparaje as a forward base for their aggressive tribe in the region. Many Grimtotem settlements bear blue markings, but the great totem here is carved with deep crimson paint.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who used to live at Camp Aparaje?",a="Peaceful tauren affiliated with the Horde and Bloodhoof tribe lived at Camp Aparaje, including Makaba Flathoof and his daughter Kaya, before the settlement was invaded.",al={"who lived here","camp aparaje original villagers","makaba flathoof village"},it="people"},{q="Why is the camp hostile to Horde players?",a="The Grimtotem seized the village by force. The xenophobic, treacherous tauren clan rejects Cairne Bloodhoof's authority and attacks outsiders, including members of the Horde.",al={"why are tauren attacking me","who controls camp aparaje","why is camp aparaje red"},it="hostile"},{q="Who led the assault on Camp Aparaje?",a="Grundig Darkcloud led the assault from Grimtotem Post. The brutal Grimtotem chieftain seeks to extend his tribe's violent hold over Stonetalon.",al={"who attacked aparaje","grundig darkcloud","who is the leader here"},it="threat"},{q="What happened to the surviving villagers?",a="Most villagers died in the raid. A few escaped, while others, including young Kaya Flathoof, were captured and held at nearby Grimtotem Post.",al={"kaya flathoof","where are the survivors","are there survivors"}},{q="What is Camp Aparaje?",a="Camp Aparaje was once a peaceful tauren settlement tucked into the eastern heights of the Stonetalon Mountains. It served as a home for quiet families like Makaba Flathoof and his daughter, but that tranquil existence was shattered when violent Grimtotem raiders swept down from their stronghold to seize the village by force.",al={"camp aparaje overview","what is this camp","tell me about camp aparaje"},it="place",add="fcad7814"},{q="What happened at Camp Aparaje?",a="Hostile Grimtotem warriors launched a sudden, brutal assault on the village from nearby Grimtotem Post. Led by Grundig Darkcloud, the attackers drove out or slaughtered the resident tauren, capturing those who could not escape in time and claiming the outpost entirely for their own treacherous tribe.",al={"what happened here","camp aparaje history","how was camp aparaje destroyed"},it="history",add="358940fc"},{q="Who controls Camp Aparaje now?",a="The camp is currently held by occupying Grimtotem raiders under the command of Grundig Darkcloud. Having displaced the original inhabitants, these hostile tauren now use the village as an active encampment, maintaining sentries and keeping prisoners under guard.",al={"who lives in camp aparaje","who holds camp aparaje","who is in camp aparaje"},it="residents",add="8b937e47"},{q="Why was Camp Aparaje abandoned by its original people?",a="The peaceful villagers had no chance against the surprise assault mounted by the Grimtotem. Those who survived the initial massacre, such as Makaba Flathoof, were forced to flee for their lives into the surrounding wilderness, leaving their homes and belongings behind to be ransacked by their conquerors.",al={"why is camp aparaje ruined","why was the village lost","why did the villagers leave"},it="ruin",add="33da0239"},{q="Is Camp Aparaje dangerous?",a="Yes. The settlement is heavily occupied by aggressive Grimtotem warriors who will attack anyone approaching the camp on sight, regardless of your standing with the rest of the Horde. Wandering into its borders invites immediate combat with Grundig Darkcloud's hardened raiders.",al={"is camp aparaje safe","danger at camp aparaje","camp aparaje threats"},it="danger",add="46090024"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see Camp Aparaje's ruins as a reminder of the cruelty of Magatha's Grimtotem tribe. Not all children of the Earth Mother share Cairne Bloodhoof's vision of honor and peace.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you have reason to drive the Grimtotem from Camp Aparaje in vengeance and defense. The tribe butchered innocent Horde subjects in Stonetalon."},kw={"camp aparaje","grimtotem","grimtotem post","grundig darkcloud","kaya flathoof","makaba flathoof","stonetalon"},rel={"quest:6548","quest:6629","quest:6523","npc:makaba-flathoof","topic:grimtotem-tribe","zone:stonetalon","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Camp Aparaje"}}
E["subzone:charred-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Charred Vale",z="stonetalon",s="In southwestern Stonetalon, flames and smoke consume the Charred Vale. The Venture Company's logging left a once thriving woodland in ruins, where fire elementals roam and Bloodfury harpies guard their territory.",h="In southwestern Stonetalon, flames and smoke consume the Charred Vale.",sec={{t="A Scorched Woodland",b="The Charred Vale was once a thriving woodland in a basin of southwestern Stonetalon. Majestic treants guarded it, while native chimaeras and harpies made their home among the trees. The Venture Company brought the ruin. Its goblins clear-cut the forest with explosive machinery, corrupting the treants and waking chaotic fire elementals. The treants eventually drove the goblins back, but the loggers left the land broken and scarred by fire. Whatever foul devices they used as they retreated also tainted the valley.",sp=0},{t="Struggles of Renewal",b="Blackened ancients wander blindly through smoke and ash, among enraged elementals. Bloodfury harpies roost in skeletal snags and defend what remains of their territory. Druids from Sun Rock Retreat refuse to abandon the valley. They send travelers to sow enchanted seeds and tend the corrupted ancients as they work to reclaim the scorched earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Charred Vale on fire?",a="The Venture Company's ruthless logging set the Charred Vale ablaze. Its destructive machinery and aggressive deforestation enraged the land's primal spirits and unleashed fire elementals that spread through the valley.",al={"why is it burning","who burned charred vale","what happened to charred vale"},it="ruin"},{q="Can the forest in the Charred Vale ever recover?",a="Tauren druids from nearby Sun Rock Retreat believe the forest can recover. They ask travelers to soothe the maddened treants and plant enchanted earthen seeds in the ash, hoping green shoots will rise from the ruined soil.",al={"is charred vale healing","druids charred vale"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the Charred Vale?",a="Hostile fire elementals, blackened and vengeful ancients, Scorched Basilisks, and wild chimaeras inhabit the Charred Vale. Bloodfury harpies plague the basin as well.",al={"monsters in charred vale","what lives in charred vale"},it="residents"},{q="What was the Charred Vale called before it burned?",a="The Charred Vale's original name has been lost to time. Long before goblin axes arrived, it was renowned as a lush woodland sanctuary.",al={"charred vale old name","original name of charred vale"},it="name"},{q="What is the Charred Vale?",a="The Charred Vale is a vast, smoldering valley in southwestern Stonetalon Mountains. Once a lush, verdant woodland watched over by ancient treants, it has been reduced to ash, lava fissures, and blazing stumps following devastating industrial exploitation.",al={"what is charred vale","charred vale overview","about charred vale"},it="place",add="e38ca889"},{q="What happened at the Charred Vale?",a="The goblins of the Venture Company swept through the valley, clear-cutting the forest and burning the land. When the ancient tree-guardians rose up to defend the woods and drive the loggers out, the conflict enraged the local nature spirits, shattered the earth, and unleashed volatile fire elementals. As the goblins retreated, their toxic weaponry corrupted the surviving ancients into blackened, maddened husks.",al={"charred vale history","what happened in charred vale","how was charred vale destroyed"},it="history",add="97858e06"},{q="Is the Charred Vale dangerous?",a="It is one of the most hostile places in Stonetalon. Beyond the smoldering ground and choking smoke, you face fiery elementals, feral Bloodfury harpies, aggressive chimaeras, scorched basilisks, and maddened blackened ancients.",al={"is charred vale dangerous","charred vale threats","dangers of charred vale"},it="danger",add="543e0702"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see how uncontrolled greed shattered the natural balance here. The valley remains a focus of reclamation efforts.",["faction:Horde"]="From Sun Rock Retreat, Horde forces work with Cenarion allies to contain the elemental unrest and push back the Venture Company's lingering corruption."},kw={"blackened ancient","bloodfury","charred vale","chimaera","fire elemental","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","venture company"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","topic:venture-company","quest:1083","quest:1084","quest:6381","quest:1844","topic:druid"},src={"Charred Vale"}}
E["subzone:cragpool-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Cragpool Lake",z="stonetalon",s="At Cragpool Lake, the Venture Company’s timber structure looms over the dark water in Windshear Crag.",h="At Cragpool Lake, the Venture Company’s timber structure looms over the dark water in Windshear Crag.",sec={{t="Industrial Encroachment",b="Cragpool Lake lies beneath a vast timber structure built by the Venture Company in Windshear Crag. Platforms cross above the water, where Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle watches operations across the mountain valley. Venture Company workers occupy the platforms overhead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the massive wooden structure hanging over the lake?",a="The Venture Company built a vast wooden structure over the lake to manage its logging and mining in Windshear Crag. Platforms and heavy machinery span the water.",al={"venture co platform","cragpool scaffolding","cragpool bridge"},it="place"},{q="Who oversees the operations at Cragpool Lake?",a="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle oversees the operations at Cragpool Lake. The Venture Company operative watches deforestation and resource extraction across Windshear Crag from the high scaffolding.",al={"who leads venture co here","who is the boss here","gerenzo wrenchwhistle"},it="in_charge"},{q="What dangers surround Cragpool Lake?",a="Venture Company workers operate on the platforms above the lake. Their armed presence makes the site dangerous for intruders.",al={"what is in cragpool lake"},it="danger"},{q="Has the Venture Company abandoned Cragpool Lake?",a="No. Venture Company workers and Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle occupy the structure above the lake.",al={"is venture company gone","who lives at cragpool lake"},it="ruin"},{q="What is Cragpool Lake?",a="Cragpool Lake is a small body of water nestled within Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. It is dominated by a sprawling, elevated wooden superstructure built across its waters by the Venture Company to support their logging and excavation machinery in the valley.",al={"what is cragpool lake","cragpool lake lore","cragpool lake stonetalon"},it="place",add="588e76b4"},{q="What happened at Cragpool Lake?",a="The Venture Company built its enormous wooden structure above Cragpool Lake as part of its operations in Windshear Crag. Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle oversees the work from the platforms.",al={"cragpool lake history","what happened at cragpool lake","cragpool lake past"},it="history",add="686f269e"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The timber scaffolding and cantilevered machinery above Cragpool Lake show goblin industry built quickly, heavily loaded, and indifferent to the land beneath it.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the runoff, timber platforms, and disruption around Cragpool Lake as a scar on Stonetalon. They warp the local ecosystem and displace native wildlife."},kw={"cragpool lake","gerenzo wrenchwhistle","stonetalon","venture company","windshear crag"},rel={"subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","quest:1096","topic:venture-company"},src={"Cragpool Lake"}}
E["subzone:greatwood-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Greatwood Vale",z="stonetalon",s="The Grimtotem have seized Greatwood Vale in the eastern foothills of the Stonetalon Mountains. The perilous Webwinder Path leads into the forested valley, which the tribe now uses to launch bloody assaults on nearby settlements.",h="The Grimtotem have seized Greatwood Vale in the eastern foothills of the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Contested Valley",b="Greatwood Vale has become a violent frontier off the Webwinder Path. Grundig Darkcloud leads the Grimtotem who have moved into the vale in force. They block safe passage and terrorize the surrounding foothills.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge of Camp Aparaje",b="From Greatwood Vale, Grimtotem raiders swept into nearby Camp Aparaje and slaughtered nearly every tauren there. Makaba Flathoof escaped the attack. Now he directs vengeful Horde warriors into the heart of the vale to kill the renegade Grimtotem and end Grundig Darkcloud's rule.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Greatwood Vale right now?",a="Grundig Darkcloud leads the Grimtotem tribe occupying Greatwood Vale. Their warbands and spellcasters menace anyone traveling through the woods.",al={"who lives in greatwood vale","greatwood vale enemies","grimtotem in greatwood vale"},it="residents"},{q="What happened at Camp Aparaje?",a="Grimtotem raiders attacked Camp Aparaje from Greatwood Vale and massacred most of its peaceful tauren residents. Makaba Flathoof survived and seeks vengeance against the raiders and their leader.",al={"camp aparaje lore","what happened to aparaje","why did grimtotem attack"},it="history"},{q="Why is the Horde fighting the Grimtotem here?",a="The Grimtotem have not formally joined the Horde, despite Magatha's presence in Thunder Bluff. Grundig Darkcloud's followers attacked fellow tauren at Camp Aparaje, so survivors called on Horde warriors for aid.",al={"why kill grimtotem","makaba flathoof quest","avenge my village"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Greatwood Vale?",a="Greatwood Vale is a wooded valley in the Stonetalon foothills, reached through Webwinder Path. Malaka'jin lies to its south. Hostile Grimtotem tauren have made the vale a base for attacks on nearby settlements.",al={"greatwood vale","what is this place","stonetalon vale"},it="place",add="87537350"},{q="Is Greatwood Vale dangerous?",a="Yes, Greatwood Vale is exceptionally hostile. Aside from venomous webwood spiders infesting the approach along the Webwinder Path, the valley has fallen into the hands of renegade Grimtotem tauren. Led by warlord Grundig Darkcloud, these raiders actively hunt down any outsiders who venture into the woods.",al={"greatwood vale danger","is it safe here","threats in greatwood vale"},it="danger",add="3922b097"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For loyal children of Thunder Bluff, cleansing Greatwood Vale is a sorrowful, personal duty after the Grimtotem slaughtered fellow tauren at Camp Aparaje.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing Greatwood Vale helps protect Malaka'jin, the fragile southern outpost, from sudden flank attacks by rogue Grimtotem."},kw={"camp aparaje","greatwood vale","grimtotem","grundig darkcloud","makaba flathoof","malaka'jin","stonetalon","webwinder path"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","subzone:camp-aparaje","npc:makaba-flathoof","quest:6548","quest:6629","topic:grimtotem-tribe","subzone:malaka-jin","subzone:webwinder-path"},src={"Greatwood Vale"}}
E["subzone:malaka-jin"] = {t="subzone",n="Malaka'jin",z="stonetalon",s="Malaka'jin shelters Horde hunters in the lower Stonetalon hills, south of Grimtotem Post. Darkspear trolls make the camp a waystation for travelers climbing from the Barrens into the mountains.",h="Malaka'jin shelters Horde hunters in the lower Stonetalon hills, south of Grimtotem Post.",sec={{t="A Hunters' Refuge",b="Malaka'jin sits beside the main trail into the Stonetalon Mountains. Horde travelers find a small camp of troll hunters living off the crags and scrublands. The hunters trade supplies and fresh game with those passing through, while watching for mountain predators and Grimtotem tauren farther up the trails.",sp=0},{t="A Foothold in the Heights",b="Malaka'jin marks an early Horde foothold in Stonetalon, near the Barrens boundary. Sun Rock Retreat is a larger stronghold farther north, while this quiet camp gives Horde trackers a place to watch tribal unrest and guard the winding roads against threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Malaka'jin?",a="Malaka'jin is a small Horde village and outpost in the southern Stonetalon Mountains. Darkspear troll hunters live there and offer shelter, trade, and supplies to travelers climbing from the Barrens.",al={"where is malakajin","what is this place","malakajin stonetalon"},it="place"},{q="Who lives in Malaka'jin?",a="Darkspear troll hunters make their home in Malaka'jin. They hunt mountain game and trade meat and leather with passing adventurers.",al={"malakajin npcs","who is here","trolls in stonetalon"},it="residents"},{q="What threats face the camp?",a="Mountain predators threaten the camp, and hostile Grimtotem tauren live directly north at Grimtotem Post. The trolls stay alert to aggression from the tribe.",al={"malakajin enemies","who attacks malakajin"},it="danger"},{q="Is there a flight master here?",a="No. Malaka'jin has no flight master. Travelers through Stonetalon must use the flight master at Sun Rock Retreat, farther northwest, or follow the road on foot.",al={"malakajin flight path","fly to malakajin"},gp=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you can find fellow hunters at Malaka'jin, making a home in the rugged heights far from Kalimdor's tropical shores.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can use Malaka'jin as a waystation on the trail between the Barrens and the northern mountain strongholds."},kw={"darkspear","grimtotem","horde","hunters","malaka'jin","outpost","stonetalon","trolls"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","topic:horde","topic:troll","topic:grimtotem-tribe"},src={"Malaka'jin"}}
E["subzone:mirkfallon-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Mirkfallon Lake",z="stonetalon",s="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Mirkfallon Lake fills a basin beneath Windshear Crag. Native wildlife crowds its waters and banks, from aggressive slimes to thunder lizards and wyverns.",h="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Mirkfallon Lake fills a basin beneath Windshear Crag.",sec={{t="A Highland Basin",b="Mirkfallon Lake lies at the center of the Stonetalon range, between the passes to Webwinder Path in the south and Stonetalon Peak in the north. Runoff from the highlands feeds its waters, drawing thunder lizards down to drink and wyverns from their high roosts. Strange slimes bubble in the lake, making the crossing hazardous for travelers.",sp=0},{t="Crossroads of the Crag",b="Paths cross the lake basin in every direction. To the east, rocky tracks climb into Windshear Crag and the logging operations deep in its forested valleys. North of the lake, travelers climb toward night elven sanctums and tauren heights. Southward, the route skirts venomous spider hollows. Explorers and scouts crossing the contested mountains must reckon with the shifting dangers around the lake.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures live around Mirkfallon Lake?",a="Thunder lizards roam the banks, noxious ooze slimes inhabit the shallows, and mountain wyverns hunt around the basin and nest in the heights overhead.",al={"mirkfallon lake beasts","mirkfallon wildlife","what is at mirkfallon lake"},it="residents"},{q="Where does the lake lead?",a="Northward, the route climbs toward Stonetalon Peak. Southward, it descends through Webwinder Path, while rocky tracks to the east wind up into Windshear Crag.",al={"mirkfallon paths","where does mirkfallon go","mirkfallon lake directions"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Mirkfallon Lake safe to fish in?",a="Sagefish and floating salvage tempt anglers, but aggressive slimes and wyverns frequent the shoreline and make quiet fishing difficult.",al={"fishing mirkfallon lake","can i fish in mirkfallon"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="What is Mirkfallon Lake?",a="Mirkfallon Lake is a prominent body of water resting near the center of the Stonetalon Mountains. Nestled amid the crags and mountain trails connecting Stonetalon Peak to the surrounding peaks, the lake serves as a wild watering hole and basin in the heart of this rugged land.",al={"what is mirkfallon lake","mirkfallon lake overview","mirkfallon lake lore"},it="place",add="402ec74a"},{q="Is Mirkfallon Lake dangerous?",a="Yes, travelers should stay on guard. The lake and its shores are inhabited by aggressive wildlife, including wandering thunder lizards, foul slimes crawling along the shallows, and wild wyverns that nest in the surrounding heights and descend to hunt.",al={"is mirkfallon lake safe","dangers of mirkfallon lake","mirkfallon lake monsters"},it="danger",add="a8300c3c"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see wild beasts around Mirkfallon Lake in a delicate balance, uncomfortably close to the mechanical axes advancing in the crag above."},kw={"mirkfallon","mirkfallon lake","stonetalon lake","stonetalon thunder lizards","windshear lake"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:webwinder-path","subzone:stonetalon-peak"},src={"Mirkfallon Lake"}}
E["subzone:sishir-canyon"] = {t="subzone",n="Sishir Canyon",z="stonetalon",s="Sishir Canyon runs east through the Stonetalon Mountains, crowded with Deepmoss spiders. Webs choke the gorge on the dangerous approach to the Ruins of Eldre'thar, where travelers face venomous spiders and their matriarch.",h="Sishir Canyon runs east through the Stonetalon Mountains, crowded with Deepmoss spiders.",sec={{t="The Webbed Pass",b="Sishir Canyon cuts through the Stonetalon Mountains toward the ancient Ruins of Eldre'thar. Deepmoss spiders have overrun the gorge, covering its stone floor and walls with sheets of web and clusters of egg sacs. Travelers and sentinels heading for the night elven ruins must fight their way through swarms of aggressive webspinners.",sp=0},{t="Besseleth's Domain",b="Besseleth lurks in the deepest recess of Sishir Canyon as matriarch of the Deepmoss brood. Her great size and venom make her a danger to anyone trying to secure the pass. Local forces in Stonetalon keep watch and warn travelers that the webbed depths hold more than scattered spiders: Besseleth fiercely guards her brood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Sishir Canyon?",a="Sishir Canyon is a gorge in the Stonetalon Mountains that winds from the main mountain paths toward the ancient Ruins of Eldre'thar.",al={"where is sishir canyon","sishir canyon location"},it="place"},{q="What creatures live in the canyon?",a="Predatory Deepmoss spiders have claimed the canyon. They cover the ravine with webs and egg sacs and prey on creatures that enter their territory.",al={"monsters in sishir canyon","spiders in stonetalon canyon"},it="residents"},{q="Who is Besseleth?",a="Besseleth is the massive, deadly matriarch of the Deepmoss brood, dwelling deep within Sishir Canyon. She is a grave threat to travelers passing through.",al={"besseleth location","giant spider sishir canyon"}},{q="Where does Sishir Canyon lead?",a="Follow Sishir Canyon east to reach the Ruins of Eldre'thar, an ancient night elven site high in the mountains.",al={"what is at the end of sishir canyon","path through sishir canyon"}},{q="Is Sishir Canyon dangerous?",a="Sishir Canyon is extremely perilous for any traveler unprepared for arachnids. The ravine is entirely overrun by aggressive Deepmoss spiders that string thick webs across the rocky walls and guard clutches of eggs. Venturing too deeply puts you in path of their monstrous broodmother, Besseleth.",al={"sishir canyon danger","is sishir canyon safe","sishir canyon threats"},it="danger",add="8c6e4ccd"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you must fight through dense spider nests to reach the ancestral Ruins of Eldre'thar, since the overrun canyon blocks safe passage. Kaldorei sentinels and scholars face the same danger.",["class:Hunter"]="As a Hunter, you can test your skill tracking and trapping wild beasts in Sishir Canyon's tight ravine. Its webs and venomous Deepmoss spiders make the work dangerous."},kw={"besseleth","deepmoss","eldre'thar","sishir canyon","spiders","stonetalon","webbing"},rel={"zone:stonetalon"},src={"Sishir Canyon"}}
E["subzone:stonetalon-peak"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonetalon Peak",z="stonetalon",s="At Stonetalon Peak, kaldorei Sentinels and druids keep watch over an ancient sanctuary. The sheltered valley is sacred to the night elves and remains the Alliance’s main foothold in the high mountains.",h="At Stonetalon Peak, kaldorei Sentinels and druids keep watch over an ancient sanctuary.",sec={{t="A Sacred Mountain Vale",b="Stonetalon Peak opens into a green valley high above the dry lower ranges. Its ruins reach back millennia, to temples that honored Queen Azshara before the Great Sundering. Night elven Sentinels and druids now care for the sanctuary. They keep a barrow den and an Alliance flight roost here.",sp=0},{t="Crossroads of Destiny",b="During the Third War, Jaina Proudmoore’s human expedition and Thrall’s Horde climbed Stonetalon Peak, each seeking the Oracle in the mountain’s deep caverns. Medivh’s visions had guided them there. Their encounter brought mortal enemies together, and they set aside their blades. That uneasy pact helped them stand against the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal. Sentinel patrols still guard the peak, while Horde incursions in the lowlands keep its defenders alert.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Stonetalon Peak so green compared to the rest of the mountains?",a="A sheltered basin and ancient magic help keep Stonetalon Peak green. Night elves and druids from nearby Talon Den care for its forest, which contrasts with the charred, jagged cliffs below.",al={"why is stonetalon peak green","why forest in stonetalon peak","stonetalon peak weather"}},{q="What happened here during the Third War?",a="During the Third War, Jaina Proudmoore and Thrall came to Stonetalon Peak seeking the Oracle in the mountain caverns, guided by Medivh’s warnings. Their meeting led humans and orcs to make a truce against the Burning Legion.",al={"what happened at stonetalon peak warcraft 3","jaina and thrall stonetalon","the oracle stonetalon"},it="history"},{q="Who controls Stonetalon Peak right now?",a="The Alliance holds Stonetalon Peak, where night elf Sentinels and druids maintain the outpost. It offers Alliance travelers a haven, flight connections, and aid in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"is stonetalon peak alliance or horde","who lives at stonetalon peak","stonetalon peak faction"},it="residents"},{q="What ancient ruins are located here?",a="The vale’s crumbling pillars and marble buildings are remnants of the ancient night elven empire. They once formed temple grounds dedicated to Queen Azshara, before her descent into madness and the Great Sundering.",al={"stonetalon peak ruins","old temple stonetalon","azshara temple stonetalon peak"}},{q="What is Stonetalon Peak?",a="Stonetalon Peak is a verdant mountain valley and night elven settlement nestled at the far northwestern end of the Stonetalon Mountains. Sacred to local cultures and suffused with ancient magic, this lush sanctuary stands in stark contrast to the barren crags below. It serves as a vital northern bastion for the night elves and their Alliance allies in central Kalimdor.",al={"what is stonetalon peak","stonetalon peak overview","about stonetalon peak"},it="place",add="755df306"},{q="Is Stonetalon Peak dangerous?",a="While the grove itself is a fortified haven for the Alliance, the surrounding peaks harbor severe perils. Aggressive harpies roost in the crags, hostile Venture Company loggers despoil the nearby forests, and the Horde contests the mountain passes. Travelers climbing toward the peak must remain constantly vigilant against ambushes along the narrow trails.",al={"is stonetalon peak safe","threats in stonetalon peak","stonetalon peak dangers"},it="danger",add="d4bc90d5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can find shelter, flight paths, and aid at Stonetalon Peak, your fortified foothold in the western mountains.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can look to Stonetalon Peak and the sacred Talon Den as places tied to Cenarion history, pilgrimage, and the defense of the wild."},kw={"jaina","kaldorei","night elf","oracle","sentinels","stonetalon","stonetalon peak","talon den","thrall"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","topic:night-elf","topic:sentinels","topic:druid","topic:third-war","npc:thrall","npc:jaina-proudmoore","quest:1088"},src={"Stonetalon Peak"}}
E["subzone:sun-rock-retreat"] = {t="subzone",n="Sun Rock Retreat",z="stonetalon",s="Atop the central Stonetalon peaks, Sun Rock Retreat shelters the Horde south of Mirkfallon Lake. Tauren hold the mountain sacred, while orcs and tauren use the settlement as a base and supply post.",h="Atop the central Stonetalon peaks, Sun Rock Retreat shelters the Horde south of Mirkfallon Lake.",sec={{t="A Sacred Haven in the Peaks",b="Sun Rock Retreat lies in a mountain basin south of Mirkfallon Lake, on ground the tauren have long held sacred. Ancient tradition says An'she, the Sun, kissed the peak above the village. For generations before the Horde came, tauren shamans and pilgrims traveled here for rites that crossed the mortal veil. They drew strength from the land's close bond with the spirit world.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Outpost",b="Orcs and tauren now hold Sun Rock Retreat as the Horde's chief base across the Stonetalon Mountains. Together they seek a secure foothold against hostile harpy broods, local night elf sentinels, and the Venture Company's industrial pillaging. Trade and flight routes link the retreat with Thunder Bluff, the Crossroads, and the borders of Ashenvale. The outpost offers shelter, provisions, and spiritual guidance to those who brave the crags.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Sun Rock Retreat is the Horde's main outpost in the Stonetalon Mountains. Mostly tauren and orcs live there, and it is a sanctuary, trading station, and command post for Horde champions in the region.",al={"what is sun rock","sun rock retreat info","who runs sun rock retreat"},it="place"},{q="Why is this place sacred to the tauren?",a="Tauren legend says An'she, the Sun, touched the mountain where Sun Rock Retreat now stands. Its enduring bond with the spirit world has made the land a pilgrimage site for visions and communion with ancestors.",al={"why is sun rock sacred","anshe stonetalon","tauren sun rock lore"},it="origin"},{q="What threats does the retreat face?",a="The retreat faces aggressive harpies, hostile night elves guarding the sacred woods, and the Venture Company's destructive mining and logging, which ravage the land.",al={"sun rock threats","who is attacking sun rock","stonetalon enemies"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the local flight master connect?",a="Wind riders from Sun Rock Retreat connect travelers with major central Kalimdor destinations, including the Crossroads in the Barrens and Thunder Bluff, the tauren capital.",al={"sun rock flight paths","flying to sun rock retreat","sun rock flight master"},gp=true},{q="What happened at Sun Rock Retreat in the past?",a="For generations, Sun Rock Retreat served as a sacred destination for tauren pilgrims. Because of the land's deep and enduring connection to the spirit realm, travelers came from across the plains to conduct solemn rituals that allowed them to cross over into the world of the spirits. In recent times, the Horde established a permanent presence here, turning the secluded haven into an active base dedicated to protecting the mountains from environmental devastation.",al={"sun rock retreat history","past of sun rock retreat","history of sun rock retreat"},it="history",add="ea57691e"},{q="Who lives in Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Sun Rock Retreat is populated by a dedicated contingent of Horde forces, predominantly tauren and orcs. Alongside the spiritual shamans and druids who honor the sanctified grounds, warriors and laborers work together to heal the scars carved into the Stonetalon peaks by reckless exploiters like the Venture Company.",al={"who lives in sun rock retreat","sun rock retreat residents","who runs sun rock retreat"},it="residents",add="399aba06"},{q="Is Sun Rock Retreat dangerous?",a="The retreat itself is a secure haven guarded by vigilant Horde defenders, offering safety to travelers and pilgrims. However, the wilderness surrounding it is perilous. Aggressive beasts, territorial harpies, and the destructive mercenaries of the Venture Company infest the nearby crags and ravines, meaning you should remain watchful the moment you leave the camp's borders.",al={"is sun rock retreat safe","how dangerous is sun rock retreat","sun rock retreat danger"},it="danger",add="7401fa7d"},{q="Why is it called Sun Rock Retreat?",a="The settlement draws its name from ancient tauren mythology. According to their legends, An'she—the sun in tauren belief—once leaned down and personally kissed the mountain peak where the village now rests, blessing the stone and infusing the area with divine warmth and spiritual power.",al={"why is it called sun rock","sun rock retreat name origin","meaning of sun rock retreat"},it="name",add="f56a5eae"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="To the shu'halo, Sun Rock Retreat is sacred ground blessed by An'she, where shamans have walked the spirit realm for centuries.",["faction:Horde"]="Sun Rock Retreat is the Horde's main staging hub in the Stonetalon Mountains, with supplies and flight routes among contested peaks."},kw={"an'she","mirkfallon lake","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","sunrock","tauren","venture company"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:crossroads","topic:tauren","topic:horde","topic:venture-company","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Sun Rock Retreat"}}
E["subzone:talondeep-path"] = {t="subzone",n="Talondeep Path",z="stonetalon",s="Talondeep Path cuts beneath the ridge between Ashenvale and the Stonetalon Mountains. The quiet tunnel links the woods west of Mystral Lake to Windshear Crag.",h="Talondeep Path cuts beneath the ridge between Ashenvale and the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Quiet Mountain Pass",b="Talondeep Path runs beneath the ridge between Ashenvale and the Stonetalon Mountains. The tunnel links the woods west of Mystral Lake to the northwestern reaches of Windshear Crag. Surface trails cross dangerous country, with predators and warring factions, but the passage is calm and has no hostile beasts or encampments. Twisting side pockets, crevices, and natural alcoves break up the rock. Above ground, faint traces of an old road remain along the peaks, where travelers once crossed before the sheltered route through the stone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Talondeep Path lead?",a="Talondeep Path connects southwestern Ashenvale to the northeastern Stonetalon Mountains. Its northern entrance lies just west of Mystral Lake, and its southern mouth opens into northwestern Windshear Crag.",al={"where does talondeep path go","talondeep path connections","talondeep tunnel exits"},it="purpose"},{q="Are there monsters or enemies inside the tunnel?",a="No hostile creatures live inside Talondeep Path. The cavern is peaceful and has no hostile beasts or friendly folk, leaving travelers a safe passage through the mountain divide.",al={"is talondeep path safe","talondeep path mobs","talondeep path threats"},it="danger"},{q="What are the ruins above the cavern?",a="The ruins above Talondeep Path are remnants of an overgrown road along the mountain ridge. They suggest travelers once crossed the crags by a treacherous surface route before the tunnel passage.",al={"road above talondeep path","overland path stonetalon"}},{q="Is Talondeep Path an Alliance or Horde tunnel?",a="Neither faction holds Talondeep Path. The unfortified tunnel is neutral wilderness, open to travelers of any allegiance moving between the contested forest and the mountains.",al={"who controls talondeep path","talondeep path faction"},it="side"},{q="What is Talondeep Path?",a="Talondeep Path is a winding underground tunnel carved straight through the peaks, providing a crucial shortcut between the lush forests of Ashenvale and the rugged heights of the Stonetalon Mountains. Entering from the west of Mystral Lake in Ashenvale, travelers emerge near the northwestern reaches of Windshear Crag in Stonetalon. Inside, the cavern branches into curious nooks and dead ends, yet remains one of the quietest mountain crossings in Kalimdor.",al={"what is talondeep path","talondeep path tunnel","about talondeep path"},it="place",add="3cd0cb65"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The winding rock alcoves cut through the mountain range's deep stone foundation. They make Talondeep Path a natural landmark when traveling between mineral-rich Ashenvale and Stonetalon."},kw={"ashenvale","cave","mystral lake","stonetalon","talondeep","talondeep path","tunnel","windshear crag"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","zone:ashenvale","subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:mystral-lake"},src={"Talondeep Path"}}
E["subzone:webwinder-path"] = {t="subzone",n="Webwinder Path",z="stonetalon",s="Webwinder Path winds through the lower Stonetalon Mountains, linking Malaka'jin with Mirkfallon Lake. Spiders and native beasts roam its crags and woods.",h="Webwinder Path winds through the lower Stonetalon Mountains, linking Malaka'jin with Mirkfallon Lake.",sec={{t="A Treacherous Thoroughfare",b="Webwinder Path runs from Malaka'jin toward Mirkfallon Lake through the lower Stonetalon Mountains. Thick webs hang among the trees and along the jagged cliffs. Mountain spiders prowl the road, while thunder lizards and territorial rams roam nearby. Travelers must watch their step along the winding route.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Webwinder Path lead?",a="Webwinder Path runs north from Malaka'jin, the Darkspear troll outpost, toward Mirkfallon Lake.",al={"webwinder path location","where is webwinder path","what does webwinder path connect"},it="place"},{q="Why is it called Webwinder Path?",a="Webwinder Path takes its name from the many arachnids in the region. Spiders spin webs high in the trees and along rocky ledges beside the road.",al={"why webwinder","why is it called webwinder"},it="name"},{q="What creatures wander the path?",a="Venomous spiders weave webs above the road, while thunder lizards, highland rams, and other mountain creatures roam nearby.",al={"what lives here","webwinder path beasts","mobs on webwinder path"},it="threat"},{q="Is Webwinder Path safe to travel?",a="Webwinder Path is dangerous, with fierce, territorial predators along the way. It also passes Malaka'jin, a Horde camp, putting Alliance travelers coming from the Barrens at risk.",al={"is webwinder path dangerous","can alliance travel webwinder path"},it="danger"},{q="What is Webwinder Path?",a="Webwinder Path is a winding mountainous road in Stonetalon Mountains, cutting a critical route from the troll outpost of Malaka'jin toward Mirkfallon Lake. Running through craggy peaks and web-draped canopies, it serves as a vital thoroughfare for travelers journeying deeper into the range, bordered by rugged wilderness and aggressive native beasts.",al={"what is webwinder path","webwinder path lore","webwinder path stonetalon"},it="place",add="4490b183"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can use this overland route beside Malaka'jin to reach the deeper valleys of Stonetalon.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can scout the path for thunder lizards, mountain rams, and venomous spiders to tame."},kw={"malaka'jin","mirkfallon lake","road","spiders","stonetalon","webwinder","webwinder path"},rel={"subzone:malaka-jin","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","zone:stonetalon","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Webwinder Path"}}
E["subzone:windshear-crag"] = {t="subzone",n="Windshear Crag",z="stonetalon",s="In central Stonetalon, Windshear Crag lies scarred by the Venture Company's logging. The old forest is gone, replaced by machinery, muddy runoff, and logging crews. Kobolds dig for ore nearby, while a mountain passage leads beneath the ridges to Ashenvale.",h="In central Stonetalon, Windshear Crag lies scarred by the Venture Company's logging.",sec={{t="Industrial Devastation",b="Windshear Crag's old forest is gone, cut down by the Venture Company for profit. Stumps and machinery now fill the basin. Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a leper gnome, oversees the logging from a platform above Cragpool Lake. His engineering gave the company the Super Reaper 6000, which fells great trees in moments. The operation strips the mountain bare, stirring anger among rival engineers and local inhabitants alike.",sp=0},{t="Mines and Mountain Passes",b="Windshear Crag's timberyards are not its only danger or crossroads. In the southeast, kobolds dig through Windshear Mine for Smoky Iron Ingots and attack those who approach their haul. The Talondeep Path runs beneath the ridges from the crag's northeast reaches into Ashenvale. Near its entrance, the tauren elder Braug Dimspirit tests the historical wisdom and resolve of Horde travelers crossing the contested peaks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is running the logging operation here?",a="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle directs the logging operation at Windshear Crag. The brilliant leper gnome engineer works under contract with the Venture Company and watches over the crag from a timber platform above Cragpool Lake.",al={"who leads venture co here","who is the boss of windshear","gerenzo wrenchwhistle lore"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Super Reaper 6000?",a="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle built the Super Reaper 6000, a mechanical logging prototype. It clears timber at great speed, grinding ancient mountain trees into sawdust within moments and hastening the company's clear-cutting.",al={"super reaper 6000","what is the big shredder","venture co reaper"},it="item"},{q="Why is the Undermine Tinkers' Union targeting Gerenzo?",a="Director Riddlevox of Undermine's Tinkers' Union wants Gerenzo dead. Ziz Fizziks, a goblin who helped steal the Super Reaper 6000 blueprints, carries out the order. Undermine's trade princes disapprove of the Venture Company consorting with the gnome.",al={"why kill gerenzo","ziz fizziks motives","tinkers union vendetta"},sp=1,it="conflict",bt={"q1483.3"}},{q="Where does the cave in the northeast lead?",a="The cave in the northeast is the Talondeep Path. It runs beneath the mountain roots, connecting Windshear Crag and Ashenvale by foot.",al={"talondeep path destination","windshear cave exit","tunnel in windshear crag"},it="place"},{q="Who are the kobolds digging in the southeast?",a="Windshear kobolds have overrun the mine in the crag's southeast. They defend their claim as they dig for Smoky Iron Ingots, which regional smiths use.",al={"windshear mine kobolds","why are kobolds here","smoky iron ingots"},it="residents"},{q="What is Windshear Crag?",a="Windshear Crag is a deep valley in the Stonetalon Mountains, once famed for its towering, ancient forest. Today, relentless clear-cutting has turned the green woodlands into a scarred landscape of jagged tree stumps, churning mud, and noxious run-off.",al={"what is this place","windshear crag lore","windshear crag stonetalon"},it="place",add="c9b71aef"},{q="What happened to Windshear Crag?",a="In the years following the Third War, the Venture Company moved into the valley with heavy industrial machinery. Led by the leper gnome Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, their destructive logging operations and massive shredders have virtually wiped out the old-growth timber, polluting the local waters and stripping the crag bare for timber and profit.",al={"history of windshear crag","why is windshear crag deforested","what happened here"},it="history",add="f4630a37"},{q="Is Windshear Crag dangerous?",a="Very dangerous. The Venture Company employs aggressive loggers, mechanics, and merciless shredders that attack anyone intruding on their claim. To the southeast, hostile kobolds defend the Windshear Mine, making the entire basin hostile to wandering travelers.",al={"is windshear crag safe","threats in windshear crag","windshear crag dangers"},it="danger",add="bab211f4"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The machinery across Windshear Crag reveals goblin trade secrets and Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle's lethal Super Reaper designs.",["faction:Horde"]="On the way to Ashenvale, Horde travelers meet Braug Dimspirit near the Talondeep Path. He tests their knowledge of Kalimdor's history."},kw={"braug dimspirit","cragpool lake","gerenzo wrenchwhistle","super reaper 6000","talondeep path","venture company","windshear crag","windshear mine","ziz fizziks"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","topic:venture-company","subzone:cragpool-lake","subzone:talondeep-path","quest:1096","quest:1483","quest:1152"},src={"Windshear Crag"}}
E["zone:stonetalon"] = {t="zone",n="Stonetalon Mountains",z="stonetalon",s="In Stonetalon Mountains, sacred heights now face smoke, deforestation, and elemental ruin. Night elves and tauren revere the range, while border hostilities simmer below.",h="In Stonetalon Mountains, sacred heights now face smoke, deforestation, and elemental ruin.",sec={{t="The Ill Winds and the Peaks",b="Stonetalon Mountains rise from central Kalimdor beneath the Ill Winds. Moisture from the western seas brings sudden downpours and slick sandstone trails, while fierce gusts scour the lower valleys, blinding travelers with grit and hurling the careless from cliffs. Higher ridges carry evergreen forests around Stonetalon Peak. Night elves tend ancestral barrows and glades there, and watch sacred wyvern and hippogryph roosts along Mirkfallon Lake.",sp=0},{t="Industry and Intrusion",b="The Venture Company has broken the range's quiet with logging camps and strip mines in Windshear Crag. The goblins, aided by the deranged leper gnome Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, have felled old-growth timber, filled the skies with furnace smoke, and fouled mountain runoff with industrial sludge. Local shamans from Orgrimmar answered the mountain spirits' cries. Small Alliance camps nearby also resist the defilers and try to protect the highlands that remain.",sp=0},{t="Scars of the Past",b="South lies the Charred Vale, once a blossoming wilderness and now an ash-covered wasteland filled with rogue fire elementals, black dragonspawn, and harpies. During the Third War, the Horde and Alliance forged an uneasy truce in these peaks under the mysterious Oracle's guidance. Relations have since frayed. Renegade Grimtotem tauren hold seized encampments, while Darkspear trolls in Malaka'jin clash with Alliance forces pressing out from the Barrens and Ashenvale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I get to the Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Most travelers reach Stonetalon Mountains through Talondeep Pass, a mountain trail from southwestern Ashenvale. High trails lead south into Desolace, and routes descend east into the northern Barrens.",al={"stonetalon entrance","how to get to stonetalon","stonetalon road"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Why is the Charred Vale burned and ruined?",a="The Charred Vale was once a lush haven, but cataclysmic devastation consumed it in flames. Now the valley is an ash-covered ruin crawling with aggressive fire elementals, rogue drakes, and deadly harpies.",al={"charred vale fire","what happened to charred vale","why charred vale burnt"},it="ruin"},{q="What is the Venture Company doing in Windshear Crag?",a="The Venture Company cuts timber and mines deep into Windshear Crag for mineral wealth. Its operations have fouled Cragpool Lake with engine grease, stripped the valleys bare, and enraged local spirits and native inhabitants.",al={"venture co stonetalon","windshear crag goblins","why are goblins cutting trees"},it="threat"},{q="Where are the main flight masters located?",a="Alliance heroes use the flight master at Stonetalon Peak's high sanctuary in the north. Horde adventurers rely on the central mountain village of Sun Rock Retreat.",al={"stonetalon flight path","where is flight point stonetalon","stonetalon fp"},gp=true},{q="What happened at Stonetalon Peak during the Third War?",a="During the Third War, Thrall and Jaina Proudmoore followed visions of the Prophet Medivh through Stonetalon Peak's caverns in search of the Oracle. There they forged a temporary alliance against the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal.",al={"stonetalon peak lore","the oracle stonetalon","third war stonetalon"},it="history"},{q="Who are the Grimtotem in Stonetalon?",a="The Grimtotem are a renegade tauren tribe hostile to outsider influence. In Stonetalon, they occupy a mountain post near the Barrens border, terrorize travelers, and take prisoners.",al={"grimtotem post","grimtotem stonetalon"},it="threat"},{q="What is Stonetalon Mountains?",a="The Stonetalon Mountains are a rugged, wind-carved range in central Kalimdor, situated west of the Barrens, south of Ashenvale, and north of Desolace. Known for extreme winds, deep chasms, and sheer sandstone peaks created during the Great Sundering, the region forms a historical borderland where night elves and tauren have coexisted for generations. Its high, sacred summits remain lush with evergreens, while lower valleys are dry, rocky, and heavily scarred by industry.",al={"stonetalon mountains zone","what is stonetalon","about stonetalon mountains"},it="place",add="4946a833",nx={9}},{q="Is Stonetalon Mountains dangerous?",a="Yes, travelers face both natural perils and fierce hostiles. Violent gales and sudden rain can make the high sandstone cliffs slick enough to send people tumbling to their deaths. Beyond the weather, the mountains crawl with aggressive Bloodfury harpies, predatory wyverns, spiders, kobolds, and enraged elementals. Furthermore, the ruthless machinery and armed enforcers of the Venture Company make contested valleys like Windshear Crag exceptionally perilous.",al={"stonetalon danger","is stonetalon safe","hazards of stonetalon"},it="danger",add="4e995438"},{q="Who lives in Stonetalon Mountains?",a="The region is home to scattered factions rather than a single governing power. The night elves hold Stonetalon Peak and guard sacred sites across the heights, while the Horde maintains settlements at Sun Rock Retreat and the troll village of Malaka'jin. Native Bloodfury harpies roost in the crags, hostile Grimtotem tauren occupy nearby posts, and the goblin-run Venture Company occupies deforested tracts around Windshear Crag.",al={"who lives in stonetalon","stonetalon factions","inhabitants of stonetalon"},it="residents",add="9d849e11"},{q="Why is the Venture Company logging in Windshear Crag?",a="The Venture Company is a ruthless merchant conglomerate seeking profit through unconstrained resource stripping. In Windshear Crag, they clear-cut ancient forests using heavy machinery like the Super Reaper 6000 and blast the earth for precious ore. Their disregard for nature fills the air with soot and poisons local waters with sludge and oil, earning the furious opposition of both local druids and the Horde.",al={"venture company logging","why are goblins cutting trees","venture co lumber stonetalon"},it="threat",add="a4f73e64",nx={11}},{q="Who runs the Venture Company in Windshear Crag?",a="The local logging and mining operations in Windshear Crag are directed by a leper gnome named Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle. Overseeing the clear-cutting from a platform built high above Cragpool Lake, Gerenzo employs his mechanical expertise to maximize destruction. His rogue operations have even drawn the ire of rival goblin inventors from the Tinkers' Union, who seek to eliminate him.",al={"who runs windshear crag","gerenzo wrenchwhistle","venture company leader stonetalon"},it="leader",add="66935983"},{q="Who are the Bloodfury harpies?",a="The Bloodfury harpies are a vicious tribe of bird-women native to the Stonetalon Mountains. Historically, these mountains were their ancestral heartland before they spread into the Barrens and beyond. They aggressively defend their territory from outsiders, capturing local beasts and clashing violently with both tauren pilgrims and encroaching goblin machines in places like the Charred Vale.",al={"bloodfury harpies","stonetalon harpies","who are the harpies here"},it="threat",add="ff0da62d"},{q="What is Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Sun Rock Retreat is a peaceful Horde settlement nestled in a secluded mountain valley south of Mirkfallon Lake. It serves as the primary base for tauren and orcs in the region, housing shamans and druids dedicated to restoring the land from Venture Company pollution and combating the threats encroaching upon the sacred mountains.",al={"sun rock retreat lore","what is sunrock retreat","sun rock tauren"},it="place",add="66599fe7",nx={14}},{q="Why did the tauren settle Sun Rock Retreat?",a="For generations, the tauren have revered this valley as a place with a profound connection to the spirit realm. Ancient legends say the sun god An'she kissed the peak upon which the retreat stands. Tauren long made sacred pilgrimages here to commune with spirits and light great ritual bonfires to illuminate the shadowed mountains.",al={"why tauren settle sun rock","history of sun rock retreat","an'she sun rock"},it="history",add="5a5a6e9c"},{q="What is Windshear Crag?",a="Windshear Crag was once a verdant old-growth forest, but it has been devastated by industrial exploitation. The Venture Company clear-cut the valley into a barren sprawl of stumps, dirt, and smoking machinery. Between the Venture Company's deforestation, foul runoff in Cragpool Lake, and kobolds infesting the local mine, it stands as a ruined monument to unchecked greed.",al={"about windshear crag","windshear crag zone","windshear crag lore"},it="place",add="51d42c77",nx={16}},{q="What is in Windshear Mine?",a="Windshear Mine, located in the southeastern cliffs of Windshear Crag, is overrun by aggressive Windshear kobolds. Driven out or abandoned by regular miners, the kobolds now furiously excavate veins of Smoky Iron Ingots, fiercely attacking anyone who attempts to intrude on their subterranean diggings.",al={"windshear mine kobolds","what is in windshear mine","windshear mine smoky iron"},it="threat",add="d850bc0a"},{q="What is the Talon Den on Stonetalon Peak?",a="The Talon Den is an ancient night elven barrow den carved into the heights of Stonetalon Peak. It is maintained by Cenarion druids who commune with the spirits of nature and the Emerald Dream. Deep within, druids have traditionally slept in sacred contemplation, guarded by dryads, keepers, and the peak's magical protections.",al={"talon den","the den stonetalon peak","barrow den stonetalon"},it="place",add="d3863c46"},{q="Does Ashenvale connect to Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Yes. The rugged Talondeep Path directly connects southwestern Ashenvale to northeastern Stonetalon Mountains through a cavernous mountain passage. Travelers and adventurers frequently pass between the pristine, contested forests of Ashenvale and the barren heights of Stonetalon while tracking threats from the Venture Company or the ongoing faction conflicts.",al={"how does ashenvale connect to stonetalon","talondeep path ashenvale","ashenvale border stonetalon"},it="ties",add="a547ffd6"},{q="How did I end up in Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Most travelers reach these jagged heights through the Talondeep Path, an ancient mountain tunnel carved into southwestern Ashenvale. Other wanderers climb up along the rugged trails leading west out of the Barrens, ascending the windswept passes into the rocky crags. Whether sent south by night elven commanders in Astranaar or dispatched west across the scorched border from the Crossroads, the high canyons and howling Ill Winds greet anyone making the arduous trek into the range.",al={"how did i get here","how do i get to stonetalon","arrival in stonetalon"},it="arrival",add="a5c2784c"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Stonetalon Mountains?",a="You are here to confront the mounting threats despoiling these sacred heights. At Windshear Crag, the ruthless goblins of the Venture Company tear down ancient forests and pollute the rivers with machinery, drawing the wrath of both factions. Meanwhile, the Grimtotem tribe causes strife along the eastern border, while vicious harpies and raging fire elementals infest the scorched basin of the Charred Vale. You must assist your allies in driving back these polluters and monsters to safeguard the land.",al={"what should i do here","why am i here","what is my mission in stonetalon"},it="purpose",add="4abc7ef6"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers rely on Sun Rock Retreat and Malaka'jin, the southern troll post, to curb Venture Company pollution and root out Grimtotem outlaws.",["faction:Alliance"]="From Stonetalon Peak and hidden camps around Windshear Crag, the Alliance defends ancient kaldorei barrows against goblin machines and territorial rivals.",["class:Druid"]="Windshear Crag's desecration and the Charred Vale's scorched corruption call druids to soothe enraged nature spirits and protect sacred roosts.",["class:Shaman"]="Goblin drills assault the mountain spirits, whose cries reach Orgrimmar. Shamans answer the call to quell rampaging rock elementals and restore balance to the peaks."},kw={"charred vale","gerenzo wrenchwhistle","malaka'jin","stonetalon","stonetalon peak","sun rock retreat","talondeep pass","windshear"},rel={"subzone:stonetalon-peak","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:malaka-jin","zone:ashenvale","zone:barrens","zone:desolace"},m={levels="15-27"},src={"Stonetalon Mountains (Classic)","Stonetalon Mountains"}}
